    "language": "en",
    "md5": "f5d88245589e1cb3b3e5a5f3e1723103",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1499,
    "chunk_text": "India beat Sri Lanka by 72 runs to win record Eighth Women\u2019s Asia Cup Title\n\nSEP.14 (Mirror Sports) - India produced a dominant performance to beat Sri Lanka by 72 runs in the Women\u2019s Asia Cup 2026 final in Dubai, securing a record eighth title.\n\nBatting first after being asked to set a target, India posted 183 for 5 at the Dubai International Cricket Stadium, with Shafali Verma and Smriti Mandhana leading the way.\n\nVerma smashed 68 runs, while Mandhana added 59 as the Indian openers put their side in control early in the innings.\n\nHarmanpreet Kaur contributed 14, Richa Ghosh scored 17, and Kamalini Gunalan remained unbeaten on 15 as India finished on 183.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s wickets were shared by Mithali Ayodhya, Chamari Athapaththu and Chamudi Praboda, who claimed one wicket each.\n\nChasing 184 for victory, Sri Lanka struggled against India\u2019s bowling attack and were restricted to 111.\n\nChamari Athapaththu top-scored with 36, while Vishmi Gunaratne made 20 and Nilakshika Silva added 22. Imesha Dulani, Harshitha Samarawickrama, Kavisha Dilhari, Hasini Perera and Kaushini Nuthyangana failed to make significant contributions as Sri Lanka\u2019s chase lost momentum.\n\nShree Charani was the star with the ball for India, taking four wickets, while Deepti Sharma claimed three. Kranti Gaud, Shafali Verma and Prema Rawat took one wicket each.\n\nIndia\u2019s 72-run victory sealed their record eighth Women\u2019s Asia Cup title, adding another major chapter to their dominance in the tournament."
  },
