    "chunk_size_bytes": 2013,
    "chunk_text": "China\u2019s Xi and India\u2019s Modi in landmark meeting at BRICS Summit\n\nChinese President Xi Jinping (left) with Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi\n\nChinese President Xi Jinping makes four observations on promoting steady and sustained development of China-India relations\n\nIndian Prime Minister Narendra Modi says India always views relations with China from strategic and long-term perspective; hopes to be a partner, not rival, of China\n\nChinese President Xi Jinping on Saturday met with Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi while attending the 18th BRICS Summit in New Delhi, India.\n\nThe two leaders had a sincere and in-depth exchange of views and reached the important consensus that China and India should be partners.\n\nPresident Xi pointed out that China always approaches and develops its relations with India from a strategic and long-term perspective.\n\nHe said: \u201cOver the past two years, I have met with Prime Minister Modi twice, guiding the bilateral relations from starting afresh to making further improvements. The institutional exchanges between the two countries have gradually resumed, the cooperation list has continued to lengthen, and the bilateral trade volume has hit a new high. This situation has not come easily and needs to be cherished. China and India have different national realities. We should draw on each other\u2019s strengths, support each other, help each other succeed, and develop together. In the face of the changing and turbulent international landscape, the world\u2019s two most populous countries and important members of the Global South shoulder important responsibilities. Both sides should keep in mind the future of humanity and the well-being of the people, and work together to promote the high-quality development of greater BRICS cooperation, so as to contribute more positive energy to promoting world peace, stability, development, and prosperity.\u201d\n\nPresident Xi made four observations on promoting the steady and sustained development of China-India relations."
  },
