    "num": "dailymirrorlk-367f5409",
    "date_str": "2026-09-14",
    "description": "Salesforce pivots from AI hype to real biz value in SL\u2019s digital push",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-news/Salesforce-pivots-from-AI-hype-to-real-biz-value-in-SLs-digital-push/273-350231",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1789366753.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-14-dailymirrorlk-367f5409-0002",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "89eeca47893c79eda48a8c3648e1ab9d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1714,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cYou are able to unlock the power of data and technology when the data speaks to itself.\u201d\n\nUnlocking this connectivity is critical to fostering customer loyalty, an imperative Chowhan illustrated using the local retail landscape.\n\n\u201cYou could be Nishel Fernando, you could be N. Fernando or you could be Nishel F. You could have different identities across channels but the ability for the data to be connected allows the brand to understand that you are the same consumer,\u201d Chowhan explained.\n\n\u201cTherefore, your buying patterns, your loyalty requirements and what you need as a consumer are understood at a connected level. If the brand knows who you are, their ability to serve you becomes vastly superior.\u201d\n\n\u201cIf you are unhappy with something and I am marketing another product to you from the same brand at the exact same time, you are not going to be happy,\u201d she pointed out.\n\n\u201cVery simply put, the data has to connect so that there is one single version of truth about the story of the customer and the reality of what is happening today. That is the foundational power of connected data.\u201d\n\nTo support the Sri Lankan enterprises in executing this technological shift, Chowhan said Salesforce has deployed a localised four-pillar strategic framework spanning workforce skilling, start-up incubation, developer community engagement and customer success.\n\nShe noted that the first three pillars are aimed at widening the base of local AI talent, with the company\u2019s dedicated start-up incubation initiative introduced to the market in January 2026, alongside grassroots activity anchored by the Trailblazer community and Yal Dreamin conference scheduled to take place in Jaffna this November."
  },
