    "language": "en",
    "md5": "bf82d281072174a2352fe7c6b26a4558",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1962,
    "chunk_text": "She noted that the first three pillars are aimed at widening the base of local AI talent, with the company\u2019s dedicated start-up incubation initiative introduced to the market in January 2026, alongside grassroots activity anchored by the Trailblazer community and Yal Dreamin conference scheduled to take place in Jaffna this November.\n\nWhen addressing the financial evaluation of enterprise software investments, Chowhan challenged the rigid, one-size-fits-all accounting models, urging executives to align technological expenditure directly with bespoke corporate outcomes.\n\n\u201cROI is like beauty; it is in the eye of the beholder,\u201d Chowhan remarked.\n\n\u201cThere is no single uniform source of truth for ROI; every company will measure it differently based on their operational priorities. What matters is the business outcomes you drive using the technology. Whether that is making decisions faster, achieving higher customer satisfaction scores, executing sharper marketing campaigns or reducing average service turnaround times, achieving better results for your customers is the true measure of ROI.\u201d\n\nTo make these capabilities viable for mid-sized and growing local businesses, Salesforce provides flexible commercial structures, spanning traditional user licences, consumption-based pricing and scalable enterprise packages.\n\nChowhan noted that the focus must remain on precision problem identification rather than sheer capital allocation, ensuring enterprises commit resources only where technological intervention creates measurable operational leverage.\n\nBeyond technical architecture and corporate productivity, Chowhan is an outspoken proponent of inclusive leadership, viewing business enterprise as an instrument for broader societal development. Her perspective is deeply shaped by her six-year tenure serving on the board of the Latika Roy Foundation, an organisation in Dehradun, India, dedicated to supporting severely disabled children."
