    "chunk_size_bytes": 1952,
    "chunk_text": "Shift Group celebrates 8 wins at The Dragons\n\nShift Group has marked another significant milestone in its creative journey, securing eight wins, including two Golds and a Bronze, at The Dragons of Sri Lanka 2026, one of the country\u2019s most recognised platforms for advertising excellence.\n\nLeading the accolades was \u2018Fill Her Glass\u2019, created for American Premium Water Systems for the World Water Day. The campaign secured Golds for Creative Excellence and Cause, Environment or Sustainability, while winning a Black Dragon for Small Budget.\n\nFor Commercial Credit & Finance Sri Lanka, Shift Group\u2019s \u2018Let Her Write Her Own Story\u2019 challenged another deeply rooted social narrative: the belief that women need a saviour. The campaign won Bronze for Creative Excellence and Black for Cause, Environment or Sustainability.\n\nShift Group also brought an unconventional approach to corporate awareness with JXG (Janashakthi Group) Sri Lanka\u2019s \u2018We\u2019re Sure You\u2019re Not Aware of Us\u2019. The approach successfully turned attention into awareness, earning two Black Dragons for Innovative Idea or Concept and Social Media.\n\nMeanwhile, \u2018Dengeez 2.0\u2019 for Softlogic Life continued the brand\u2019s unconventional approach to dengue awareness. The campaign earned a Black Dragon for Innovative Idea or Concept.\n\nShift Group CEO Sujeewa Samarasekera and Managing Director Chrishani Kotalawela said, \u201cThese wins are a reflection of what happens when strong client partnerships meet courageous thinking and an exceptional team.\u201d\n\nManaging Partner and Chief Creative Officer Sandun Lakmal said, \u201cThese campaigns allowed us to use creativity to challenge social norms, shine a light on important issues and find unexpected ways to engage people.\u201d\n\nShift Solutions CEO Charitha Waidyaratne added, \u201cThe eight wins are a tremendous achievement for the team and a testament to their passion, resilience and willingness to push beyond the obvious.\u201d"
