    "md5": "00b76718933f202a488d4b4264e9aa25",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1669,
    "chunk_text": "To answer your question- when I had to work with, for example the Communist Party and whether it clashes with the concept of entrepreneurship and entrepreneurial state-in today\u2019s context socialism does not clash with these two.\n\nThis is a quite a complex arrangement, both with the people, political parties, leaders and the rest of the stakeholders. You\u2019ve got to work with the state. In such as arrangement creating effective brands is a challenge. We as a team take it as a challenge\n\nQYou are known as a strategist who created brands and personalities. But do you think you have been successful in your own political campaign so far?\n\nNo a lot more needs to be done. As they say, just because I have been an effective strategist for other political campaigns does not necessarily guarantee the same for myself. So that\u2019s a challenge. We need to work on our strategies in crafting, communicating and building the brand \u2018Sarvajana Balaya\u2019. We need to work on strategies. We take challenges. But brands and personalities or political parties as brands is an evolving process. So it does not mean that you give your best product on the first day itself.\n\nBecause this is a quite a complex arrangement, both with the people, political parties, leaders and the rest of the stakeholders. You\u2019ve got to work with the state. In such as arrangement creating effective brands is a challenge. We as a team take it as a challenge. But we are confident that we can build a brand especially which is relevant to youth, GenZs, Gen Alpha and the millennials. But to answer your question am I happy so far? I really work harder on it, every day, 365 days while on the go."
  },
