    "chunk_text": "Because this is a quite a complex arrangement, both with the people, political parties, leaders and the rest of the stakeholders. You\u2019ve got to work with the state. In such as arrangement creating effective brands is a challenge. We as a team take it as a challenge. But we are confident that we can build a brand especially which is relevant to youth, GenZs, Gen Alpha and the millennials. But to answer your question am I happy so far? I really work harder on it, every day, 365 days while on the go.\n\nQOne common criticism levelled at the opposition- mainly the SJB and UNP- is that the leadership did not allow or give opportunities to build a second-tier leadership. Both the parties seem to be person centric. Even Sarvajana Balaya, we do not see much of the faces except you. Would you agree? Have you taken measures to build a second tier?\n\nOur whole plan is to build a second tier. We saw this as the biggest gap in Sri Lankan politics. But it is unfortunate that we haven\u2019t yet been successful enough in communicating the message that we are building our second tier.\n\nWe have taken very non-traditional steps to bring these new faces to the forefront. We have a programme called hundred new faces. So we are exposing this, especially the youth as our next leadership.\n\nWhy you are asking this question is because I have more visibility because I give leadership. The truth is that the media likes to take voice cuts or appearances of mine than the others in the party. If you take a look at district leaders and chief organizers in the districts, we have many professionals.\n\nWhich is why so far, we have been successful as a new party which is more than two years old. As you can see, we don\u2019t have to transport people to our meetings. Instead, we work with our ground level network. There we promote entrepreneurship, creativity. We got youth and it\u2019s working organically."
