    "md5": "0659da84c36fb86fdf719095ba4acd2e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1727,
    "chunk_text": "Gnanasara Thera reportedly missing after pardon annulled\n\nColombo, Sep. 14 (Daily Mirror) - Bodu Bala Sena (BBS) General Secretary Galagoda Aththe Gnanasara Thera is reportedly untraceable after the Supreme Court annulled the presidential pardon granted to him in 2019, requiring him to serve the remaining portion of his prison sentence.\n\nPrison officials had reportedly visited the Thera\u2019s temple in Nawala, Rajagiriya, to take steps to return him to prison. However, monks at the temple had informed the officials that they were unaware of his current whereabouts.\n\nA prison official said prison authorities could not take further action unless the Thera surrendered to the police or was taken into custody by the police.\n\nMeanwhile, a senior BBS official told the Daily Mirror that ethnic tensions in the country had declined following the identification of Zahran Hashim as the leader of the National Thawheed Jama'ath (NTJ), which the official alleged was responsible for the coordinated Easter Sunday bomb attacks.\n\nThe BBS official also claimed that Gnanasara Thera had never attempted to create ethnic conflict in the country.\n\nThe Supreme Court recently ruled that the presidential pardon granted to Gnanasara Thera by then-President Maithripala Sirisena in May 2019 was null and void. The Court held that the decision was arbitrary and violated public trust and principles of natural justice.Gnanasara Thera had been sentenced to six years in prison for contempt of court and had served around nine months of the sentence before receiving the presidential pardon.\n\nFollowing the Supreme Court ruling, he is required to serve the remaining portion of his sentence, subject to applicable legal and prison procedures."
  },
