    "md5": "f33a8ed947ae9b2c39f70572497569b4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1237,
    "chunk_text": "Complaint to CID over alleged LTTE promotion at SLPP rally\n\nColombo, Sep 14 (Daily Mirror) - A complaint has been lodged with the Criminal Investigation Department (CID) over the alleged promotion of the Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam (LTTE) at the Sri Lanka Podujana Peramuna (SLPP) rally held in Anuradhapura.\n\nPolice Spokesman ASP F.U. Wootler confirmed today that the complaint was lodged by a group of civil society members named \u201cjoint opposition\u201d following allegations that statements made during the rally amounted to promoting or supporting the LTTE, which remains a proscribed organisation in Sri Lanka.\n\nOn Sunday, the opposition had raised concerns over remarks reportedly made during the rally, where several political figures, including former Minister Wimal Weerawansa and Parliamentarian Archchuna Ramanathan, were present.\n\nAddressing the rally, MP Archchuna Ramanathan referred to himself as a\u00a0 \u201cTiger\u201d and criticized the people for electing a fox, referring to President Anura Kumara Dissanayake.\n\nThe move came as a surprise even to SLPP supporters who have long been critical of any reference to the LTTE but instead saw SLPP politicians cheering when the LTTE name was mentioned on stage in Anuradhapura."
  },
