    "chunk_size_bytes": 1907,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cPick a Book is a platform of possibilities, where books open doors to knowledge, meaningful connections, and the lifelong journey of becoming your best self,\u201d Ragulan said, adding that its next phase is considerably more ambitious.\n\nThe idea is to give individual clubs access to infrastructure, technology and networks that would be difficult to create independently, while allowing them to maintain their own identities.\n\n\u201cMost book clubs run on passion, but they can\u2019t build a platform, a home, the technology or the connections on their own. That takes scale. So we\u2019re opening ours. The things you couldn\u2019t build alone but now shared,\u201d Ragulan said.\n\nThe program will give authors direct access to engaged readers, publishers a network of reading communities and booksellers a channel to some of the country\u2019s most active book buyers.\n\nMore importantly, it represents a change in scale for Pick a Book - from creating readers to connecting the institutions and communities that make a reading culture possible.\n\nThat idea fits closely with the movement\u2019s philosophy. A book does not have to provide the final answer. It can instead create the question that leads to another book, another conversation or another way of seeing the world.\n\nPick a Book\u2019s social initiative, Read and Rise, is also gaining momentum. Launched last year with the donation of 30,000 books to children and communities with limited access to reading material, the program is now moving towards developing sustained reading habits.\n\nWeekly reading sessions are being conducted in underprivileged schools, shifting the focus from distributing books to developing regular readers.\n\n\u201cA book is a beginning, but a habit is what changes a life. This year we are moving from giving books to building readers, week after week, in the schools that need it most. Reading should never be a privilege,\u201d Ragulan said."
  },
