    "chunk_size_bytes": 1818,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka and Thailand to strengthen labour cooperation with signing  of landmark agreements\n\nSri Lanka and Thailand further strengthened bilateral cooperation in the field of labour with the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Labour Cooperation and a Memorandum of Agreement (MoA) on the Employment of Sri Lankan Workers in Thailand yesterday in Bangkok.\n\nThe two instruments were signed by Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Minister Vijitha Herath and Thai Labour Minister Julapun Amornvivat. The agreements follow sustained negotiations between the relevant authorities of the two countries and establish a structured and transparent framework for the recruitment and employment of Sri Lankan workers in Thailand, while promoting their rights, welfare, and protection.\n\nThe signing marks an important milestone in the expansion of safe, regular, and mutually beneficial labour mobility between Sri Lanka and Thailand. The Thai Cabinet has approved the recruitment of an initial 10,000 Sri Lankan workers through the established legal framework to address labour shortages in Thailand. The MoU provides a framework for cooperation in areas including labour policies and practices, labour market information, skills development, labour productivity, labour protection, and the prevention of illegal recruitment and human trafficking.\n\nThe MoA establishes the practical arrangements for the recruitment and employment of Sri Lankan workers in Thailand, including transparent recruitment procedures, employment contracts, legal protection, welfare, visas and work permits, as well as return and repatriation arrangements.\n\nTogether, the two instruments provide a comprehensive framework to facilitate the orderly employment of Sri Lankan workers while safeguarding their rights and welfare."
