    "chunk_text": "The MoA establishes the practical arrangements for the recruitment and employment of Sri Lankan workers in Thailand, including transparent recruitment procedures, employment contracts, legal protection, welfare, visas and work permits, as well as return and repatriation arrangements.\n\nTogether, the two instruments provide a comprehensive framework to facilitate the orderly employment of Sri Lankan workers while safeguarding their rights and welfare.\n\nIn this context, Minister Herath also sought Thailand\u2019s consideration of expanding employment opportunities for Sri Lankan nationals, particularly the youth, in the IT and tourism sectors, which could provide new avenues for skilled employment and contribute to the development of Sri Lanka\u2019s youth workforce.\n\nMinister Julapun said that the Sri Lankan workers employed under this framework will enjoy equal rights and protection under Thai labour law, including legally mandated wages, benefits, and health care. Beyond worker recruitment and employment, the MoU also provides a foundation for broader labour cooperation to strengthen the workforce of both countries in line with future labour market and economic developments.\n\nThe Government of Sri Lanka views Thailand and the wider Southeast Asian region as important emerging destinations for Sri Lankan workers, as Sri Lanka continues to explore and diversify new labour markets for its nationals. The similarities in social and cultural characteristics between Sri Lanka and many Southeast Asian countries are expected to enable Sri Lankan workers to adapt more readily to their new working and living environments.\n\nThe establishment of structured employment opportunities in Thailand is therefore an important step towards diversifying Sri Lanka\u2019s foreign employment destinations, expanding opportunities for skilled workers and professionals, particularly youth, and further strengthening the longstanding and multifaceted relations between Sri Lanka and Thailand."
