    "chunk_text": "Ambassador of Sri Lanka to Thailand, Wijayanthi Edirisinghe, participated in a panel discussion on \u201cStrengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s Gem and Jewellery Industry and Expanding Its Global Presence\u201d, alongside National Gem and Jewellery Authority (NGJA) Chairman Dr. S. P. Chaminda, and other industry leaders.\n\nSri Lankan exports to Thailand more than doubled in 2025, reaching over $ 90 million from approximately $ 41.6 million in 2024, with precious and semi-precious stones accounting for almost 70% of Sri Lanka\u2019s exports to Thailand.\n\n\u201cGem Sri Lanka 2027\u201d, scheduled to be held in Sri Lanka in January 2027, is expected to provide an important platform for international buyers, investors and industry stakeholders to explore Sri Lanka\u2019s gem and jewellery sector and establish new business partnerships."
