    "chunk_text": "During the award review period, HNB participated in several landmark transactions that demonstrated the increasing breadth of its corporate banking proposition. These included participation in the US $ 1 billion sustainability-linked syndicated financing for Aster Chemicals & Energy, cross-border acquisition financing involving Surge Global and Calcey Technologies and the arrangement of Rs.44.5 billion in syndicated financing for the 350MW Sobadhanavi power project.\n\nHNB\u2019s participation in the Aster Chemicals & Energy transaction also represented an important step in strengthening its involvement in complex international and sustainability-linked financing alongside leading global financial institutions.\n\nWeerasuriya said, \u201cReceiving this recognition for a second consecutive year is a strong endorsement of the trust our corporate clients place in HNB. Our focus has always been on understanding their businesses, anticipating their requirements and delivering solutions that extend beyond traditional financing. As Sri Lankan corporates pursue new opportunities locally and internationally, we will continue to strengthen our capabilities across financing, transaction banking, trade and digital solutions to help our clients grow sustainably and compete with confidence.\u201d"
