    "chunk_text": "Sampath Bank acquires Anilana\u2019s last 2 hotels under parate execution\n\nBoard contests takeover; tells court unnamed party has offered Rs.1.2bn for Nilaweli, Pasikudah\n\nJune quarter loss of Rs.88.5mn on zero revenue; negative net assets widen to Rs.615.7mn\n\nAnilana Hotels and Properties PLC\u2019s two remaining hotels in Nilaweli and Passikudah have been acquired by Sampath Bank PLC, under parate execution, closing off the strategic investor search the loss-making group launched a year ago, to restart its dormant properties, according to a filing with the Colombo Stock Exchange.\n\nThe properties were taken over under Recovery of Loans by Banks (Special Provisions) Act No. 04 of 1990, which allows the licensed commercial banks to sell the mortgaged property on a board resolution, without going to court.\n\nThe company annexed a letter from the bank dated August 31, 2026, which it received on September 01, confirming the acquisition. The disclosure was made to the bourse on September 11, ten days later.\n\nThe board is resisting the takeover on three fronts. Two cases have been filed in the Commercial High Court \u201cchallenging the resolution adopted by Sampath Bank PLC\u201d, both of which are now pending in appeal before the Supreme Court.\n\nSeparately, the company has applied under Companies Act No. 07 of 2007, informing the court of \u201ca prospective investor who had offered a sum of Rs.1.2 billion\u201d for the hotels, in an effort to compromise with the bank. The Commercial High Court has issued notice on Sampath Bank and the company said it would disclose the outcome \u201cin the event a compromise is reached between the bank and us\u201d.\n\nThe offer, if it holds, would cover only about 47 percent of the Rs.2.55 billion in borrowings carried on the group balance sheet as at end-June and a little over half the Rs.2.23 billion at which the group\u2019s property, plant and equipment are stated. The investor has not been identified in the filing."
