    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "abbf32ae2a315ebd1e0b773bd31f84be",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1959,
    "chunk_text": "SEC warns allegations risk denting confidence in capital market regulation\n\nConcerns relate to statements made publicly in Colombo last month and subsequently circulated through social media and other media channels\n\nCapital market regulator maintained that statements contained claims that were false, baseless, misleading, derogatory and defamatory and devoid of factual foundation\n\nAsserts statements undermine public confidence in integrity, independence and proper functioning of securities regulatory framework established under Sri Lankan law\n\nSEC has expressly reserved its right to seek appropriate relief, including injunctions, damages, compensation and costs\n\nThe capital market regulator, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka (SEC), has warned that the allegedly false and unsubstantiated claims against the regulator and its officials risk undermining public confidence in the integrity and independence of the country\u2019s capital market regulatory framework. The SEC\u2019s concerns relate to the statements made publicly in Colombo last month and subsequently circulated through social media and other media channels.\n\nTaking a serious view of the matter, the capital market regulator maintained that the statements contained claims that were false, baseless, misleading, derogatory and defamatory and devoid of factual foundation.\n\nThe SEC said such statements were likely to cause serious reputational damage to the SEC, its chairman, members and officers, while more importantly undermining the public confidence in the integrity, independence and proper functioning of the securities regulatory framework established under the Sri Lankan law.\n\nThe regulator has also taken issue with claims that it said sought to impugn the integrity, impartiality, competence and conduct of the SEC and its officials in discharging their statutory duties and functions under Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka Act No. 19 of 2021."
