    "md5": "659df54f718c7a6b3e106526f2edc6ea",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1880,
    "chunk_text": "The international audience doesn\u2019t understand the scale, brutality and complexity of Sri Lanka\u2019s armed conflict - Gen. Shavendra Silva\n\n\u201cI believe the more important question today is how societies prevent future cycles of terrorism, instability and state fragility\u201d-Gen. Shavendra Silva (Pix by Waruna Wanniarachchi)\n\nI continue to engage actively across the Indo-Pacific, Indian Ocean region, Asia, Africa and multilateral platforms where practical discussions on resilience and security governance are taking place. My focus and speeches are increasingly directed towards how states build resilience against both traditional and emerging threats\n\nFormer Commander of the Army and Chief of Defence Staff General (Retd.) Shavendra Silva is a battle-hardened military leader with an illustrious career spanning nearly 41 years. Having served under four Presidents and four Prime Ministers during his military career, he is also the only military officer to have been appointed as an Ambassador while in service. During the Vanni Humanitarian Operation, he commanded the victorious 58 Infantry Division, Commando and Air Mobile Brigades that fought relentlessly to eradicate terrorism from Sri Lankan. But according to General Silva, even though the war ended and Sri Lankans are enjoying the outcomes of achieving peace, people associated with the Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam (LTTE) are \u201cstill trying to achieve what they wanted to achieve.\u201d\n\nIn an exclusive interview with the Daily Mirror, General Silva spoke about how the final humanitarian operation unfolded, false narratives created by LTTE sympathizers living overseas, pain endured by civilians affected by the conflict and challenges faced during COVID-19 pandemic recovery efforts.\n\nQYou have had an illustrious career in the Army spanning 40 years. How does it feel like to retire from active service?"
