    "chunk_text": "QEven though we talk about reconciliation there are people who are still suffering as a result of the armed conflict. What are your thoughts?\n\nQDuring your tenure as Chief of Defence Staff and Army Commander you also headed the COVID-19 task force. How challenging was this operation?\n\nQHowever, at one point the government was scrutinised for carrying out mandatory vaccinations for instance. What do you have to say?\n\nWhen it came to vaccinations it was mainly based on the medical specialists\u2019 advices. The President had to make decisions based on these advices given at that particular time. After 5-6 years someone might look back and wonder whether these could have been done in a better manner. But at that particular time, somebody will have to execute a decision made by the consultant committee. When they said that vaccinations was the best way to prevent spread of the virus and protect people, we had to execute it. Today people might be talking about the vaccine, but at that time almost everybody was keen on being vaccinated.\n\nQ 17 years have elapsed since the war ended. Do you think Sri Lanka has achieved intended goals of recovery?"
