    "chunk_text": "Government rejects claims of diaspora funding to NPP\n\nColombo, Sep. 15 (Daily Mirror) - The Government today rejected allegations by MP Ramanathan Archchuna that the Tamil diaspora provided financial support to the National People\u2019s Power (NPP) for its election campaign.\n\nCabinet Spokesman Minister Nalinda Jayatissa said legal action would be taken against the MP over what he described as false statements.\n\nResponding to a question about Archchuna\u2019s recent remarks allegedly promoting the proscribed LTTE organisation at an SLPP rally in Anuradhapura, Minister Jayatissa said complaints had been lodged with the Police and the Criminal Investigation Department (CID)."
