    "md5": "bc9ef51dd3557d5796de93e15380a861",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1411,
    "chunk_text": "Professor Nethsinghe together with the Registrar of the University of Visual and Performing Arts, Dr. Chani Imbulgoda and Director, Centre for Research and Creative Work and Knowledge Dissemination of the University, Prof. Tharanga Dandeniya then announced a special programme UVPA PRAXIS 2026, an international conference to be held at the University premises on September 16th to the 18th.\n\nUVPA PRAXIS 2026 will comprise keynote speeches by local and international experts, panel discussions, performance items and screening of movies, paintings and photography exhibitions. The subjects covered will be traditional arts, history and memory, traditional dance identity and cultural continuance, digital media , visual semiotics and communication , heritage , ritual space and cultural identity, embodied dance technique and practice based knowledge, embodied dance techniques and practice based knowledge , music education , professional practice and therapy and performance pedagogy, movement and scenography, community memory and embodied expressions, music language , emotion and embodied performance and the Arts, community. Society and cultural change.\n\n\u201cWe hope to build a bridge between tradition and cultural heritage and modernity,\u201d Professor Nettisinghe said.\n\nInternational expert of folk music Professor Svanibor Pettem, performance artist Tim Crouch are expected to participate in the event."
  },
