    "chunk_text": "Railway Operating Service Union supports Sept. 17-18 action\n\nColombo, Sep. 16 (Daily Mirror) - The Railway Technological and Operating Service Union has announced that it will join the joint trade union action scheduled for September 17 and 18, while calling for the intervention of the authorities over issues affecting the railway service.\n\nIn a letter addressed to the Secretary of the Railway Joint Trade Union Alliance, the union expressed support for the proposed trade union action and said it would actively participate in the process.\n\nThe union also raised serious concerns over the performance of the current General Manager of Railways, alleging that the administration has failed to maintain the progress and standards of the railway service.\n\nIt said the long-standing issue of delayed pension processing for railway employees had also not been resolved, despite expectations that the General Manager's previous experience in using technology to streamline administrative processes would help address the problem.\n\nThe union argued that the head of the Railway Department requires expertise suited to a highly specialised engineering and operational institution, and warned that continued experimentation with the administration of the department could further affect the service.\n\nThe union said it would participate in the joint trade union action to draw the special attention of President Anura Kumara Dissanayake to the issues."
