    "md5": "b613671c166f3b475e2d16c472555496",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1907,
    "chunk_text": "SAJ expands product range through growing Lakarcade network\n\nSAJ Associates Ltd., is expanding its product range through the growing network of Lakarcade, which currently holds a significant share of Sri Lanka\u2019s souvenir and gift market.\n\nLakarcade has recently strengthened its market presence with the opening of a new souvenir shop at a hotel in Colombo.\n\nThrough its expanding network of showrooms across the country, the company is taking the skills and capabilities of Sri Lankan craftsmen directly to tourists.\n\nSAJ Associates Founder Jayampathy Arambepola said the company was pleased to introduce a new range of products to cater to the increasing number of tourists arriving in Sri Lanka this season.\n\n\u201cWe are extremely happy to state that we are moving forward to cater to the increasing tourist arrivals this season with an additional new range of products through the expanding network of Lakarcade.\u201d\n\nHe further explained that SAJ Associates had been working closely with Lakarcade for the past one and a half years.\n\n\u201cWe initially started with 12 glycerine-based soaps and then expanded our range with another 12 products, comprising four shampoos, four conditioners and four liquid soaps. We are now privileged to add four more face creams and two face washes, bringing our total range to 30 high-quality products targeted at the tourist and diaspora markets.\u201d\n\nArambepola said Lakarcade\u2019s expanding network of exclusive outlets in key tourist locations would further improve the availability of SAJ products to visitors.\n\n\u201cThe expanding network of Lakarcade, with exclusive shops at very important locations, will enhance the availability of our products to tourists,\u201d he said.\n\nHe added that Lakarcade\u2019s focus on the specialised tourist gift market, together with its new showrooms, including the outlet at Shangri-La Hotel, would create further opportunities for growth."
  },
