    "chunk_size_bytes": 1526,
    "chunk_text": "Though occasioned by Karuna\u2019s rebellion and the intra-LTTE mini civil war in the East, with Karuna already on the backfoot, my prognosis was grounded far more in the comparative study of successful asymmetric wars; Prabhakaran\u2019s sustained transgression of their characteristic features and norms; and the axiom of Vietnam\u2019s General Giap that \u201cif you override the objective laws of development of a phenomenon, those objective laws will override you\u201d.\n\nReal-time social media coverage and TV newscasts showed that the Anuradhapura rally of the SLPP and partners, with Mahinda Rajapaksa on stage, was discernibly larger than the ruling party\u2019s public meetings in Polonnaruwa and Anuradhapura (the next day), featuring President Anura Dissanayake.\n\nAnuradhapura was a more organic mass mobilisation. The SLPP rally was energised by a cocktail of strong emotions\u2014overweening affection and respect for Mahinda Rajapaksa, combative loyalty to the incarcerated Namal Rajapaksa, open declaration of a determination to ensure Namal\u2019s election as President in 2029, renewed collective hope at that prospect, defiant resistance to the ruling JVP-NPP and reawakened bitter memories of JVP barbarism in the locality. (Especially poignant was the recollection of the JVP\u2019s murder in 1987 in the Anuradhapura bazaar, of Nandana Marasinghe, a hero of the JVP\u2019s April 1971 uprising). The mood was more upbeat and applause from the audience was far more spontaneous, animated, enthusiastic and frequent at SLPP/Anuradhapura."
  },
