    "chunk_size_bytes": 1944,
    "chunk_text": "AKD\u2019s Polonnaruwa and Anuradhapura speeches had nothing of the appeal his oratory had in 2024. The thrill was gone. All he had was a surly negativism, a truculently articulated commitment to \u2018lawfare\u2019 (amounting to a McCarthyite witch-hunt) against the Rajapaksa family. No credible, constructive hope for an improved life was communicated. His appeal has been funnelled-down to reassuring and remotivating the JVP-NPP hardcore. The combative cockiness of AKD and other JVP-NPP leaders, is hollow.\n\nAKD has embarked on a highly polarising two-pronged project. The dynamic of polarisation that cannot possibly work in his favour; it can only undermine him and his Government, shrinking its space.\n\nAnura and the JVP-NPP do not seem to understand that the legitimacy enjoyed by Mahinda is long, deep and unassailable because his achievement in winning in three years a 30-year war and restoring peace and territorial unity, is historic. That historic legitimacy sheds a penumbra of sympathy in the mass mind, on his son Namal and spouse Shiranthi.\n\nMahinda\u2019s legitimacy in the mass-mind, is that of a living legend, rooted in the Mahavamsa matrix of real and mythicised history. Targeting Mahinda\u2019s emotional and physical wellbeing by targeting his family, depletes governmental legitimacy and popularity.\n\nAKD is indirectly targeting a man and directly targeting the family of that man whose popularity and legitimacy he will never begin to approximate. It is a battle he may win in the post-22A courts but can never win in the hearts and minds of the people.\n\nThe mechanism of jailing people before they are convicted of a crime also raises questions of natural justice. This is more so when it comes to a family that shared deadly risks when its patriarch was leading the country in a titanic war against the world\u2019s worst terrorism. The family could have chosen to spend the war safely overseas in East Asia/Eurasia, but didn\u2019t."
