    "chunk_size_bytes": 1853,
    "chunk_text": "The mechanism of jailing people before they are convicted of a crime also raises questions of natural justice. This is more so when it comes to a family that shared deadly risks when its patriarch was leading the country in a titanic war against the world\u2019s worst terrorism. The family could have chosen to spend the war safely overseas in East Asia/Eurasia, but didn\u2019t.\n\nThey now seem to be \u2018soft targets\u2019 which the JVP was notorious for, e.g., Vijaya Kumaratunga. Public memory will recall the barbaric lethal targeting of relatives and whole families by the JVP in the late 1980s. This time the vengeful targeting of families isn\u2019t lethal but legal.\n\nMahinda\u2019s legitimacy in the mass-mind, is that of a living legend, rooted in the Mahavamsa matrix of real and mythicised history. Targeting Mahinda\u2019s emotional and physical wellbeing by targeting his family, depletes governmental legitimacy and popularity\n\nThe second prong of Anura\u2019s lawfare is the \u2018Inquisition\u2019 against the top-brass of the war-winning military; a military perceived as having played the role of liberators of the island\u2019s vast majority.\n\nThus, Anura\u2019s double-barrelled campaign is against two targets\u2014the family of Mahinda Rajapaksa, the living national patriarch, and the victorious military high command. These two targets are components of the war-winning \u2018power-bloc\u2019, and taken together constitute a single composite target. Such a sweeping witch-hunt of the political and military victors in a historic national war would be riskily destabilising in any post-war society.\n\nMoreover, AKD\u2019s polarising \u2018lawfare\u2019 takes place while the ground the Government stands on is being eroded by the heart-rending economic suffering of \u201cthe working poor\u201d as journalist Methmalie Dissanayake has put it in an exceptional piece of social reportage."
