    "md5": "79032d7203f894bca3dbef51e771e2b1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1865,
    "chunk_text": "Moreover, AKD\u2019s polarising \u2018lawfare\u2019 takes place while the ground the Government stands on is being eroded by the heart-rending economic suffering of \u201cthe working poor\u201d as journalist Methmalie Dissanayake has put it in an exceptional piece of social reportage.\n\nThe post-Anuradhapura tri-polarity will damage the Government for two major reasons:\n\nAs foreign experts have pointed out, the debt repayment really starts biting in 2028 and will probably be compounded by the requirements of an unavoidable IMF program when the current one ends in 2027.\n\nAKD-JVP-NPP will be besieged on two fronts, the centrist/centre-right, and nationalist-populist/statist-populist. The SJB and SLPP will each take a \u2018limb\u2019 in its jaws and pull the NPP\u2019s 2024 socio-electoral bloc apart. (The NPP just lost the Eppawela Multi-Purpose Cooperative Society election to the SJB-led Opposition).\n\nWith a rampaging national \u2018crisis of affordability\u2019 (to borrow New York Mayor Mamdani\u2019s famous phrase), the AKD-NPP bloc will hardly win a two-front battle in the heartland with the SJB and SLPP. The SJB will savage it on economics and governance; the SLPP will do so on economics and nationalism. Because of its small but raucous old allies, the SLPP may forfeit minority votes that Namal could win back, but that won\u2019t save the JVP-NPP since some of its minority votes will go to Sajith and the SJB.\n\nIf unfairly imprisoned, could \u2018Release Namal!\u2019 motivate voters in 2029?\n\nStrictly theoretically, 2029 should be something of a slam-dunk for Sajith, because the unprecedented growth of poverty and inequality should provide a socioeconomic majority for him if he deploys the franchise he holds exclusively, i.e., that of the developmentalist-populist paradigm of his father President Premadasa. Today\u2019s political narrative is also about \u2018Fathers and Sons\u2019"
