    "chunk_size_bytes": 2010,
    "chunk_text": "Strictly theoretically, 2029 should be something of a slam-dunk for Sajith, because the unprecedented growth of poverty and inequality should provide a socioeconomic majority for him if he deploys the franchise he holds exclusively, i.e., that of the developmentalist-populist paradigm of his father President Premadasa. Today\u2019s political narrative is also about \u2018Fathers and Sons\u2019\n\nSo also, with the AKD-JVP-NPP rulers and the Opposition. What is currently primary will become secondary, and what is currently secondary will become primary.\n\nMao Zedong and General Giap, geniuses of asymmetric conflict, perceived three stages of development: (a) strategic defensive (b) contention or equilibrium (c) strategic counteroffensive. With the SLPP\u2019s fierce fightback in Anuradhapura, the overall political struggle shifted from the Opposition on the strategic defensive and the Govt on the strategic offensive, to the second stage: the Opposition in a mode of contention, and a resultant equilibrium between Government and Opposition in public perception and opinion.\n\nIt is illogical to accurately condemn the 22nd Amendment as an attempt by the executive to coopt the judiciary, while simultaneously staying non-committal on NR, on the presumption that a transparently fair trial is structurally possible post-22A, especially for a Rajapaksa rival of the rulers.\n\nSilence is also unwise because AKD will inevitably attempt to entrench his incumbency by using \u2018lawfare\u2019 against Sajith and other non-SLPP Opposition candidates too.\n\nThat said, the SLPP\u2019s revival is certain to spur the SJB from trot to canter.\n\nStrictly theoretically, 2029 should be something of a slam-dunk for Sajith, because the unprecedented growth of poverty and inequality should provide a socioeconomic majority for him if he deploys the franchise he holds exclusively, i.e., that of the developmentalist-populist paradigm of his father President Premadasa. Today\u2019s political narrative is also about \u2018Fathers and Sons\u2019."
