    "md5": "8cb916b340c0b27f3c9de4356780f5dc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1388,
    "chunk_text": "Any SJB-UNP convergence can decisively attract votes only if such a convergence takes place on the basis of a shift to progressive centrism/social democracy and the revival of President Premadasa\u2019s pro-people development paradigm.\n\nYou cannot fight a battle effectively if you share the same ideological-paradigmatic space as the enemy. Sajith Premadasa certainly doesn\u2019t share AKD\u2019s views on the economy, but the SJB\u2019s lead economist Dr. Harsha de Silva plays softball.\n\nIn the remake of The Magnificent Seven with Denzel Washington (I preferred the 1960 original with Yul Brynner), Ethan Hawke, playing a burnt-out ace marksman and former officer in the defeated Confederate Army, tries to train the hopelessly inaccurate townsfolk in rifle shooting. In frustrated irritation, he yells at one point \u201cyou\u2019ve got to hate what you\u2019re shooting at!\u201d \u2013 and demonstrates by unerringly shooting the straw heads off the line of scarecrows erected for target practice.\u00a0 So long as it stays a centre-right party espousing and thereby tacitly endorsing a neoliberal right-wing economic agenda, the SJB can\u2019t \u2018hate\u2019 what the AKD-JVP-NPP is doing in economics.\u00a0 By contrast, the SLPP as a party with a rather more \u2018Statist\u2019 Rajapaksa ideology, takes a greater distance from the ruling bloc, and therefore can naturally, instinctively, hit the electoral adversary harder."
