    "chunk_text": "In the remake of The Magnificent Seven with Denzel Washington (I preferred the 1960 original with Yul Brynner), Ethan Hawke, playing a burnt-out ace marksman and former officer in the defeated Confederate Army, tries to train the hopelessly inaccurate townsfolk in rifle shooting. In frustrated irritation, he yells at one point \u201cyou\u2019ve got to hate what you\u2019re shooting at!\u201d \u2013 and demonstrates by unerringly shooting the straw heads off the line of scarecrows erected for target practice.\u00a0 So long as it stays a centre-right party espousing and thereby tacitly endorsing a neoliberal right-wing economic agenda, the SJB can\u2019t \u2018hate\u2019 what the AKD-JVP-NPP is doing in economics.\u00a0 By contrast, the SLPP as a party with a rather more \u2018Statist\u2019 Rajapaksa ideology, takes a greater distance from the ruling bloc, and therefore can naturally, instinctively, hit the electoral adversary harder.\n\nThe JVP-NPP won in 2024 because the two main democratic parties were in severe crisis:\n\nThe SLPP lost, crashed and splintered because it had shifted from Mahinda Rajapaksa\u2019s pragmatic-progressivism to Gotabaya\u2019s Far Right ideology, banned imports of agrochemicals overnight, was overthrown by the people, and fissured by clinging to President Ranil Wickremesinghe (the \u2018Gas Cylinder\u2019) while Namal Rajapaksa fought bravely to return the party to its roots.\n\nThe SJB which had initiated the Galle Face struggle with a militant march to the Presidential Secretariat and a speech by Sajith challenging Gotabaya, failed to serve as a Premadasa-ist populist Opposition when Ranil\u2019s harsh austerity policy was massively alienating people. SJB\u2019s Harsha and Eran urged\u2014and cheered\u2014\u201cpainful\u201d reforms. Sajith failed to veto them and override their line.\n\nAKD and the JVP-NPP moved into the breach opened by the SLPP and SJB."
  },
