    "md5": "b3ba88a4115665dfda3828da132b2739",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1329,
    "chunk_text": "Namal remanded until 23 Sept. over Airbus money laundering probe\n\nParliamentarian Namal Rajapaksa was ordered to remain in remand custody until 23 September by the Colombo Fort Magistrate\u2019s Court yesterday (16), after being produced as a suspect in an investigation into the alleged misuse of approximately $ 2 million during the procurement of Airbus aircraft by SriLankan Airlines.\n\nThe court also ordered that its decision on Rajapaksa\u2019s bail application be delivered on 23 September.\n\nRajapaksa, who is currently in remand custody, was produced before the Colombo Fort Magistrate\u2019s Court yesterday in connection with the investigation. He was recently named as a suspect in a money laundering case linked to alleged financial irregularities surrounding SriLankan Airlines\u2019 aircraft procurement process.\n\nFollowing submissions made by Deputy Solicitor General Janaka Bandara on behalf of the Criminal Investigation Department (CID), and a legal team led by President\u2019s Counsel Anil Silva representing Rajapaksa, Fort Magistrate Pasan Amarasena issued the order.\n\nThe money laundering investigation is related to the controversial 2013 SriLankan Airlines Airbus procurement. Rajapaksa was named as a suspect following instructions from the Attorney General after investigators submitted material relating to the case."
