    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "7c86d984fea6eeec0f50a2749471c27a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1657,
    "chunk_text": "Roar Global introduces Sri Lanka\u2019s first AI gateway\n\nRoar AI brings more than 200 frontier and open-source AI models together with locally hosted infrastructure, giving Sri Lankan developers and businesses a simpler way to build and scale with AI\n\nRoar Global has introduced Roar AI, Sri Lanka\u2019s first AI gateway, giving developers, startups and businesses access to over 200 leading frontier and open-source AI models through a single platform.\n\nBuilt in Sri Lanka, Roar AI is designed to address some of the practical barriers organisations face when building with artificial intelligence - from fragmented access to multiple models and complex international payments to application hosting, cost management and data governance.\n\nThrough a single integration, Roar AI users can access and build with a wide range of global AI models such as Anthropic, Gemini, Perplexity, Llama, DeepSeek and Mistral - choosing the right model for each application or workload without having to manage multiple platforms, accounts and billing relationships.\n\nBeyond model access, Roar AI provides the infrastructure needed to deploy and operate AI applications, including locally hosted applications, integrated databases, transactional email and automated backups. The platform also incorporates usage controls, budgets and guardrails to help organisations manage how AI is accessed and used across their teams.\n\nBilling in Sri Lankan rupees gives local businesses greater predictability and control over AI expenditure, while local infrastructure and engineering support provide a closer-to-home option for organisations looking to build and operate AI applications."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
