    "language": "en",
    "md5": "f535ed5fde4e7c069f95e31c0f746846",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1981,
    "chunk_text": "PwC-FCCISL Business Resurgence Study Project Chairman Ruwan De Silva, led the research and consolidation of the interconnected reform framework. These proposals reflect the longstanding need for coordinated institutional support and practical business recovery mechanisms.\n\nFCCISL has also prepared and submitted \u201cSri Lanka\u2019s Path to Inclusion in the World Bank\u2019s Business Ready (B-READY) Index,\u201d supporting coordinated business-environment reforms.\n\nWorking with ministries, regulators, district and provincial institutions, FCCISL and other chambers, the NBFC could map business constraints against these pillars, coordinate responsible agencies, introduce clear service standards and deadlines, and monitor implementation through measurable indicators.\n\nIndividual business issues should enter an accessible registration and tracking process, with appropriate escalation for institutional or policy resolution. District-level feedback can identify recurring barriers, while digital services and transparent reporting can demonstrate whether reforms reduce delays, costs and uncertainty.\n\nThis collaboration could support effective engagement with World Bank B-READY assessments and stronger international benchmarking. Participation and assessment outcomes remain subject to World Bank processes. The objective should be practical improvements that enable enterprises to compete effectively in domestic and global markets.\n\n\u201cThe NBFC offers a significant opportunity to rebuild enterprise capacity and strengthen the relationship between the State and the business community. FCCISL is committed to contributing practical experience, research and implementable proposals to support regional and national business recovery, expansion and integration into economic value chains,\u201d stated Ruwan De Silva.\n\nFCCISL looks forward to constructive collaboration to make the NBFC an accessible, accountable and results-oriented platform serving entrepreneurs across Sri Lanka."
  },
