    "md5": "0d218ad911ffaa6b57ee83a82b8a7368",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1985,
    "chunk_text": "Central Bank hosts inaugural Reserve Management Conference\n\nCentral Bank Governor Dr. Nandalal Weerasinghe delivers keynote address at inaugural Reserve Management Conference\n\nAIIB Treasurer Domenico Nardelli delivers Special Guest Address at Reserve Management Conference\n\nThe Central Bank successfully hosted its inaugural Reserve Management Conference on September 10 and 11, 2026, at The Kingsbury, Colombo.\n\nThis distinguished gathering brought together leading central bankers, sovereign asset managers, policymakers, economists and investment professionals to exchange perspectives on the evolving global challenges and opportunities shaping the official reserve management.\n\nApproximately 50 speakers and participants joined the conference, representing institutions including the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB), Asian Development Bank, Banque de France, Bank for International Settlements, Bank Indonesia, Bank Negara Malaysia, Bank of Korea, Bank of Thailand, Inter-American Development Bank, Reserve Bank of India, Swiss National Bank, World Bank and World Gold Council.\n\nThe conference addressed a broad range of issues shaping the future of reserve management.\n\nThe key areas of discussion included strategies for building and strengthening foreign reserve buffers, implications of geopolitical fragmentation for Asia and the global economy, evolving role of digital and tokenised assets in official reserves, currency power and the continued prominence of the US dollar in international reserve portfolios and the role of gold and other alternative assets.\n\nThe participants also explored how technological innovation and artificial intelligence could support reserve management through enhanced investment decision-making, market intelligence, portfolio optimisation and risk management.\n\nThe keynote address was delivered by Central Bank Governor Dr. Nandalal Weerasinghe, on \u2018Challenges in Building Foreign Reserves Amidst Geopolitical Uncertainties\u2019."
  },
