    "chunk_text": "The provision alone is equivalent to 48 percent of the pre-tax profit reported in the interim accounts and 7 percent of equity. However, it accounts for only part of the Rs.338 million decline in profit.\n\nThe fallout also extends into the current year\u2019s accounts, as the audited equity of Rs.3.61 billion sits Rs.429.5 million below the unaudited March figure, on which the June quarter interim statements, released on August 11, were built. On the audited base, the net assets per share fell to around Rs.17.09, from Rs.19.12.\n\nMeanwhile, the June quarter accounts point to a business still expanding at pace, with the profit rising 51 percent year-on-year to Rs.90.4 million, already exceeding the audited profit for the whole of the previous financial year, on the back of a 35 percent jump in the interest income to Rs.1.83 billion.\n\nGold loans generated Rs.70.7 million or 78 percent of the quarter\u2019s profit, while the leasing segment\u2019s contribution fell 42 percent to Rs.24.4 million. Bank overdrafts climbed 68 percent to Rs.1.42 billion over the same three months.\n\nJanashakthi Limited controls close to 93 percent of the company through direct and custodial holdings. The company has been listed on the CSE\u2019s Second Board since March 2021, as its 6.14 percent public float falls short of the minimum public holding requirement.\n\nThe company stated that it intends to complete remedial action \u201cat the earliest possible time and within the timeframe stipulated under the Listing Rules, subject to independent verification by the external auditors\u201d. (NF)"
