    "chunk_text": "Meanwhile, Secretary to Prime Minister G. Pradeep Saputhanthri, attending as the chief guest, pointed out that Sri Lanka is undertaking important economic and structural reforms as it rebuilds from the most difficult economic crisis in its recent history. At the same time, artificial intelligence and other technologies are changing businesses, institutions and the way decisions are made.\n\n\u201cFor directors, technology can no longer be left entirely to technical specialists. It has become a question of governance, accountability and institutional responsibility,\u201d he observed.\n\nStrong institutions need accountability, integrity, transparency and the rule of law and their quality is shaped not by the government alone but also in boardrooms, businesses and professional bodies, he stressed.\n\n\u201cGood governance and performance are not competing objectives over time. One sustains the other,\u201d Saputhanthri added, noting that leadership is measured not only by results but by the strength of the institutions left behind."
