    "chunk_text": "Transportation grew 3.1 percent, supported by an 8.9 percent increase in port cargo and a 12.0 percent expansion in transport-support and warehousing activities. However, air passenger kilometres declined 15.8 percent and water transport contracted 6.1 percent.\n\nThe computer-services earnings alone, however, fell to US $ 195 million, from US $ 216 million, with the overall increase driven by the gains in the other business-service categories.\n\nOverall, the 2Q performance shows the economy is still expanding at a relatively firm pace, however, with the increasingly different fortunes across sectors.\n\nConstruction, mining, finance and selected services are driving growth, while agriculture, apparel and tourism remain exposed to the domestic supply constraints and external shocks."
