    "date_str": "2026-09-17",
    "description": "MasterChef Sri Lanka Judges Clarify the Context Behind the Challenge",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/opinion/MasterChef-Sri-Lanka-Judges-Clarify-the-Context-Behind-the-Challenge/231-350508",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1789626182.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-17-dailymirrorlk-fc13b7e3-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "78569085238ca00fea993801f7eed822",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1791,
    "chunk_text": "MasterChef Sri Lanka Judges Clarify the Context Behind the Challenge\n\nUnderstanding the responsibility that we have as judges gets harder every day because, at the end of the day, you are shaping someone\u2019s dream.\u201d\n\nSeason 2 now is solidifying MasterChef Sri Lanka on the global platform as something Sri Lanka can do as well, which is why I\u2019m here.\u201d\n\nMasterChef Sri Lanka returned for its second season with a redesigned studio, a more experienced production team and a new group of contestants. Judges Peter Kuruvita and Savindri Perera spoke on how the programme has developed, the context behind a recent challenge, the choices available to contestants and the support provided during the competition. Excerpts of the interview:\n\nQSeason 2 of MasterChef Sri Lanka has attracted considerable attention. How has the programme developed since its first season?\n\nSavindri Perera: I think there\u2019s a lot more effort that\u2019s now gone into Season 2, because obviously Season 1 was a learning curve for all people, including myself. Now, you know, we have redone the studio. I think the audience is really responding to that.\n\nFor me personally, I was on the side of the contestants. That\u2019s how I ended up in this seat. I\u2019ve not lost the novelty of seeing someone walk into this space for the first time, because I still remember that feeling as well. Understanding the responsibility that we have as judges gets harder every day because, at the end of the day, you are shaping someone\u2019s dream. That\u2019s not lost on me at all.\n\nI am thoroughly enjoying this season, I think probably a bit more than Season 1, because things are running a bit smoother now. The entire crew understands the production a lot better, and I believe it will just continue to get better as we go through."
  },
