    "md5": "a0aa504ac7d456982f6d414957a7c5be",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1650,
    "chunk_text": "The Opposition: NPP\u2019s greatest asset\n\nColombo, September 17 (Daily Mirror)- One wonders whether the public rally organised by the Sri Lanka Podujana Peramuna (SLPP) with massive publicity in Anuradhapura last Saturday \u2014 intended to create a favorable political wave across the country \u2014 has instead turned into a political disaster for the party itself.\n\nThe meeting appeared to be a chaotic blend of political contradictions, conducted without a clear realisation of who is a friend and who is an enemy. At a time when the party needed to demonstrate that they are engaged in meaningful, civilised politics superior to the ruling National People's Power (NPP), the rally degenerated into a farce filled with contradictions and lack of discipline.\n\nPrior to the meeting, hundreds of attendees under the heavy influence of alcohol were seen behaving deplorably in videos widely shared on social media. The slogans raised by some of these individuals went so far as to openly brand the party's national organizer, Namal Rajapaksa \u2014 who is positioned to lead the party \u2014 as a \"thief\".\n\nAccording to social media footages, several attendees explicitly stated that although they showed up at the meeting, they would not vote for SLPP in the upcoming elections. They even added that if Namal had plundered public property, he must face the full force of the law.\n\nThese individuals cannot be genuine supporters of the SLPP. Instead, it seems that the event organisers simply brought in whoever they could find to fill the venue. The disruptive behaviour of these highly intoxicated crowds did absolutely nothing to restore the party's reputation."
  },
