    "chunk_size_bytes": 882,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s first battery storage, floating solar plant to open tomorrow\n\nColombo, September 17 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka\u2019s first Battery Energy Storage System (BESS), aimed at strengthening renewable energy capacity and improving the stability of the national electricity grid, will be inaugurated tomorrow (18) in Anuradhapura.\n\nThe inauguration will be held in the morning under the patronage of President Anura Kumara Dissanayake, with the participation of Minister of Ports, Civil Aviation and Energy Anura Karunathilake.\n\nMeanwhile, the \u201cDiya Janani\u201d floating solar power plant, constructed on the Ibbankatuwa Reservoir in Dambulla under the Government\u2019s national renewable energy generation programme, will also be inaugurated tomorrow afternoon.\n\nThe event will be held under the patronage of President Dissanayake, with Minister Karunathilake also participating."
