    "md5": "4a19b81867f4a2f153e533adf1840583",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1480,
    "chunk_text": "The MP, who identified himself as a doctor, said he had served in hospitals including Kalubowila and Peradeniya and had treated Sinhala patients throughout his career.\n\n\u201cI have been a doctor for the past 40 years. If I represented the LTTE, I would not have been able to provide medicine to Sinhala people,\u201d he said.\n\nArchchuna said he was not afraid of being questioned or arrested under the Prevention of Terrorism Act (PTA), adding that he would cooperate if summoned by the Terrorism Investigation Division (TID).\n\n\u201cIf I am told to report to the TID, I can come there wearing slippers, shorts and a T-shirt,\u201d he said.\n\nHe said there was no need for authorities to pursue or arrest him and invited the TID to inform him if his presence was required.\n\n\u201cI request the TID to send me the location through WhatsApp. I will be there. There is no need to chase me and catch me,\u201d he said.\n\nArchchuna also urged President Anura Kumara Dissanayake to focus on what he described as major cases rather than pursuing \u201csmall people\u201d.\n\nReferring to former Central Bank Governor Arjuna Mahendran in connection with the Central Bank bond controversy, he called for individuals wanted in connection with major cases to be brought before the law.\n\nArchchuna said he had previously asked people to vote for the present government but had since become disappointed.\n\n\u201cI requested people to vote for this government. Now I also feel ashamed that I asked them to do so,\u201d he said."
