    "md5": "7a8c9c7ca76faaf41e1e18041c4ca73e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1129,
    "chunk_text": "Senior SLPP member remanded over permit corruption charges\n\nThe Colombo Magistrate\u2019s Court yesterday ordered that National Transport Commission Former Chairman Renuka Perera be remanded until 29 September, 2026, following his arrest by the Bribery Commission in connection with a corruption allegation.\n\nThe remand order was issued by Colombo Chief Magistrate Asanga S. Bodaragama after considering submissions from Bribery Commission officials and Perera\u2019s lawyers. Perera, a senior Sri Lanka Podujana Peramuna (SLPP) figure, was produced before the court earlier in the day, after which the order was delivered.\n\nInvestigating officers told the court that Perera was arrested over the issuance of 56 passenger transport permits for the Southern Expressway in violation of regulations, and that he was taken into custody on charges of corruption.\n\nAccording to the submissions, the permits were issued outside Cabinet approval, with 30 allocated to Perera\u2019s committee and 26 distributed at his own discretion to individuals of his choice.\n\nThe Bribery Commission said it is conducting further investigations into the case."
  },
