    "md5": "0351b89da2bbc195694349fbff1c3655",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1439,
    "chunk_text": "This landmark achievement inaugurates a new chapter in Sri Lanka\u2019s energy journey, one where storage technology transforms the country\u2019s abundant renewable resources into dependable, dispatchable power. This partnership between the public and private sectors marks a historic breakthrough, advancing resilience, sustainability, and national progress.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s energy transition is about much more than batteries, solar panels, or renewable energy targets. It is about making intelligent use of the exceptional natural resources our country has been endowed with, and converting them into lasting economic and national value.\n\nOur abundant sunshine, together with our hydropower and wind potential, gives us a strong foundation for a cleaner and more self-reliant future. According to the Sri Lanka Sustainable Energy Authority, the country\u2019s renewable energy potential exceeds 13,000 MW including 6,700 MW of solar, 4,000 MW of offshore wind, 1,860 MW of mini hydro, and 300 MW of biomass (Sri Lanka Sustainable Energy Authority, 2025) more than double our current installed capacity.\n\nBattery Energy Storage Systems are central to unlocking this potential. They provide the flexibility to store renewable electricity when it is abundant and release it when it is most needed, helping manage generation fluctuations, support grid stability, reduce renewable energy wastage, and strengthen the reliability of electricity supply."
