    "md5": "ad5f744e5796aae8c8c672a4f1d86bf6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1180,
    "chunk_text": "The 63rd session of the United Nations Human Rights Council (UNHRC) is currently underway in Geneva. The UN High Commissioner for Human Rights Volker T\u00fcrk released a comprehensive report on Sri Lanka, urging robust accountability, institutional reforms and a moratorium on the Prevention of Terrorism Act.As an experienced politician who served various portfolios as a foreign minister and minister of external affairs and having represented Sri Lanka on various international platforms, Prof. G. L. Peiris spoke to the Daily Mirror regarding his observations on the High Commissioner\u2019s report. He raised concerns regarding the way the incumbent government is handling the country\u2019s foreign policy while highlighting repercussions of the inability to deliver its promises made to international organisations such as the United Nations. Excerpts:\n\nQ What are your thoughts regarding United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights Volker T\u00fcrk\u2019s report on Sri Lanka?\n\nQ The UN has consistently pressured Sri Lanka to repeal the PTA. The incumbent government has instead proposed the Protection of State against Terrorism Act. What are your thoughts regarding this new Act?"
