    "chunk_size_bytes": 1647,
    "chunk_text": "ITFC signs $ 1.5 b framework agreement with Maldives Govt.\n\nITFC Chief Executive Officer Eng. Adeeb Yousuf Al-Aama (left) with Maldives Finance and Public Enterprises Minister and IsDB Governor for the Maldives Hassan Zareer\n\nIslamic Development Bank Group member to support trade financing operations in the Maldives between 2026 and 2031\n\nThe International Islamic Trade Finance Corporation (ITFC), a member of the Islamic Development Bank (IsDB) Group, and the Government of the Republic of Maldives have signed a new five-year Framework Agreement.\n\nUnder the agreement, ITFC will mobilise up to $ 1.5 billion to support trade financing operations in the Maldives between 2026 and 2031.\n\nThe agreement was signed at the Ministry of Finance and Public Enterprises in Mal\u00e9 recently by ITFC Chief Executive Officer Eng. Adeeb Yousuf Al-Aama and Maldives Minister of Finance and Public Enterprises and IsDB Governor for the Maldives Hassan Zareer during the ITFC CEO\u2019s official visit to the country.\n\nAs part of the visit, Maldives President Dr. Mohamed Muizzu granted audience to CEO Eng. Adeeb Al-Aama, to discuss strengthening cooperation between ITFC and the Maldives and supporting the country\u2019s economic priorities.\n\nThe Framework Agreement covers financing for the import of essential and strategic commodities, primarily through state owned enterprises, as well as lines of financing to local banks in the Maldives to support SMEs and the private sector. The parties will also explore trade-related technical assistance and advisory services to enhance trade capacity and market access, in line with the Maldives\u2019 development agenda."
  },
