    "chunk_size_bytes": 1710,
    "chunk_text": "The Framework Agreement covers financing for the import of essential and strategic commodities, primarily through state owned enterprises, as well as lines of financing to local banks in the Maldives to support SMEs and the private sector. The parties will also explore trade-related technical assistance and advisory services to enhance trade capacity and market access, in line with the Maldives\u2019 development agenda.\n\nITFC CEO Al-Aama said: \u201cThis new Framework Agreement builds on a partnership that has developed over many years. Through the agreement, ITFC will work with the Government and its partners to mobilise financing for essential commodities as well as support to the private sector through local financial institutions. We will continue to work with the Maldives on the trade financing priorities identified by the Government whilst exploring further cooperation in the areas of trade development.\u201d\n\nThe new agreement follows the first five-year Framework Agreement between ITFC and the Maldives, signed in 2019 and concluded in 2024, during which ITFC approved $ 1.7 billion.\n\n$ 3.3 billion in financing for the Maldives for the import of petroleum products, staple food, medicine and medical equipment, and construction materials, alongside financing for the private sector.\n\nIn addition to the signing, Eng. Adeeb Al-Aama held discussions with Maldives Minister of Finance and Public Enterprises Hassan Zareer and the Maldives Monetary Authority Governor Ahmed Munawar, on strengthening cooperation and exploring ways for further supporting the country\u2019s economic priorities. He also met with STO Managing Director and CEO Shimad Ibrahim, and other senior officials of the Government."
