    "md5": "c5db7421074e1c3b871cb20de3c033c0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1963,
    "chunk_text": "LOLC \u2018Govi Diri Danamuthu\u2019 empowers farmers\n\nPresentation of complimentary by Senior Manager SME and Personal Finance Susantha Neelawalla during the function\n\nReinforcing its commitment to supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s rural communities and agricultural entrepreneurs, LOLC Finance recently launched its islandwide agricultural awareness and farmer knowledge-sharing programme \u2018LOLC Govi Diri Danamuthu\u2019, with its inaugural session in Monaragala.\n\nThe first session brought together 55 farmers for an interactive and insightful knowledge-sharing experience, aimed at strengthening their agricultural knowledge, business capabilities and awareness, while empowering them to build more sustainable and resilient livelihoods.\n\nThe programme provided an opportunity for LOLC Finance to engage with both the existing and new customers while contributing to the development and sustainability of the local farming community in Monaragala, a district that has made a significant contribution to Sri Lanka\u2019s agricultural sector, with a strong presence of farmers and agricultural entrepreneurs.\n\nThe interactive programme focused on practical topics designed to help the farmers manage agricultural operations more effectively and build sustainable businesses.\n\nThe key areas included modern and sustainable farming practices, crop productivity and yield management, pest and disease control, efficient water and resource management, financial planning and cash flow management, entrepreneurship and business development, market awareness and value-added opportunities in agribusiness.\n\nA dedicated session also focused on preparing the farmers for the anticipated El Ni\u00f1o conditions, providing practical knowledge on managing farming activities, mitigating potential impacts and preparing for possible outcomes.\n\nThe programme was facilitated by experienced agricultural resource personnel and industry experts, together with the representatives from LOLC Finance."
