    "md5": "5c29931d2f98b5938897b7cb0195a487",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1777,
    "chunk_text": "A dedicated session also focused on preparing the farmers for the anticipated El Ni\u00f1o conditions, providing practical knowledge on managing farming activities, mitigating potential impacts and preparing for possible outcomes.\n\nThe programme was facilitated by experienced agricultural resource personnel and industry experts, together with the representatives from LOLC Finance.\n\nThe programme is expected to translate the knowledge gained into practical improvements in farmers\u2019 agricultural operations and business performance. It will encourage the adoption of new technologies and improve farming practices, supporting farm expansion, mechanisation, increase profitability and more sustainable livelihoods. These outcomes are expected to strengthen the farmers\u2019 resilience and support the long-term growth of their agricultural enterprises.\n\nParticipant farmer S.P. Chula Dhamayanthi from Monaragala said, \u201cThe Govi Diri Danamuthu programme conducted by LOLC Finance is an important initiative for us. During the programme, we gained useful knowledge from the agricultural officers on how to improve our crop yields and effectively manage diseases and infections in paddy fields.\n\nWe also learned about the challenges the farmers in Monaragala and surrounding areas are facing due to the changing weather conditions, including the changes in the rainfall patterns. The programme gave us practical knowledge that can be applied to our day-to-day farming activities. It is encouraging to see LOLC Finance supporting the farmers by not only through lending but also by providing valuable agricultural knowledge and awareness. I hope LOLC Finance will continue to conduct more programmes to support the farmers and strengthen the agricultural community in the future.\u201d"
