    "md5": "825c6cbd987d6b891ef4cb4f609ba18e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1680,
    "chunk_text": "WIM to hold Business & Leadership Night 2026 in December\n\nThe launch and announcement of the Business & Leadership Night 2026\n\nWomen-led enterprises, responsible workplaces and next-generation leadership\u00a0 will take centre stage on 9 December, as Women in Management Global (WIM) brings three flagship platforms together for WIM \u2014 The Business & Leadership Night 2026.\n\nThe evening will unite the 2nd Women MSME Awards 2026, Respectful Workplace Audit & Certification, and 2nd NextTier Mentorship & Awards 2026 to celebrate achievement, champion better workplaces and recognise the enterprises and leaders shaping Sri Lanka\u2019s business future.\n\n\u201cThe world is no longer competing on quantity alone; it is competing on value, innovation, quality, talent and the ability to think beyond borders. Sri Lanka must move with greater ambition and see itself not merely as a participant in the global economy, but as a nation capable of creating influence within it.\n\nWe have the talent, resilience, creativity and resources to compete with the world. What we need is the courage to think bigger, invest in our people, embrace technology, strengthen our businesses and turn our national strengths into global opportunities. Sri Lanka must prepare to compete, lead and make its mark \u2014 we simply cannot afford to be left behind,\u201d said Sulochana Segera, Founder/Chairperson, Women in Management (Sri Lanka, Maldives, Canada, United Kingdom, UAE & Malaysia).\n\nThe Women MSME Awards 2026 will recognise women entrepreneurs creating employment, economic value, innovation and social impact across 10 categories. Nominations are open from 20 September to 20 October 2026 via the website."
  },
