    "md5": "f0393a7a7e2579601d1f420c89a6953b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1654,
    "chunk_text": "The Women MSME Awards 2026 will recognise women entrepreneurs creating employment, economic value, innovation and social impact across 10 categories. Nominations are open from 20 September to 20 October 2026 via the website.\n\nFor the second consecutive year, NextTier will select 35 participants for direct access to the experience and perspectives of 12 local and international WIM Global mentors, providing structured mentorship to prepare them for greater leadership responsibilities.\n\nThe WIM Leadership Awards Night will also honour three outstanding business leaders whose influence extends beyond their organisations, creating meaningful impact across Sri Lanka\u2019s economy, industries and society.\n\nAdding an international dimension will be Deena Tissera, Labour Councillor of Aberdeen City Council for Hilton, Woodside & Stockethill. She will be joined by Lushani Kodituwakku, Commercial Due Diligence Expert, United Kingdom and WIM Top50 Global Award Winner 2025.\n\nThe three platforms will be guided by experienced business and leadership professionals. Dr. Nirmal De Silva, Group Director, RNH Ventures, will chair the Respectful Workplace Audit & Certification; Dr. Rohantha Athukorala, Vice Chairman \u2013 Asia Pacific, World Rural Tourism Council, will chair the NextTier Mentorship & Awards; and Prashantha Mahadevan, Director, Dazzle (Pvt) Ltd, will chair the Women MSME Awards 2026.\n\nFazeela Dharamaratne will serve as WIM Leadership Night Event Chair. The Awards Chairs are Anjali Goonetilake for the Respectful Workplace Awards, Arunnia Vimalendren for the NextTier Leadership Awards, and Dilsha Ruwanpathirana for the Women MSME Awards."
  },
