    "language": "en",
    "md5": "eac9ca1606b7044fd4727ac3883a6e5f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1815,
    "chunk_text": "Sampath Bank named \u2018Best Bank for Corporate Responsibility\u2019 at Euromoney Awards\n\nFrom left: Allan Wu, MC for the Event; Dr. Lalith Weragoda - Chief Transformation Officer, Sampath Bank PLC; Nuwan Pathirana - Head of Sustainability, Sampath Bank PLC; David Byrne - Head of Asia, Euromoney and Ajantha de Vas Gunasekara - Executive Director/Chief Financial Officer, Sampath Bank PLC\n\nSampath Bank PLC has been recognised as Sri Lanka\u2019s Best Bank for Corporate Responsibility at the Euromoney Awards for Excellence 2026.\n\nThe award was presented at the Asia-Pacific regional awards ceremony held in Singapore recently.\n\nSanjaya Gunawardana, Managing Director and Chief Executive Officer of Sampath Bank said, \u201cThis recognition is a tremendous source of pride for Sampath Bank and for Team Sampath. It reflects our belief that corporate responsibility must create meaningful, measurable and lasting value for communities, while strengthening the resilience of the country we serve.\n\n\u2018Wewata Jeewayak\u2019 demonstrates how environmental restoration can be connected to community resilience, food security, economic opportunity as well as climate adaptation. The recognition from Euromoney reinforces our commitment to advancing this integrated approach and creating measurable impact that extends well beyond the projects themselves.\u201d\n\nThe \u2018Wewata Jeewayak\u2019 programme reached a new scale in 2025, with Rs. 63.7 million (approximately USD 190,000) invested in 11 new tank restoration projects, benefiting 14,780 people and rejuvenating 3,370 acres of paddy land. The initiative forms part of Sampath Bank\u2019s broader efforts to strengthen climate resilience and rural development by restoring neglected irrigation tanks that serve as critical water infrastructure for Sri Lanka\u2019s agricultural communities."
  },
