    "md5": "8334c39cd873030ba79054b18156eddc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1896,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cTraditionally, Sri Lankan investors have favoured conventional investment avenues, but it has yielded comparatively fewer returns than the capital market,\u201d remarked Executive Vice President \u2013 Marketing, CSE,\u00a0 Niroshan Wijesundera, speaking on the Unit Trust and Stockbrokering firm outreach objectives of the broad-basing initiative.\n\nSpeaking on the favourable investment climate, he noted that the Sri Lankan capital market is at a relatively low Price-to-Earnings (P/E) ratio of 11.03x in a global context.\n\nOver the past six years the All-Share Price Index (ASPI) has increased from 5,320 points in August 2020 to 21,315 points by the end of August 2026, representing a growth of 300 percent and a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of around 26 percent.\n\nThe Investor Forums began with presentations by representatives of leading stockbroking firms. Speakers, including A. Visaahan, Vice President - Research at Asha Securities (Pvt) Ltd, and Dilina Kulatunga, Head of Research at Capital Trust Securities (Pvt) Ltd, provided an introductory presentation on the capital market and a comprehensive overview of the current market outlook for prospective investors in Jaffna and Anuradhapura, respectively.\n\nParticipants also had the opportunity to hear directly from unit trust management companies about investing in equity funds and the benefits they offer. These insights were provided through presentations by Kumudu Kekirideniya, Manager - Business Development at Softlogic Asset Management (Pvt) Ltd, and Thillainadarajah Luxchan, Senior Manager at NDB Wealth (Pvt) Ltd, who delivered their presentations in Anuradhapura and Jaffna.\n\nBoth forums concluded with a panel discussion and Q&A session. During the investor forums, prospective investors had the opportunity to meet representatives from stockbroking firms and unit trust management companies to open investment accounts."
