    "chunk_text": "Mixed secondary market sentiment, with buying edging ahead\n\nSecondary market activity remained mixed yesterday, with both buying and selling interest observed throughout the session.\n\nHowever, buying activity was marginally stronger, resulting in a slight downward movement in the belly of the yield curve. Moderate volumes were recorded during the day, although overall market activity remained relatively subdued.\n\nAmong the traded maturities, in the short-tenor segment, both the 15.10.2028 and 15.12.2028 maturities traded within the range of 10.90%-10.75%, while the 15.09.2029 maturity traded at 11.05%.\n\nIn the 2030 segment, the 01.08.2030 and 15.10.2030 maturities traded between 11.45% to 11.35%. Further along the curve, the 01.02.2031 maturity traded within a range of 11.65% -11.40%.\n\nAt the longer end, the 15.12.2032 maturity traded between 11.80% and 11.70%, while the 01.11.2033 maturity traded between 12.00% and 11.95%. Finally, the 15.09.2034 maturity traded within a range of 12.20%-12.17%.\n\nOn the external front, the LKR depreciated against the USD, standing at LKR 331.89/USD, compared to LKR 330.18/USD seen earlier.\n\nMarket liquidity in the banking system contracted\u00a0 \u00a0317.84 bn compared to LKR 336.44bn recorded previously."
