    "chunk_text": "Since opening its doors, Am\u00e3na Bank has steadily expanded its presence across the country, serving a growing customer base through its 80+ branch and self-banking centre network while remaining focused on Retail, SME, and development-oriented banking with a selective approach to Corporates. The Bank\u2019s asset-backed banking model continues to channel financing towards productive sectors of the economy, supporting entrepreneurs, households, and businesses in a manner aligned with its values and customer-centric promise.\n\nManaging Director & CEO of Am\u00e3na Bank PLC Mohammed Azmeer, also speaking at the occasion, remarked \u201cWe are thankful to the Colombo Stock Exchange for honouring Am\u00e3na Bank 15-year journey through today\u2019s ceremonial market opening. Today is not only a celebration of fifteen years, but also an opportunity to reflect on how far Am\u00e3na Bank has progressed as a listed financial institution and to look ahead with renewed confidence to the next chapter of our journey. As we look ahead, our focus remains on further strengthening the Bank, creating sustainable value for our shareholders, supporting the country\u2019s economic development, and continuing to deliver on our promise of Development Focused, People Friendly Banking.\u201d\n\nAddressing the gathering, Nilupa Perera, Chief Regulatory Officer of the Colombo Stock Exchange, congratulated Am\u00e3na Bank PLC on the milestone, remarking \u201cAmana Bank\u2019s first fifteen years have been defined by vision and progress, and we look forward to seeing the Bank continue to expand its impact in the years ahead.\u201d\n\nOver the years Amana Bank has received numerous accolades, namely \u2018Best Up-and-Coming Islamic Bank in the World\u2019 by Global Finance Magazine USA during its formative years, being ranked among the \u2018World\u2019s Top 50 Strongest Islamic Banks\u2019 by The Asian Banker and selected as the \u2018Most Impactful ICD Investee Company\u2019 by the Islamic Development Bank Group."
