    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "f3b105819117e3a716a802d2bb4ad2bd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1886,
    "chunk_text": "Former envoy urges govt. to conclude US trade pact to lock in 10% tariff\n\nFormer Ambassador Mahinda Samarasinghe says around 90% of the text of the Sri Lanka-US trade agreement has been agreed, although domestic legal processes must still be completed before it is signed and implemented\n\nAlmost every country that has finalised an agreement with Washington has had to offer complete or near-complete duty-free access for American exports, he pointed out\n\nSri Lanka would like a clause similar to one secured by Bangladesh, which offers a zero-rated quota in return for sourcing raw materials such as cotton and fibre from the US\n\nSri Lanka must conclude its pending trade agreement with the United States in order to lock in the favourable 10 percent tariff rate it currently enjoys, according to former Sri Lankan Ambassador to the United States Mahinda Samarasinghe.\n\nDelivering the keynote address at the 25th anniversary celebrations of the Sri Lanka Institute of Directors (SLiD) in Colombo this week, Samarasinghe, who recently concluded his assignment in Washington, revealed that negotiations were in their final stages, with around 90 percent of the agreement\u2019s content already finalised.\n\nAgreeing on the content in principle is only one step, he explained, as domestic processes are needed to give the agreement legal effect before it can be signed and implemented.\n\n\u201cWhat I have recommended very strongly to the government before I left was that we need to conclude the agreement so that we can lock in the very favourable tariff rate that Sri Lanka has got up to now,\u201d he said.\n\n\u201cThe government is committed to sorting out whatever differences that are there to give and take and come to that agreement so that there is some guarantee that can be given to domestic exporters that that market opportunity is available not only today but moving forward,\u201d he added."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-18-dailymirrorlk-117ab699",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-117ab699",
