    "chunk_size_bytes": 1450,
    "chunk_text": "Severe lightning advisory issued for Uva, Eastern Provinces and two districts\n\nColombo, September 18 (Daily Mirror) - The Natural Hazards Early Warning Centre has issued an advisory warning of severe lightning activity in several areas, valid until 11.30 p.m. today (18).\n\nAccording to the advisory issued at 11.00 a.m., thundershowers accompanied by severe lightning are likely at several places in the Uva and Eastern provinces and in the Mullaittivu and Polonnaruwa districts.\n\nTemporary localised strong winds may also occur during thundershowers, the Department of Meteorology warned.\n\nThe public has been urged to take adequate precautions to minimise possible damage caused by lightning activity.\n\nThe Department advised the public to seek shelter, preferably indoors, and avoid taking shelter under trees during thunderstorms.\n\nPeople were also advised to avoid open areas such as paddy fields, tea plantations and open water bodies while thunderstorms are occurring.\n\nThe public has been cautioned against using wired telephones and electrical appliances connected to power outlets during thunderstorms.\n\nPeople should also avoid travelling in open vehicles such as bicycles, tractors and boats during thunderstorms.\n\nThe Department further urged the public to be cautious of fallen trees and power lines following thunderstorms.\n\nThose requiring emergency assistance have been advised to contact their local disaster management authorities."
