    "chunk_text": "Nimal Perera should be treated as accomplice if bribe money went to his account \u2013 Defence counsel argued\n\nColombo, Sep. 19 (Daily Mirror) - \u201cIf the alleged bribe money had been credited to Nimal Perera\u2019s account, he too should be treated as an accomplice,\u201d defence counsel told court while making submissions on behalf of Parliamentarian Namal Rajapaksa.\n\nDeputy Solicitor General Janaka Bandara told court that the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption had sought the Attorney General\u2019s advice regarding the investigations into the alleged offence.\n\nMaking submissions, Deputy Solicitor General said a statement had been recorded from the former Speaker of Parliament regarding a SriLankan Airlines board meeting allegedly held at the Speaker\u2019s official residence and concerning his son, Shashindra Rajapaksa, the third suspect in the case, who is currently overseas.\n\nHe said statements had also been recorded from several other individuals, including Susanta Chaminda Ratnayake and Dimuthu Sanjaya.\n\nThe Deputy Solicitor General further informed court that the suspect had been produced before the Colombo Fort Magistrate\u2019s Court last Wednesday and that the Fort Magistrate had remanded him till September 23.\n\nThe first suspect in the case, Kapila Chandrasena, has since died, while the second suspect, Priyanka Neomali Wijenayake, is said to have fled to Australia. The third suspect, Shashindra Rajapaksa, is said to have fled to the United States.\n\nDeputy Solicitor General Bandara said the investigation was being conducted jointly by CIABOC and the Criminal Investigation Department (CID).\n\nHe further said the CID had forwarded the extracts of its investigations relating to the incident to the Attorney General.\n\nHe added that under Section 69 of the Anti-Corruption Act, CIABOC has the statutory power to seek the Attorney General\u2019s advice regarding investigations."
