    "chunk_text": "Making submissions, President\u2019s Counsel Shavindra Fernando said an international investigation had been conducted into the Airbus transaction and that the suspect\u2019s name did not appear in any of the relevant reports.\n\nHe also said the suspect\u2019s name was not mentioned in the report of the commission appointed by former President Maithripala Sirisena to investigate the matter.\n\nHe claimed that Perera had, on one occasion, stated that the money had not been credited to his account and that the CID had also made observations in B reports at one stage alleging that he had made false statements.\n\nThe President\u2019s Counsel further submitted that if the alleged bribe money had been credited to Perera\u2019s account, he too should be treated as an accomplice to the alleged offence.\n\n\u201cMy client has received an invitation from the Government of India to undertake a visit. The visit is scheduled to take place from September 27 to October 1. The invitation has been extended by the Government of India. I request Your Honour to take that also into consideration,\" he said.\n\nHowever sources told the Daily Mirror that the invitation was extended from the Indian Opposition Leader's office and not the Indian government and it was extended long before Namal's arrest.\n\n\"Further, my client has been invited by the chief incumbent of the Pothgul Viharaya in Hanguranketha to participate in the placing of the pinnacle of the temple on September 26. This is another historic procession held after the Dalada Perahera. If my client fails to participate in it, it should also be considered as an act of disrespect towards the chief incumbent of the temple.\u201d\n\nHe requested court to consider these circumstances as exceptional circumstances and release the suspect on bail subject to appropriate conditions.\n\nCiting the judgement delivered by Supreme Court Justice Janak de Silva in SC/Contempt/3, 4 and 5/2025, Deputy Solicitor General Janaka Bandara raised an objection and read out a portion of the judgement."
