    "chunk_size_bytes": 2012,
    "chunk_text": "I cannot take over the nation now as I am not in Parliament: Ranil\n\nColombo, Sep. 19 (Daily Mirror) - Former President Ranil Wickremesinghe on Thursday said that he cannot take over the nation now if needed, as he is not in Parliament now.\n\nMr Wickremesinghe made this remark in response to a question raised by a youth as to whether he is prepared to take over the nation once again. Questions were raised by the youth from the former President during a programme to mark the 120th birth anniversary of the late President J. R. Jayewardene in Colombo.\n\n\u201cI cannot take over the nation now as I am not in Parliament,\u201d Mr Wickremesinghe said.\n\n\u201cYouth should be prepared to take leadership. I don\u2019t know how Gen Z thinks of politics. The thinking pattern of my generation will not help the country now. It is the young generation which have to think about the future of the nation. Sri Lanka will be celebrating 100 years of independence in a few years. The new generation will have to decide where the nation should be and what the nation should achieve during that time,\u201d he told the youth in response to their questions. He said this in response to a question as to what the youth could aim at when it comes to development of the nation.\n\nHe reiterated that the country is heading for an economic downturn once again. \u201cPeople had to spend their savings during the years 2022 and 2023. They had to spend the money they had hidden under their mattresses. Their savings are gone today. Inflation has increased. One has to sell the mattress you sleep on to survive today,\u201d he said, responding to a question on the present situation.\n\n\u201cIf no one accepted the responsibility of running the country during the \u2018Aragalaya\u2019 in 2022, the future of the nation would have been bleak. We knew that the country could be re-stabilised. Therefore, we took over the responsibility without fear,\u201d he also said in response to a question about his thoughts on the decision to take over the nation back in 2022."
