    "chunk_size_bytes": 1471,
    "chunk_text": "Agarkar\u2019s current contract is set to expire on October 4, with the board also looking to fill five vacancies on the junior selection committee.\n\n\u201cThe office-bearers have been authorised to take decisions on matters concerning the selection committees,\u201d a senior BCCI official said after the meeting.\n\nMeanwhile, the Mumbai Cricket Association requested consideration for hosting prominent matches, while Jharkhand State Cricket Association secretary Saurabh Tiwary denied any knowledge of reports suggesting that an India-Australia Test would be moved away from Ranchi.\n\nUEFA President Aleksander Ceferin and CONCACAF President Victor Montagliani have called for an independent review of FIFA\u2019s financial reserves and proposed a $2.1 billion payout to its 211 member associations.\n\nIn a letter to FIFA President Gianni Infantino, the two FIFA vice-presidents proposed making at least $10 million available to each association during the 2027\u201330 cycle, in addition to existing FIFA Forward Programme funding.\n\nThey said FIFA was on course to end the 2023\u201326 cycle with reserves of around $6 billion, raising questions about the need for the abandoned FIFA Forward Enterprise project, which sought investment from outside parties.\n\nCeferin and Montagliani said an independent review should assess FIFA\u2019s financial position and determine how much additional funding could be distributed. They also proposed considering a similar payout for the 2031\u201334 cycle."
