    "md5": "b5a2264d0437323135683658d7c1770f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1771,
    "chunk_text": "INTERPOL notice issued for Basil Rajapaksa\n\nColombo, Sep. 19 (Daily Mirror) - INTERPOL has issued a blue notice on former minister Basil Rajapaksa following a request by the Criminal Investigations Department as authorities step up efforts to trace and bring back individuals wanted in connection with ongoing legal proceedings, Public Security Minister Ananda Wijepala told the Daily Mirror.\n\nMinister Wijepala said the government is using international law enforcement mechanisms to track down former politicians and other wanted individuals who are residing overseas while facing legal proceedings in Sri Lanka.\n\nBasil Rajapaksa is currently facing court proceedings in Sri Lanka and has failed to appear before court on several occasions. The Matara Chief Magistrate\u2019s Court reissued an arrest warrant in July against him after he failed to appear in connection with a case involving the alleged purchase of a 1.5-acre property at Brown\u2019s Hill, Eliyakanda Road, Matara, for Rs.60 million.\n\nThe minister said that a Blue Notice had already been issued in respect of Basil Rajapaksa, enabling international law enforcement authorities to obtain information concerning his identity, location or activities in connection with the relevant criminal investigations.\n\nThe case was filed by the Police Financial Crimes Investigation Division and named several other accused. Basil\u2019s lawyers had previously informed court that he was overseas receiving medical treatment, while the court ordered that the arrest warrant be enforced after considering his repeated absence.\n\nAn Interpol Blue Notice is an international alert used by law enforcement to collect extra information about a person's identity, location, or activities in connection with a criminal investigation"
  },
