    "md5": "8d63b11e8bc9d38ec0d651ebfb185e92",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2011,
    "chunk_text": "Christell shines a spotlight on longevity\n\nFrom left: Christell Luxury Wellness Metabolic Lab Head Dr. R. Hiruni Poornima, CEO & Anti-Aging and Regenerative Medicine Specialist Dr. Shanika Arsecularatne and Hair Restoration Specialist Dr. Nilaharan Robinson\n\nChristell Luxury Wellness hosted \u2018Age Gracefully\u2019, an exclusive evening bringing longevity, preventive health, regenerative medicine, beauty and wellness into the spotlight.\n\nHeld at The Shoppes at City of Dreams, the event brought together distinguished guests, industry leaders and luxury wellness partners around a critical question that frames our everyday lives: How can we live longer, healthier and better?\n\nAt the heart of the evening was an overview of longevity and preventive health led by Dr. Shanika Arsecularatne, CEO & Anti-Aging and Regenerative Medicine Specialist of Christell Luxury Wellness. The event focused on the concept of longevity through a luxury wellness experience, encouraging people to focus on their long-term health through awareness, preventive measures, health optimization and a proactive mindset to ageing.\n\nWhile the global conversation around longevity is rapidly growing, Christell\u2019s emphasis on longevity and preventive health has been built for over 30 years.\n\nChristell has continuously evolved with advances in science, technology and regenerative medicine.\n\nAge Gracefully represents the next chapter of that journey \u2014 advancing beyond looking good to living healthier and ageing better.\n\nGuests experienced this philosophy through interactive health and wellness experiences, including a \u2018Check Your Health Status\u2019 quiz, Vitamin Level Test demonstration and Hair Scan demonstration, alongside luxury beauty, fragrance and wellness experiences by Exclusive Lines, Zam Gems and Dilmah.\n\nThe evening highlighted an important shift in modern lifestyle that has become prevalent around the world: prevention begins long before illness strikes, and good health and longevity are closely intertwined."
