    "chunk_size_bytes": 1384,
    "chunk_text": "Discussions were supported by expert presentations, facilitated roundtables and networking sessions, including contributions from the Asian Development Bank on Sri Lanka\u2019s evolving skills ecosystem and opportunities for international collaboration.\n\n\u201cWe are confident that the \u2018Applied Learning and Industry Connect\u2019 initiative will enable New Zealand and Sri Lanka to work together to develop talent, strengthen innovation, and create lasting value for both our countries.\u201d Discussions at the event identified opportunities for institutional collaboration, knowledge exchange and co-designed partnership models that can deliver practical outcomes for education providers, employers and learners in both countries.\n\nEarlier this year, ENZ delivered the first-ever Study with New Zealand Roadshow in Sri Lanka, reflecting its commitment to strengthening the long-standing education relationship between the two countries.\n\nBy combining New Zealand\u2019s expertise in applied learning with Sri Lanka\u2019s ambitions for education reform and economic transformation, both countries have an opportunity to develop innovative education partnerships that benefit learners, institutions and industry.\n\nThe successful conclusion of the Applied Learning and Industry Connect event marks another important milestone in the evolving education partnership between New Zealand and Sri Lanka."
