    "chunk_text": "AOD launches Young Creatives Programme for students with special needs\n\nFrom left: Creative Lead Maria Perez, AOD Founder and Chairperson Linda Speldewinde, Neurodiversity and Inclusive Education Adviser to AOD Zara Esufally and Internal Programme Lead Ashanthi Handunge\n\nAOD has announced the launch of the Young Creatives Programme for students with special needs, a two-year supported education programme that opens the academy\u2019s creative teaching, studios and wider community to young people aged 13 and above who learn differently.\n\nThe programme welcomes students with additional learning and support needs who demonstrate an interest in art, making or design.\n\nStudents attend the AOD campus three days a week and learn through practical art, craft and design activities, supported by a dedicated team and taught at a pace suited to each individual.\n\nAlongside the creative curriculum, the students may also follow English and mathematics tuition, working towards London O-Level examinations where this is appropriate for them.\n\nWhat sets the programme apart is its refusal to define success in a single way. Every student is understood as an individual rather than by a diagnosis, with a personal learning plan developed around their strengths, interests and needs.\n\nSome students will use the two years as a stepping stone into AOD\u2019s Foundation programme and in time, a BA (Hons) degree. Others will complete the programme with practical creative skills, a portfolio of their own work and greater confidence and independence to carry forward. Both journeys are recognised as equally worthwhile.\n\n\u201cInclusion has always been part of AOD\u2019s belief in the transformative power of creativity,\u201d said AOD Founder and Chairperson Linda Speldewinde."
  },
