    "chunk_text": "Some students will use the two years as a stepping stone into AOD\u2019s Foundation programme and in time, a BA (Hons) degree. Others will complete the programme with practical creative skills, a portfolio of their own work and greater confidence and independence to carry forward. Both journeys are recognised as equally worthwhile.\n\n\u201cInclusion has always been part of AOD\u2019s belief in the transformative power of creativity,\u201d said AOD Founder and Chairperson Linda Speldewinde.\n\nThe students will explore drawing, painting, craft, sculpture, textiles, digital creativity and more, while being introduced to the design disciplines for which AOD is known, from fashion and graphic design to photography and spatial design. Throughout the programme, they will build a portfolio and learn how to discuss and present their work.\n\nA distinctive feature of the programme is the involvement of current AOD BA (Hons) students, who will serve as Young Creatives mentors. Working alongside teachers, learning support staff and counsellors, these mentors will provide participants with relatable creative role models while embedding inclusion within the everyday life of the academy, rather than treating it as a separate activity.\n\n\u201cOur starting point is always the individual, never the label,\u201d said Young Creatives Programme Creative Lead Maria Perez.\n\n\u201cWhen learning is built around what a young person can do and what they love to do, remarkable things can follow. This programme gives every student the space to discover that for themselves.\u201d\n\nThe students will have opportunities to showcase their work through Young Creatives Exhibitions at AOD, while those who complete the two-year programme will be recognised at a dedicated graduation."
