    "md5": "265db382da6ca03c54c7daa22b67aaf0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1906,
    "chunk_text": "Vidullanka enters grid-scale energy storage with 1st of 13 BESS facilities\n\nVidullanka PLC, in partnership with WindForce PLC, will inaugurate its first of 13 standalone battery energy storage system (BESS) facilities today in Anuradhapura, in a ceremony marking a landmark achievement for the company and Sri Lanka\u2019s renewable energy industry.\n\nThe occasion will be graced by the presence of President Anura Kumara Dissanayake and Energy Minister Anura Karunathilaka.\n\nThe 10MW/40MWh facility was developed under the project company StoreX (Pvt.) Ltd, which will develop 11 more BESS projects across the island as part of Sri Lanka\u2019s first grid-scale standalone BESS initiative.\n\nVidullanka and WindForce have also partnered to develop a 13th project in Vavunathivu, under the project company Solar Universe (Pvt.) Ltd.\n\nTogether, these 13 projects will have a combined capacity of 130MW/520MWh, extending Vidullanka\u2019s footprint into grid-scale energy storage and positioning the company as a key player in shaping the next phase of Sri Lanka\u2019s energy transition.\n\nThe inaugurated facility marks Vidullanka\u2019s expansion beyond electricity generation, adding energy storage as a new dimension to its diversified portfolio.\n\nThe company is also set to commission its eighth ground-mounted solar facility in Hambantota, bringing its total capacity to 96 MW and its portfolio to 27 projects.\n\nVidullanka is a leading renewable energy company with a diversified portfolio built over the course of nearly three decades since its incorporation in 1997.\n\nThe company operates its own hydro, solar and dendro assets in Sri Lanka and Uganda and offers services in several key areas including operations and maintenance, engineering, procurement and construction and more.\n\nAlongside its entry into grid-scale energy storage, the company has also ventured into e-mobility with its EV charging brand VEDRIVE."
  },
