    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka can leapfrog into agentic AI era: Salesforce South Asia CEO\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s comparatively lower level of digital activity gives its businesses an opportunity to leapfrog into agentic artificial intelligence (AI) and become globally competitive, Salesforce South Asia President and CEO Arundhati Bhattacharya said at a virtual press conference held yesterday.\n\nResponding to media queries, Bhattacharya noted that Salesforce has been engaging regularly with the local clients to demonstrate the value of becoming an Agentic Enterprise, a model in which the AI agents orchestrate workflows alongside human employees, with a human retained in the loop to validate the outcomes.\n\n\u201cWhile Sri Lanka may not yet have become as digitally active as some other markets, I believe this gives the country an opportunity to leapfrog,\u201d she remarked, cautioning that she did not believe the businesses could remain relevant over the long term without a strong technology backbone.\n\nShe added that Salesforce was keen to bring its latest technologies into Sri Lanka and ensure that the local enterprises have equal opportunities to deploy them, surfacing the latent demand that is not yet sufficiently visible for the companies to capitalise on.\n\nPointing to early traction in the market, Bhattacharya revealed that Salesforce\u2019s first Innovation Day in Colombo, held on August 31, had been planned for around 400 participants but drew approximately 800 registrations, double the target, with some 600 professionals attending, 50 percent above the planned audience.\n\n\u201cSo, there is clearly a huge amount of curiosity and interest among the businesses in ensuring that they are not left behind and that they too move towards becoming Agentic Enterprises,\u201d she observed."
  },
