    "md5": "92f824c3c2b925118bd02d6d758dc86c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1843,
    "chunk_text": "The ceasefire collapsed in July when Saudi\u2011backed Yemeni government forces bombed the Sanaa airport, preventing an Iranian civilian aircraft from bringing home a top Houthi delegation, after they attended the funeral of Iranian leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei. The Houthis hit back at Saudi Arabia. The war broke out. Nations panicked when the Houthis, in a lightning advance, captured Bab al\u2011Mandab and continued to gain battlefield victories.\n\nThe Houthis matched each Saudi bombing campaign with attacks on Saudi oil and military facilities. Drones from Houthi allies in Iraq hit Saudi Arabia\u2019s crucial East\u2011West pipeline. The attack halted 4 per cent of global oil supplies. Moreover, with the Bab al\u2011Mandab closed for the Saudi ships and the Strait of Hormuz remaining virtually closed, Saudi oil can reach the Asian market only through the Suez Canal or through tanker-to-tanker transfer in Oman.\n\nAmidst these disruptions to global fuel supplies, the Saudis claimed they shot down a drone over the holy city of Mecca and blamed the Houthis. The news sent shockwaves across the Muslim world. The Houthis denied the reports, which they said were aimed at portraying them as enemies of Islam. Pakistan, which had recently signed a tripartite defence deal with Saudi Arabia and T\u00fcrkiye, reacted to these reports by issuing a severe warning to the Houthis.\n\nThe reports sparked a social media war, with pro\u2011Saudi accounts likening the Houthis to Abraha\u2019s elephant army, destroyed by God in the year the Prophet Muhammad was born when it sought to demolish the Ka\u2019ba. Pro\u2011Houthi voices challenged the Saudi Wahhabis\u2019 claim to Mecca, branding them invaders who erased its heritage and built toilets over the Prophet\u2019s companions\u2019 homes.\n\nSaudi Arabia has left with only two options\u2014escalate the Yemen war or ceasefire."
