    "md5": "299c7a1ab2e5931366e4e4ceea8b618d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1518,
    "chunk_text": "Rs. 1.5bn allocated to make dangerous roads safer\n\nColombo, Sep.19 (Daily Mirror) - The Government has allocated Rs. 1.5 billion to identify and make safe unsafe and dangerous locations on roads outside the national road network, Transport, Highways and Urban Development Minister Bimal Ratnayake said.\n\nUnder the programme, Rs. 60 million will be allocated to each district, with local government institutions responsible for identifying dangerous locations and carrying out necessary safety improvements.\n\nMemorandums of Understanding (MoUs) were signed with chairmen and mayors of relevant local government institutions on September 18 to implement the programme.\n\nThe Minister said the Cabinet had approved the programme in June following a Cabinet memorandum submitted on May 20.\n\nThe National Council on Road Safety has been assigned responsibility for providing technical guidance and monitoring progress in collaboration with local government institutions.\n\nSpeaking at the event, Minister Ratnayake said road safety could not be improved through laws and public awareness campaigns alone.\n\n\u201cRoad accidents cannot be reduced by enacting laws or educating the public alone. The physical unsafe conditions on the roads that cause accidents must also be changed,\u201d he said.\n\nHe said road accidents caused not only loss of life but also significant economic and social costs, making road safety a national priority.\n\nThe MoUs will remain in effect until December 31, 2026, subject to their terms and conditions."
