    "md5": "9f91cf3a78923c9c824aa54a16c4fe60",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1638,
    "chunk_text": "England sweep Sri Lanka 3-0 to reclaim No. 1 T20I ranking\n\nSEP.19 (Mirror Sports) - England crushed Sri Lanka by eight wickets in the third T20I at Old Trafford to complete a 3-0 series sweep and reclaim the top spot in the men\u2019s T20 international rankings.\n\nEngland\u2019s bowlers restricted Sri Lanka to 124 all out in 18.5 overs before the hosts raced to 126-2 in just 9.4 overs, sealing victory with 62 balls to spare.\n\nJamie Overton led the bowling effort with an economical spell of 1-15 from four overs, while Sonny Baker continued his impressive progress with figures of 2-17. Jofra Archer also claimed two wickets for 23 runs, while Will Jacks finished with 2-31.\n\nPathum Nissanka top-scored for Sri Lanka with 36 off 24 balls, while Kamindu Mendis contributed 35 off 28 deliveries. However, England\u2019s disciplined bowling and sharp fielding kept the visitors under pressure throughout their innings.\n\nJos Buttler powered England\u2019s chase with an unbeaten 62 off 32 balls, while Harry Brook added 33 from 21 deliveries. The pair shared an 85-run second-wicket partnership after Aneurin Donald fell for 13.\n\nBrook was run out before Buttler sealed the victory in style with a six, completing a dominant win for the hosts.\n\nThe victory marked England\u2019s 23rd win in 26 completed T20 internationals since Brook took charge in 2024. The clean sweep also saw England move ahead of India to return to No. 1 in the world rankings.\n\nEngland will now turn their attention to the three-match ODI series against Sri Lanka, which begins in Durham on Tuesday, as they continue preparations for the 2027 Cricket World Cup in southern Africa."
  },
