    "md5": "fb023c05cde0b0b318e17a73b007a420",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1842,
    "chunk_text": "Fairway takes Trincomalee Beach Resort four-star under long-term mgt. deal\n\nFrom left: General Manager of Fairway Colombo Avinga Wanigasekara; Chairman of Fairway Holdings Virath De Alwis; Owner of the Trincomalee Beach Resort & Spa (PVT LTD) Kumar Jeyakumaran; Chief Operations Officer of Fairway Leisure Gemunu Cooray; Chief Executive Officer of Fairway Leisure Sector Basheer Cader\n\nTrincomalee Beach Resort & Spa will be rebranded as Fairway Trinco and upgraded to a four-star standard under a long-term management agreement with Fairway Holdings, a deal that deepens the real estate developer\u2019s push into hospitality and hands it a beachfront foothold on the island\u2019s fast-growing east coast.\n\nThe agreement between Trincomalee Beach Resort & Spa (Pvt) Ltd and the conglomerate\u2019s leisure arm was signed at Fairway Colombo on Friday (18). The partners aim to position the property among Sri Lanka\u2019s leading coastal resorts while strengthening Trincomalee\u2019s standing as one of the country\u2019s fastest-growing tourism destinations.\n\nThe resort is owned by Kumar Jeyakumaran, Chairman of Platinum Group of Companies. His interests extend into travel through Platinum Travel Networks Sri Lanka, a business that has been courting travel agency partners in India, Malaysia and Singapore for pilgrimage tour programmes.\n\n\u201cThis partnership represents far more than a management agreement. It is a commitment to the future of Trincomalee\u2019s tourism industry,\u201d Jeyakumaran stated. He expressed confidence that the collaboration would bring economic benefits to the Eastern Province, create employment and encourage further investment into the region.\n\nThe 46-room resort sits on the beachfront along the boardwalk, with an outdoor pool, a children\u2019s pool, a beach bar, spa facilities and a conference centre with two meeting rooms."
  },
  {
