    "chunk_size_bytes": 1531,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cIt is between the organisations handing over their judgment to technology and those strengthening it. Our technical agenda gives the HR leaders practical tools, from governance frameworks to reskilling. If delegates leave with the confidence to say no to a machine when it matters, we have done our job,\u201d he added.\n\nInsights from Mercer will ground the discussion in data, while the HR Heads Forum and Business Leaders Forum will address Sri Lanka\u2019s market realities, talent flows and costs.\n\nThe event also features The Great HR Debate 2026, chaired by Shanaka Fernando and held in collaboration with Toastmasters International District 82, with the British Council as Official Training and Assessment Partner. Fourteen corporate teams have been competing since August 11.\n\nNational HR Exhibition 2026, led by Davina Kern, will showcase industry innovations.\n\nCIPM CEO U.A.C. Obeyesekere thanked the organisations supporting the conference, including Lead Event Partner Hatton National Bank and Strategic Partners Layup (e-learning), BIPO (technology) and Wijeya Newspapers (print media).\n\nOfficial Partners are British Council (training and assessment), Jobdaddy.lk (hiring), Thyaga.lk (gifts and rewards), Asiri Hospital Holdings (healthcare), Brandix (global apparel solutions), PickMe (mobility) and Monarch Imperial (hospitality). Omega Line, Seylan Bank and David Peiris Motors are Co-Sponsors.\n\nRegistrations will open shortly and delegates, sponsors and partner organisations may contact CIPM Sri Lanka for details."
