    "language": "en",
    "md5": "d61018dcd448097f9f2c3e232eb16735",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1691,
    "chunk_text": "Softlogic to bring Wow! Momo, Tiong Bahru Bakery and Mad Over Donuts to Sri Lanka\n\nSoftlogic restructures Rs. 59.8bn of loans, with Rs. 18.1bn due in 2026/27\n\nGroup still seeks buyers for its hotels, while ODEL Mall needs Rs. 6.1bn to complete\n\nAshok Pathirage-controlled\u00a0 Softlogic Holdings PLC plans to open three new international restaurant franchises in Sri Lanka by January, including India\u2019s Wow! Momo and Singapore\u2019s Tiong Bahru Bakery, as the debt-laden conglomerate works to convert a strong operating recovery into sustainable profits.\n\nThe group disclosed the plans in its annual report for 2025/26, in which it posted a marginal pre-tax profit of Rs. 24 million, compared with a pre-tax loss of Rs. 7.49 billion a year earlier. However, Softlogic still recorded a loss of Rs. 8.63 billion attributable to shareholders for the year ended 31 March 2026.\n\nAccording to the report, the restaurant business will introduce Tiong Bahru Bakery, the Singaporean artisan bakery and caf\u00e9, along with India\u2019s Wow! Momo and doughnut chain Mad Over Donuts.\n\nSpeaking to Mirror Business, Softlogic Chairman and Managing Director Ashok Pathirage revealed that Tiong Bahru Bakery will open at Arcade Independence Square, which is managed by the group, with a target launch in December or January. He added that Mad Over Donuts and Wow! Momo are expected to open around January at One Galle Face Mall. Founded in 2012, Tiong Bahru Bakery is known for its French-inspired handmade pastries and croissants, and operates around 20 outlets in Singapore. The brand made its international debut\u00a0 last year, opening its first overseas outlet in Manila through the Philippines\u2019 Jollibee Group."
