    "chunk_text": "Speaking to Mirror Business, Softlogic Chairman and Managing Director Ashok Pathirage revealed that Tiong Bahru Bakery will open at Arcade Independence Square, which is managed by the group, with a target launch in December or January. He added that Mad Over Donuts and Wow! Momo are expected to open around January at One Galle Face Mall. Founded in 2012, Tiong Bahru Bakery is known for its French-inspired handmade pastries and croissants, and operates around 20 outlets in Singapore. The brand made its international debut\u00a0 last year, opening its first overseas outlet in Manila through the Philippines\u2019 Jollibee Group.\n\nGroup revenue rose 24 percent to Rs. 129 billion during the year, while EBITDA grew 43 percent to Rs. 17.8 billion and operating profit increased 83 percent to Rs. 11.6 billion. Finance costs eased to Rs. 13.7 billion from Rs. 16.1 billion, helping the group narrow its loss after tax to Rs. 3.59 billion from Rs. 11.09 billion.\n\nDespite the improvement, the balance sheet remains under severe strain. Shareholders\u2019 funds stood at a negative Rs. 66.4 billion, and the current ratio was 0.48 times. Net interest-bearing borrowings declined only marginally to Rs. 115.9 billion as at 31 March 2026, from Rs. 117.6 billion a year earlier. The group also slipped back into a pre-tax loss in the first quarter of 2026/27, which management attributed to prevailing economic conditions and financing costs.\n\nTo ease its liquidity pressures, the group has signed debt restructuring offer letters for loans amounting to Rs. 47.5 billion up to 2025/26 and a further Rs. 12.2 billion after the year end, securing grace periods of six to 18 months on capital repayments. Under the rescheduled terms, Rs. 18.1 billion falls due in 2026/27 and Rs. 41.8 billion thereafter. Restructuring requests for another Rs. 15.7 billion are pending approval from lenders."
