    "chunk_text": "The latest figure is considerably higher than the approximately US$ 250 million in realised FDI he publicly cited for the period to June in early July, when he defined realised investments as those remitted into the country through Inward Investment Accounts.\n\nThe BOI is yet to formally publish its first-half figures, with the Director General indicating that data, including export figures, is still being collected and combined zone by zone ahead of release.\n\nIn early July, Jayawardena outlined a reform agenda aimed at lifting investment, including a digital single-window approval platform targeted for launch before the end of this year, an Investment Protection Act already cleared by the Attorney General\u2019s Department, and a review of land allocation rules, given that transferring State land for investment projects currently takes between 18 and 24 months.\n\nFDI inflows in 2025 rose 72 percent from a year earlier, with Singapore, India, France, the Netherlands and Luxembourg the top five sources. (NF)"
