    "chunk_text": "The landslide occurred at around 11 a.m. yesterday, and Hatton Police, together with residents, began clearing the earth from the road.\n\nPolice said the Road Development Authority had also been informed to deploy machinery and expedite the removal of the earth.\n\nMeanwhile, authorities have warned residents in several areas of Kandy District to remain alert over the possibility of flooding as water levels in the Mahaweli River continue to rise.\n\nAccording to a notice issued by the Irrigation Department, heavy flooding could occur if the water levels in the Mahaweli River rise further.\n\nThe warning covers residents in Gelioya, Gampola, Nawalapitiya and Peradeniya, with Divisional Secretaries and police authorities being requested to take necessary measures to ensure the safety of residents.\n\nAuthorities have been instructed to direct people to designated safe centres where necessary, depending on the developing flood situation.\n\nThe notice was issued by Deputy Director (Disaster Management) I.A.K. Ranaweera on behalf of the Kandy District Secretary."
