    "chunk_text": "Speaking at the inaugural event, Sri Lanka Elections Commission member Ameer Faiz said that Sri Lanka is ready to implement OCV. \u201cBut what lies in between implementation and intention is the legal authority to proceed. The difficulty has never been the principle; difficulty is in the details,\u201d he said.\n\nHe further said that there is a substantial population of citizens living and working overseas. \u201cMost of them remain deeply connected to their families, communities and country. They contribute to their country through remittances, skills, knowledge, investments and through connections they build between Sri Lanka and the wider world. Many care deeply about strengthening democracy and safeguarding rights. While we count their contributions in many ways we are yet to count them in our ballot boxes,\u201d Faiz underscored.\n\nIn her remarks, Australia\u2019s Deputy High Commissioner to Sri Lanka Ruth Baird said that the diplomatic partnership between Sri Lanka and Australia is reaching its 80-year milestone.\n\n\u201cElections are fundamental to democratic societies. Supporting citizens to participate in elections while living abroad is an issue many election management bodies continue to consider and navigate. Overseas voting raises a range of legal, policy, administrative, technological and operational considerations. Different countries have approached these questions in ways that reflect their own circumstances, institutions and priorities,\u201d she added."
