    "md5": "6d3452f1b55d1c39e2265d207b8bc045",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 890,
    "chunk_text": "Government to appeal to Saudi King for Anojan\u2019s pardon\n\nColombo, Sep. 21 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake met the parents of Sivarasa Anojan, a Sri Lankan national sentenced to death in Saudi Arabia, at the Presidential Secretariat this morning.\n\nThe President assured them that the Government was making every possible effort to secure a pardon for Anojan through both legal and diplomatic channels.\n\nHe said the Government would make a formal written diplomatic appeal to the King of Saudi Arabia seeking a pardon for Anojan.\n\nThe President also briefed Anojan\u2019s parents on measures already taken by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, including the submission of appeals to the relevant authorities.\n\nHe further assured them that the Government was closely monitoring the progress of these efforts and would continue to pursue all possible avenues to secure a pardon."
  },
