    "md5": "61f843ead755b4a9f39ea9b507f68682",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1913,
    "chunk_text": "Ambassador Wei stressed the importance of both nations speaking with a common voice on issues such as climate change, poverty reduction and development, and global governance, while effectively countering misinformation and misleading narratives.\n\nFan described media professionals as the current generation entrusted with telling the story of this long relationship.\n\nExplaining the need for upholding open cooperation, he said that Chinese and Sri Lankan media should focus on the broader picture of bilateral relations and report truthfully, objectively and comprehensively on cooperation, including projects under the Belt and Road Initiative.\n\n\u201cSuch reporting can improve mutual understanding and contribute to sustained bilateral cooperation,\u201d he said, adding that the state-to-state relations are strengthened by understanding and connections between ordinary people.\n\n\u201cArtificial intelligence, big data and social media are transforming journalism and international communication. Chinese and Sri Lankan media can exchange knowledge on new technologies, platforms and business models while creating closer cooperation among young journalists, editors and media organisations,\u201d he said.\n\nDrawing on the two countries\u2019 shared Asian philosophical traditions, University of Kelaniya Head of Department of Mass Communication Prof. Manoj Jinadasa said China-Sri Lanka media cooperation should go beyond the exchange of technology and information.\n\nHe also said that both countries have much to learn from each other, particularly as rapid technological change and digital networks reshape how people receive and understand information.\n\nProf. Jinadasa stressed that China\u2019s technological and economic advances could offer useful lessons for Sri Lanka\u2019s media sector, while Sri Lanka could contribute by bringing its own communication traditions and philosophical perspectives into the partnership."
  },
