    "chunk_text": "At the panel discussion on Deepening media ties between China and Sri Lanka through people-to people connectivity,\u00a0 International News of China Daily Deputy Director Shao Xinying emphasised that journalists in China and Sri Lanka have much in common and that media cooperation can strengthen mutual trust.\n\nShao, highlighting the importance of telling contemporary human stories, gave the example of a young Sri Lankan who learned Mandarin through an exchange program in China and later found employment at Port City Colombo.\n\n\u201cHis experience illustrated how exchanges between the two countries can directly affect individual lives,\u201d she said while proposing to use city-to-city relationships to tell stories of people-to-people connections.\n\n\u201cRegional media networks could provide another platform. Cooperation between Chinese and Sri Lankan media could be strengthened to leverage Asian regional media networks and jointly amplify the voice of the Global South,\u201d Shao noted."
