    "chunk_text": "The Irrigation Department said significant rainfall continued across the Western, North Western and Sabaragamuwa provinces and the Galle, Matara, Kandy, Nuwara Eliya and Matale districts, though intensity had eased slightly. The upper catchment areas of the Kelani River had received 100mm to 125mm of rainfall as of yesterday morning, while most other river basins recorded 50mm to 80mm over the preceding 24 hours.\n\nThe Irrigation Department extended flood warnings for the Kuda Ganga sub-basin of the Kalu Ganga and the Gin Ganga basin by a further 24 hours, urging residents and motorists, particularly on by-roads, to exercise extreme caution.\n\nSeparately, the Department of Meteorology said a low-pressure area over the Andaman Sea is expected to intensify into a depression within 24 hours. While not expected to directly impact Sri Lanka, associated wind flow is forecast to sustain rainy conditions, particularly in the southwest. Showers or thundershowers are forecast today in the Western, Sabaragamuwa, Central and North-Western provinces, and in the Galle and Matara districts, with heavy rainfall of around 100mm possible in some areas. Strong winds of 40-50kmph are also forecast over the western slopes of the Central Hills, North-Central and North-Western provinces, and in Trincomalee, Hambantota and Matale.\n\nThe Education Ministry said 38 schools island-wide, including 35 in the Central Province, were granted a holiday yesterday due to the adverse weather, with local education authorities empowered to decide on school closures in their areas."
