    "chunk_size_bytes": 1984,
    "chunk_text": "Blue Diamonds Jewellery Worldwide appoints new Chairman, Directors\n\nBlue Diamonds Jewellery Worldwide PLC has appointed R.J.A.M.S. Arshan as Chairman of the Board, while Sivakumar Ramabhadra and Balachandran Niransan have been appointed as Independent Non-Executive Directors.\n\nArshan is a projects, business consulting, operations, sales and marketing professional with over 25 years of experience across government projects and private-sector industrial businesses.\n\nHe most recently served as a Projects Consultant to the Sri Lanka Ports Authority and has held senior positions including Director \u2013 Logistics and Operations at Massline International Ltd., Senior Manager \u2013 Sales, Marketing and Projects at Magline Switchboards Ltd., and Senior Manager \u2013 Industrial Projects and Corporate at OREL Corporation.\n\nHis qualifications include a B.Sc. in Electrical Engineering from the University of Moratuwa; a B.Sc. (Honours)/Higher Education qualification from the University of Portsmouth/SQA, UK; a Diploma in Business Higher Management; higher education studies in Business Management; a Higher National Diploma in Computing from SYSCOMES, UAE/SQA, UK; a Diploma in Computing with Second Class Honours (Lower Division) from SYSCOMES, UAE; an Advanced Diploma in Information Technology; a Diploma in Business Management from the British Council, Colombo; a Diploma in English; and a Junior Diploma in Information Technology from SYSCOMES, UAE.\n\nHe is also a member of the Federation of Information Technology Industry Sri Lanka and the Sri Lanka Computer Vendor Association. Arshan possesses extensive expertise in project consulting, industrial project management, business development, corporate account management, logistics, operations, tender management, commercial negotiation and stakeholder coordination. His broad project, operational and commercial experience will strengthen the Board\u2019s strategic planning, business-development and project-oversight capabilities."
