    "md5": "afa616340029b0c412354c83362c0546",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1838,
    "chunk_text": "EDB promotes \u201cSri Lanka Expo 2027\u201d in collaboration with SriLankan  Airlines\n\nThe Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB) recently unveiled a specially branded Airbus A321 Neo aircraft of SriLankan\u00a0 Airlines, liveried with the \u201cSri Lanka Expo 2027\u201d brand identity, to promote Sri Lanka Expo 2027 \u2013 the country\u2019s premier international exhibition. The Expo will comprehensively showcase Sri Lanka\u2019s diverse export sectors, including agriculture, industrial manufacturing, export services, innovation, and tourism.\n\nThe special event held to mark the departure of the newly branded aircraft was attended by EDB Chairman and CEO Mangala Wijesinghe, Director General Erandika Dissanayake, Sri Lanka Expo 2027 Project Lead and Director \u2013 Export Services Indumini Kodikara, Sri Lanka Expo 2027 Consultant Coordinator Anoma Premathilake, and a number of officials from SriLankan Airlines.\n\nOperating under the guidance of the Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Ministry, the Sri Lanka Export Development Board will organise the \u201cSri Lanka Expo 2027\u201d international exhibition from 14 to 17 January 2027 at the Bandaranaike Memorial International Conference Hall (BMICH) in Colombo. This landmark event is strategically designed to position Sri Lanka as a vital trade and investment hub within the South Asian region.\n\nThe exhibition is poised to host over 750 prominent exhibitors and welcome more than 1,500 international buyers and investors. In addition to the main exhibition, the event will feature an array of parallel high-level forums, including a dedicated Investment Forum, industry-specific sessions and structured B2B matchmaking meetings. To provide a holistic experience of Sri Lanka\u2019s economic and cultural dynamism, the event will also feature fashion shows, culinary shows and cultural performances."
  },
