    "md5": "4b9129db078422eef50b4d426cc33ef2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1610,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka, Qatar seek more jobs for skilled workers\n\nColombo, Sep. 22 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka and Qatar have discussed measures to further strengthen bilateral cooperation in labour and foreign employment during a meeting between Sri Lanka\u2019s Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs and Foreign Employment Arun Hemachandra and Qatar\u2019s Minister of Labour, Dr. Ali bin Saeed bin Smeikh Al Marri.\n\nThe meeting was held in Doha during Deputy Minister Hemachandra\u2019s official visit to Qatar from September 20 to 23, coinciding with the 50th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries.\n\nDiscussions focused on expanding employment opportunities for skilled and professionally qualified Sri Lankan workers, strengthening worker welfare and protection, promoting transparent recruitment practices and improving the mutual recognition of vocational and professional qualifications.\n\nDeputy Minister Hemachandra noted that labour and foreign employment remain key areas of Sri Lanka-Qatar bilateral relations, with nearly 140,000 Sri Lankans currently employed in Qatar.\n\nHe also highlighted the importance of reconvening the Sri Lanka-Qatar Joint Committee meeting after several years, saying the mechanism could help translate bilateral discussions into practical benefits for workers and employers.\n\nThe two sides also discussed strengthening skills development programmes and increasing access for Sri Lankan workers to skill-based and higher-value employment opportunities in Qatar.\n\nThe Sri Lankan delegation included Sri Lanka\u2019s Ambassador to Qatar, Sitara Khan, along with other officials."
  },
