    "md5": "18e7f6ea29babbeacaad7dd9a51933a7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1835,
    "chunk_text": "Pan Asia EZY has been developed with everyday customer behaviour in mind. The users can choose to hide or display account balances, save favourite beneficiaries and billers with preferred payment amounts and receive payment reminders through push notifications and email.\n\n\u201cPan Asia EZY was built around our customers and what they want from banking today \u2013 simplicity, convenience, security and greater control. We have brought together the services they use regularly while adding features that address real everyday needs. The idea behind \u2018Built for More\u2019 is simple: we want to make banking EZY so our customers have more time and freedom to do more,\u201d said Pan Asia Bank Chief Digital Officer Pradeepan Sivalingam.\n\nSecurity remains central to the platform, which complies with the Central Bank of Sri Lanka guidelines and undergoes independent third-party security audits.\n\nPan Asia Bank Director and CEO Naleen Edirisinghe commented, \u201cDigital banking is changing the relationship between the customers and their bank. People increasingly expect banking to fit around their lives, rather than the other way around. Pan Asia EZY is our response to that change. We are investing in technology to make banking more accessible and convenient, while ensuring that the experience remains secure and relevant to our customers. Our ambition is to build a digital platform that continues to grow with them and supports the way they live, work and manage their finances,\u201d he said.\n\nPan Asia Bank is already working on further enhancements, including a fully trilingual experience, richer card management capabilities and the potential integration of artificial intelligence to provide more personalised financial insights. The bank is also developing Pan Asia EZY BIZ, a next-generation cash management platform for businesses."
