    "md5": "db3f9737ec1cc078a6cfb5a4d3ee469f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1962,
    "chunk_text": "LOLC Finance-Continental Cars promote Volkswagen vehicles across Sri Lanka\n\nLOLC Finance Chief Operating Officer Montini Warnakula and Continental Cars Deputy Chairman Charu Senavirathna with their teams during MoU handover ceremony\n\nLOLC Finance PLC has entered into a memorandum of understanding (MoU) with Continental Cars (Pvt.) Ltd to jointly promote the Volkswagen vehicles across Sri Lanka, creating enhanced opportunities for the customers seeking attractive and flexible vehicle financing solutions.\n\nThis islandwide initiative brings together the financial strength and extensive customer reach of LOLC Finance, with the globally recognised Volkswagen brand represented in Sri Lanka\u00a0by Continental Cars.\n\nUnder the partnership, LOLC Finance will offer a range of value-added financial benefits to the customers purchasing the Volkswagen vehicles. These include discounted insurance premiums through approved insurance partners, flexible and customised repayment plans and operating lease facilities designed for corporate entities to cater to diverse customer requirements.\n\nThe eligible customers will receive a complimentary credit card facility, subject to applicable eligibility criteria.\n\nAs part of the promotional initiative, Continental Cars will offer exclusive discounts of Rs.100,000 on selected Volkswagen models. The customers purchasing either the Volkswagen Taigun or Virtus models will be eligible to receive a Rs.100,000 discount, further enhancing the value offered under the partnership.\n\nLOLC Finance Chief Operating Officer Montini Warnakula said, \u201cThis partnership with Continental Cars reflects our commitment to providing the customers with greater choice, convenience and value. By combining our flexible financing solutions with the strength of the Volkswagen brand, we are creating an attractive proposition for the customers while expanding opportunities within Sri Lanka\u2019s automotive and financial services sectors.\u201d"
  },
