    "md5": "e6472e4a08b70c472876087049a27fe5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 993,
    "chunk_text": "The group pointed to foreign institutional capital as a further sign of confidence. Softlogic Life Insurance secured US $ 15 million in long-term Tier 2 capital from Norfund and OP Finnfund Global Impact Fund I.\n\nSoftlogic maintains that Phase I of the recalibrated ODEL Mall project will be funded primarily through the pre-sales of the office space and external equity, without incremental debt.\n\nIt also expects the placement of its Colombo and Bentota hotels under Accor\u2019s Pullman brand to lift international occupancy, generate foreign currency cash flows and help mitigate the exchange rate risk on its hospitality debt.\n\nHowever, the improvement in operating metrics is yet to flow through fully to the shareholders. The annual report shows the group recorded a loss of Rs.8.63 billion attributable to the equity holders for 2025/26, while the shareholders\u2019 funds remained negative at Rs.66.4 billion.\n\nThe group also returned to a pre-tax loss in the first quarter of 2026/27. (NF)"
