    "chunk_size_bytes": 1039,
    "chunk_text": "Driver, two women arrested after police pursuit in Pannala\n\nColombo, Sep. 22 (Daily Mirror) - Police have arrested the driver of a luxury car and two women following a police pursuit in Pannala town.\n\nAccording to police, officers from the Giriulla Police fired shots after the vehicle allegedly failed to stop despite repeated signals to pull over.\n\nPolice said the vehicle continued driving, prompting officers to pursue it before stopping the car and several other vehicles in Pannala town.\n\nThe driver allegedly locked the doors and remained inside the vehicle after it was stopped. Police officers subsequently pointed a T-56 rifle at the driver and warned that they would open fire if he did not open the doors.\n\nWhen the doors were not opened, police officers broke the vehicle's windows and opened the door before arresting the driver and the two women.\n\nPolice said a small quantity of suspected drugs was also recovered from the possession of the male suspect.\n\nThe three suspects are residents of the Giriulla area, police said."
