    "chunk_size_bytes": 1739,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan-origin actress will play Sita in a leading musical at Wembley Arena\n\nSri Lankan-origin actress Bhavithra Gananathan is set to make her professional acting debut as Sita in the major arena production Diwali Story: The Journey of Ram \u2013 A Musical at OVO Arena Wembley on Sunday, 27 September 2026.\n\nThe 19-year-old multidisciplinary artist and university student will appear opposite Kiran Kaanan, who plays Ram, in the large-scale musical retelling of the Ramayana. The professional cast will be joined by approximately 100 community actors and dancers. The production follows the success of the show\u2019s sold-out 2025 staging at the Royal Albert Hall and will feature new material and original music.\n\nBhavithra is an actress, writer and classically trained Bharatanatyam dancer. She began acting at the age of five, when she played Ursula in a production of The Little Mermaid. During the ensuing 14 years, she trained and performed with organisations including the National Youth Theatre and the Rose Theatre. She currently trains at the Collective Acting Studio and won the National Iris Breuer Writing Award in 2024.\n\nShe began learning Bharatanatyam at the age of seven under her aunt Meena Elankumaran, and completed her Arangetram in March 2025. Bhavithra has also trained in Carnatic vocal music since she was 12.\n\nCommenting on Sita\u2019s connection with Sri Lanka, Bhavithra said: \u201cAs a young woman, it is especially meaningful to portray Sita. An important part of her journey unfolds in Sri Lanka, and the island\u2019s landscape, history and traditions retain a powerful connection with the Ramayana. Playing Sita allows me to explore that connection while helping to bring this timeless story to a new generation.\u201d"
  },
