    "chunk_text": "Commenting on Sita\u2019s connection with Sri Lanka, Bhavithra said: \u201cAs a young woman, it is especially meaningful to portray Sita. An important part of her journey unfolds in Sri Lanka, and the island\u2019s landscape, history and traditions retain a powerful connection with the Ramayana. Playing Sita allows me to explore that connection while helping to bring this timeless story to a new generation.\u201d\n\nThe Wembley production will include original songs and music by Indian composer Rahul Ranade, with celebrated playback singer and Padma Shri recipient Kavita Krishnamurthy contributing to the new score. A newly created third act will explore the five days of Diwali and the continuing influence of the Ramayana\u2019s values on contemporary family traditions.\n\nDirected and co-written by S\u00e2mir Bhamra, the production will be presented by Sanatan Events Ltd in partnership with The Palan Foundation and Golden Tours.\n\nDiwali Story: The Journey of Ram \u2013 A Musical will be performed at OVO Arena Wembley on Sunday, 27 September 2026. Doors will open at 4.30 pm, with the performance beginning at 6.15 pm."
