    "chunk_size_bytes": 1297,
    "chunk_text": "Seat belts help reduce expressway accident casualties: RDA\n\nColombo, Sep. 22 (Daily Mirror) - Road Development Authority (RDA) Director General Anuradha Hettiarachchi said yesterday that casualties from road accidents on expressways have declined following the introduction of mandatory seat-belt regulations for all passengers.\n\nHe told the media that the number of casualties in yesterday\u2019s multiple-vehicle accident on the Southern Expressway was limited because passengers were wearing seat belts.\n\nHettiarachchi said accidents on expressways have increased in recent days due to rainy weather and urged motorists to exercise greater caution when driving under wet conditions.\n\nHe identified speeding, poor lane discipline and failure to maintain a safe distance between vehicles as some of the main causes of accidents on expressways.\n\nThe RDA Director General also said vehicles that are not roadworthy have been observed entering expressways, posing an additional risk to motorists.\n\nHe urged drivers to maintain proper lane discipline, keep a safe distance from other vehicles and drive at appropriate speeds, particularly during rainy weather.\n\nSeat belt rule to be strictly enforced on Expressways from September 19\n\nSeat belts mandatory for all passengers on expressways from midnight"
