    "chunk_size_bytes": 765,
    "chunk_text": "Mustapha, Kumarapperuma offer free legal assistance in Anojan\u2019s case\n\nColombo, Sep. 22 (Daily Mirror) - President\u2019s Counsel Faiszer Musthapha and President\u2019s Counsel Upul Kumarapperuma have agreed to provide legal assistance in the case of Sri Lankan national Sivarasa Anojan, who was sentenced to death in Saudi Arabia, Foreign Minister Vijitha Herath told Parliament today.\n\nHerath said the two lawyers had also agreed to travel to Saudi Arabia at their own expense to assist with the case.\n\nAccording to the Minister, Mustapha and Kumarapperuma will hold discussions with Anojan\u2019s legal representatives and Saudi law enforcement authorities to explore possible legal interventions.\n\n\u201cI must thank them for their contribution,\u201d Herath told Parliament."
