    "md5": "6eab450f9b802b668a2f6d894195a089",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1751,
    "chunk_text": "Bring reusable bags to Colombo Book Fair, CEA urges public\n\nColombo, Sep. 22 (Daily Mirror) - The Central Environmental Authority (CEA) has urged consumers visiting the Colombo International Book Fair to bring an environmentally friendly, reusable bag to carry the books they purchase and contribute to protecting the environment.\n\nCEA Director General R.S.P. Kapila Rajapaksa said it had been observed in recent years that plastic bags, particularly \u2018silly sili\u2019 bags, are extensively used to carry books at the Colombo International Book Fair, where a large number of consumers purchase books.\n\nThe Consumer Affairs Authority (CAA) has announced through Gazette No. 2456/41 dated October 1, 2025, that \u2018silly sili\u2019 bags should not be provided free of charge to any consumer. If such bags are sold, the amount charged for them must be mentioned in the bill.\n\nThe law has been introduced to prevent environmental damage caused by the use of single-use polythene and plastic products.\n\nTherefore, the CEA said the public could contribute to fulfilling their responsibility to protect the environment by bringing an eco-friendly reusable bag when purchasing books and minimising the use of polythene bags.\n\nFurthermore, the sale, offering for sale, giving away free of charge, displaying or using single-use plastic drinking straws; single-use plastic plates, cups, spoons, forks and knives; as well as food wrappers or \u2018lunch sheets\u2019 manufactured using polythene as a raw material in the country are prohibited by law.\n\nThe CEA said an agreement had been reached following discussions with the relevant parties to ensure that these prohibited items are not used in any manner at food outlets within the premises where the book fair is held."
  },
