    "md5": "abc5e683e726b5f4b87f1fa763dfffea",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 640,
    "chunk_text": "The Speaker informed Parliament today of the Supreme Court\u2019s determination, which stated that the 22nd Amendment did not require approval at a referendum. The Court also directed amendments to Clause 2 of the Bill, including a change concerning the age of 67 and an exception to the proposed six-year term limit for a person holding office as Chief Justice when the Act comes into operation.\n\nMinister Jayatissa said those who disagreed with the Supreme Court\u2019s determination would remain free to express their views in Parliament or organise demonstrations, while the Government would proceed according to the constitutional procedure."
