    "chunk_size_bytes": 1233,
    "chunk_text": "Heavy rainfall above 100mm expected in several areas\n\nColombo, Sep. 22 (Daily Mirror) - Heavy rainfall exceeding 100mm is expected in several parts of Sri Lanka as the depression currently located over the northwest Bay of Bengal, northeast of the island, is forecast to intensify into a deep depression within the next 12 hours.\n\nAlthough the system is not expected to directly affect Sri Lanka, rainy conditions in the southwestern parts of the country are expected to continue due to the prevailing wind flow towards the system.\n\nAccording to forecast, showers or thundershowers will occur at times in the Western, Sabaragamuwa, Central and North Western provinces, as well as in the Galle and Matara districts. Heavy falls exceeding 100mm are likely at some places in these areas.\n\nSeveral spells of showers may also occur in the North Central Province and Mannar District.\n\nStrong winds of around 40\u201350 kmph are expected at times over the western slopes of the Central Hills, North Central and North Western provinces, and in the Trincomalee, Hambantota and Matale districts.\n\nThe public is advised to take adequate precautions to minimise damage caused by temporary localised strong winds and lightning during thundershowers."
  },
