    "chunk_size_bytes": 1226,
    "chunk_text": "It further considered the treatment provided after the patient developed breathing difficulties and other complications.\n\nThe investigation had also examined the coordination between doctors and nursing staff, the response to emergencies and hospital administrative procedures.\n\nMedical statements, hospital records and other documents obtained during the investigation had been considered in reaching the observations contained in the report.\n\nThe report was signed and submitted by the investigating officer on June 21, 2023.\n\nHowever, the report itself should not be interpreted as a final determination of criminal or professional liability against any individual doctor or health worker. Any responsibility would have to be determined by the relevant authorities after considering the complete investigation report, medical records and other available evidence.\n\nDr. Chamal Sanjeewa has now urged the Health Secretary to release the investigation findings and take appropriate action based on the conclusions reached by the inquiry.\n\nThe demand comes amid renewed concerns over accountability and transparency in the public health sector, particularly when serious complications or deaths occur during hospital treatment."
