    "chunk_text": "While geopolitics and foreign policy were Nihal\u2019s public face, he was a very creative person and loved creativity in others. He loved music and opera and in his last years music would keep him calm and contented. Nihal\u2019s secret passion were old movies, especially those with Humphrey Bogart as a hero. He must have seen Casablanca a 100 times. He was an unabashed romantic. Nihal and Chitra\u2019s love story with Nihal stealing the Harischandra beauty was also testament to that fact.\n\nChitra, Nihal\u2019s wife was a professional teacher recognised by many. Generations of Ladies College girls greet and meet her all over the world. Their love and respect for her are very obvious. She was also the perfect hostess and trained generations of diplomatic wives to plan and entertain in diplomatic\u00a0 circles. My greatest respect for Chitra was for her role as carer in the last three years of Nihal\u2019s life. It was a very difficult period and she did everything to make him comfortable. Her sacrifice and dedication sometimes broke my heart."
