    "language": "en",
    "md5": "c8ce53f84919b5bf559516471e4817e2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1521,
    "chunk_text": "The Sri Lanka fund is intended to create a structured channel for capital into listed and private Sri Lankan companies, leveraging complementary deal flow, research and investor networks on both sides of the Palk Strait.\n\nSincere Syndication CEO Sivaramakrishnan R., said: \u201cIndian capital is increasingly looking beyond domestic borders for growth opportunities. Sri Lanka offers an attractive neighborhood market with improving fundamentals. Pairing the expertise behind our Bharat Transformation Fund with a dedicated Sri Lanka vehicle allows us to serve clients seeking exposure to the island\u2019s listed and private companies through a structured channel.\u201d\n\nAvyukthi Consulting and Advisory Services LLP\u2019s Ramesh R., said: \u201cCross-border transactions between India and Sri Lanka involve specific tax, regulatory and structuring considerations. Our role is to help de-risk and accelerate those processes so that good investment ideas can move from discussion to execution more efficiently.\u201d\n\nThe initiative comes against a backdrop of recovering Sri Lankan capital markets and growing Indian investor interest in frontier and near-shore opportunities. By linking a listed Sri Lankan investment platform with an established Indian multi-family office and specialist advisory capability, the parties aim to reduce friction in cross-border capital flows, improve information exchange and create a more systematic pipeline of opportunities for institutional, family-office and high-net-worth capital on both sides."
  },
