    "chunk_size_bytes": 1440,
    "chunk_text": "Prime Lands receives YouTube Silver Play Button\n\nMakes history as SL\u2019s 1st real estate developer to receive it\n\nPrime Lands has made history in Sri Lanka\u2019s real estate sector by becoming the country\u2019s first real estate developer to receive the prestigious YouTube Silver Play Button, after surpassing 100,000 subscribers.\n\nThe milestone comes as Prime Group celebrates its 30th anniversary, adding a significant digital achievement to three decades of growth and innovation.\n\nAs part of YouTube\u2019s Creator Awards programme, the Silver Play Button recognises the channels that reach significant subscriber milestones.\n\nFor Prime Lands, reaching this milestone marked more than a growth in audience; it reflected the developer\u2019s transformation from traditional marketing to a digital-first approach and its commitment to using content, technology and storytelling to redefine how Sri Lankans discover and engage with real estate.\n\nToday, with a YouTube community of more than 600,000 subscribers, Prime Lands continues to expand its digital reach and deepen its connection with property seekers across Sri Lanka.\n\nPrime Lands CEO and Executive Director Ruminda Randeniya said, \u201cThrough the YouTube journey, we have transformed the way people make real estate decisions, guiding smarter property choices to immersive, insightful content, helping them visualise opportunities, understand market dynamics and make informed choices.\u201d"
  },
