    "language": "en",
    "md5": "d35899bdc668f2a1750d0c2252bbfda2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1820,
    "chunk_text": "SLIIT Int\u2019l-Liverpool John Moores University inaugurate learning facility in Colombo\n\nPanel discussion on \u2018Beyond Borders: The Role of British Higher Education in Developing Globally Competitive Graduates\u2019 featuring SLIIT Computing Faculty Senior Lecturer Kavinga Yapa, Board Member Dr. Harsha Cabral, Vice-Chancellor, Managing Director and Chief Executive Officer Prof. Lalith Gamage, British Council Head of Education Sajeewa Meepage and Liverpool John Moores University Society and Culture Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor Prof. Timothy Nichol\n\nFrom left: SLIIT Vice-Chancellor, Managing Director and Chief Executive Officer Prof. Lalith Gamage and Liverpool John Moores University Society and Culture Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor Prof. Timothy Nichol\n\nThe Sri Lanka Institute of Information Technology (SLIIT) and Liverpool John Moores University (LJMU), United Kingdom, recently inaugurated SLIIT International in collaboration with LJMU, a dedicated international learning facility located at No. 17, Dickmans Road, Colombo 4.\n\nIt marks a significant milestone in a partnership spanning more than a decade and reinforcing their commitment to providing the Sri Lankan students with access to internationally recognised UK higher education qualifications.\n\nThe grand opening ceremony was attended by British High Commissioner to Sri Lanka Andrew Patrick, who graced the occasion as the chief guest, alongside senior representatives from SLIIT, LJMU, the British Council, academia, industry and other stakeholders, marking the next chapter of the long-standing SLIIT-LJMU collaboration.\n\nThe new facility is particularly significant as Sri Lanka\u2019s first academic facility dedicated exclusively to the delivery of LJMU degree programmes, reflecting the strength, maturity and long-term commitment of the partnership."
  },
