    "md5": "a49b704f35c09f03b971207e8e0d1e87",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1262,
    "chunk_text": "Conversely, disappointing\u00a0 Opposition political parties which predicted an economic collapse under the \u201cinexperienced\u201d NPP administration,\u00a0 Sri Lanka earned a record US$ 11.6 billion in 2025 from tourism, foreign remittances and consular services,\u00a0 and there are signs that those revenues taking a further upward trend this year. Export revenue in 2026 is also tracking a strong growth. These achievements are encouraging against the backdrop of the government\u2019s attempts to eradicate corruption and waste.\n\nNPP is acquainted with the fact that those who voted for it the last time did so on impulse and not with political awareness. Therefore, fearing that constitution-making could hit the rocks \u2014 since any solution to the ethnic problem incorporated in it would inevitably divide his vote bank \u2014 Dissanayake seems to want to put off the issue until his second term, or even indefinitely. Similarly,\u00a0 last year\u2019s local government election results would compel the government to further defer the Provincial council elections.\n\nHowever, the political trajectory of the country beyond the next Presidential election totally depends on whether the masses have realised the difference between political objectives of the NPP and the other parties."
  },
