    "chunk_text": "Muslim community suffered a massive public backlash after the Easter attack, which, while unfortunate, is a predictable social reaction. It took years for the mistrust to fade away. But that might also have reversed the runaway Arabisation within the community.\n\nThe ongoing controversial detention of former military intelligence chief Suresh Salley and the politicised narrative of the complicity of intelligence agencies in the Easter Sunday attack \u2013 which any local defence correspondent worth their salt knows is bullocks \u2013\u00a0 weakens the intelligence apparatus and delegitimises them before the international media and agencies. Sri Lanka should take lessons from the Easter Sunday attack to avoid repetition. Instead, the country is repeating the same mistakes."
