    "chunk_text": "Dickwella returns to T20I Squad after five years\n\nColombo, Sep. 23 (Daily Mirror) - Niroshan Dickwella earned a call-up to Sri Lanka\u2019s T20I squad for the first time in half a decade as the country\u2019s cricket board announced the squad for the Asian Games men\u2019s cricket competition on Tuesday.\n\nAshen Bandara also returned to the squad after three years, with the two bringing their experience to the Aichi-Nagoya Games this time around.\n\nSohan de Livera, Sineth Jayawardena, Wanuja Sahan and Garuka Sanketh received their maiden T20I call-ups, with Sahan Arachchige named captain of the side.\n\nSri Lanka earned a direct qualification to the Asian Games quarterfinals, and will open its campaign in Nissin on September 29.\n\nSahan Arachchige (c), Sohan de Livera, Wanuja Sahan, Niroshan Dickwella (wk), Ashen Bandara, Dushan Hemantha, Lasith Croospulle, Chamika Karunaratne, Nuwan Thushara, Sineth Jayawardena, Tharindu Ratnayake, Binura Fernando, Nuwanidu Fernando, Vijayakanth Viyaskanth, Garuka Sanketh"
