    "md5": "5dc1f02ea35b14d764de5da25ef5f6e2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 951,
    "chunk_text": "Three new High Court Judges appointed\n\nColombo, Sep. 23 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake today appointed three new High Court Judges, with their letters of appointment formally handed over at the Presidential Secretariat.\n\nAccording to the President\u2019s Media Division (PMD), the new appointments were made from among Special Grade officers of the Judicial Service.\n\nThe appointees are Perumal Sivakumar, currently serving as the District Judge of Jaffna; Anandi Kanagaratnam, Senior Assistant Secretary of the Judicial Service Commission; and Gnanesha Lalith Kannangara, currently serving as the District Judge of Colombo.\n\nPresident Dissanayake presented the letters of appointment to the three judges at a ceremony held at the Presidential Secretariat today (23), marking their appointment to the High Court bench.\n\nThe appointments come as the three senior Judicial Service officers take up their new roles as High Court Judges."
