    "chunk_size_bytes": 901,
    "chunk_text": "Inquiry launched into clash between Harak Kata and Kehelbaddara Padme\n\nColombo, Sep. 23 (Daily Mirror) - The Department of Prisons has launched a special investigation into a clash between two inmates identified as alleged organised crime figures, Nadun Chinthaka Wickremeratne, alias \u201cHarak Kata\u201d, and Mandinu Padmasiri, alias \u201cKehelbaddara Padme\u201d, at the Welisara Prison.\n\nPrison authorities said an Assistant Superintendent of Prisons has been appointed to conduct an inquiry into the incident and determine the circumstances that led to the confrontation.\n\nThe clash reportedly took place last night (22) while both inmates were being held at the Welisara Prison.\n\nDuring the altercation, Kehelbaddara Padme sustained injuries and was subsequently admitted for medical treatment.\n\nHe is currently receiving treatment at the Welisara Prison Hospital, according to the Department of Prisons."
