    "chunk_size_bytes": 761,
    "chunk_text": "Parliament approves Rs. 17.2 bn supplementary estimate for electricity relief\n\nColombo, Sep. 23 (Daily Mirror) - Parliament today approved Supplementary Estimate No. 05 of 2026, under the Ministry of Energy, providing Rs. 17,213 million in financial assistance to offer relief to the public on electricity bills.\n\nThe funds will be reallocated from provisions initially allocated to various line ministries for 2026 but identified as unlikely to be fully utilized by the end of the year.\n\nThe reallocation will not affect the overall expenditure ceiling approved under the Appropriation Act, No. 23 of 2025, or the Government\u2019s maximum borrowing limit.\n\nThe Supplementary Estimate was considered and approved by the Committee on Public Finance yesterday (22)."
