    "chunk_size_bytes": 1931,
    "chunk_text": "Abanchy Ceylon in landmark expansion into Kenya with incorporation of Abanchy Africa Ltd\n\nFrom left: Head of Kenya Operations Ghareeb Mazrui, Senior Executive Business Development Anupa de Silva and Abanchy Africa Head of Africa Region Seth Manickam and Abanchy Ceylon\n\nAbanchy Ceylon Ltd., the logistics arm of Pink Eagle Holdings, recently marked a significant milestone in its African expansion journey with the incorporation of Abanchy Africa Ltd., in Kenya. Abanchy\u2019s operation in the area is the latest amplification of the Group\u2019s presence in Africa, strengthening an international network and operations that began with the launch of sales offices in Ethiopia and Dubai in 2024.\n\nThe establishment of Abanchy Africa signals an important breakthrough in the Group\u2019s regional expansion strategy. Expanding the portfolio of Pink Eagle Holdings, Abanchy Africa will operate as a fully-fledged logistics and freight-forwarding company, providing comprehensive logistics solutions to customers across Kenya.\n\nPink Eagle Group Chairman and Managing Director Asitha Silva said: \u201cBy establishing our presence in Kenya, we\u2019re reaffirming our commitment to creating a resilient and future ready business group with the potential for competitive growth in new directions. Having established a presence in Africa, our goal is to deliver sustainable value and drive innovation by uniting bold, strategic thinking with a modern, global mindset to pursue excellence in innovation and performance.\u201d\n\nServing as a strategic base for Abanchy\u2019s broader vision, the inauguration of the Group\u2019s presence in Kenya offers services covering sea freight, air freight, customs clearance, transportation, warehousing, and other related logistics requirements. Furthermore, in addition to bringing the Group\u2019s capabilities to Kenya, the base will facilitate the expansion of Abanchy\u2019s offerings across the wider East African region."
