    "chunk_id": "2026-09-24-dailyftlk-7df395ba-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "769e4d39930233c98b2f5e6c231b42b1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1759,
    "chunk_text": "Parliament approves Rs. 17.2 b for  electricity relief\n\nFunds reallocated from Line Ministry provisions unlikely to be used by year-end\n\nTransfer leaves overall expenditure ceiling and Govt.\u00a0 borrowing limit unchanged\n\nCommittee on Public Finance clears Supplementary Estimate on 22 Sept.\n\nPromotion of Export Agriculture (Amendment) Bill also passed without amendments\n\nParliament yesterday approved Supplementary Estimate No. 05 of 2026 relating to the Ministry of Energy, providing Rs. 17.2 billion in financial assistance to relieve the public on electricity bills.\n\nA Supplementary Estimate authorises spending beyond the allocations approved in the annual Budget. The Estimate was approved following a debate, after the Committee on Public Finance considered and approved it on 22 September, 2026.\n\nThe funds have been drawn from provisions originally allocated to Line Ministries for 2026 but identified as unlikely to be used by the end of the year. As a result, the transfer will not affect the overall expenditure ceiling approved under the Appropriation Act, No. 23 of 2025, which gave legal effect to the 2026 Budget. Nor will it affect the Government\u2019s maximum borrowing limit.\n\nParliament also passed the Promotion of Export Agriculture (Amendment) Bill without amendments following a debate yesterday.\n\nThe Bill amends the Export Agriculture Promotion Act, No. 46 of 1992. When the Department of Export Agriculture was restructured, new positions were created and existing positions upgraded, including a change in designation from \u201cDirector\u201d to \u201cDirector General\u201d. However, the relevant provisions of the Act had not been amended to match, and other related designations had not been revised either. The Bill makes these amendments."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-24-dailyftlk-7df395ba",
    "num": "dailyftlk-7df395ba",
    "date_str": "2026-09-24",
    "description": "Parliament approves Rs. 17.2 b for  electricity relief",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/Parliament-approves-Rs-17-2-b-for-electricity-relief/34-797684",
