    "language": "en",
    "md5": "0f95ac3fe8286b2c2e1e4f3ceb2659ba",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 856,
    "chunk_text": "The Bill amends the Export Agriculture Promotion Act, No. 46 of 1992. When the Department of Export Agriculture was restructured, new positions were created and existing positions upgraded, including a change in designation from \u201cDirector\u201d to \u201cDirector General\u201d. However, the relevant provisions of the Act had not been amended to match, and other related designations had not been revised either. The Bill makes these amendments.\n\nUnder the revised definition in Section 19 of the Act, an export agricultural crop is any crop identified as having export potential in addition to local consumption. The crop must also be declared a notified agricultural crop by the Minister in charge of the subject under Section 2 of the Act. Paddy, vegetables, fruits, root crops and other food crops are excluded, as is any crop identified as a plantation crop."
  },
