    "language": "en",
    "md5": "84d97ec2d2f036317328d30463dd8464",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1268,
    "chunk_text": "Successful bidders will be granted six months to mobilise and three years to explore, an exploration period that can be extended up to eight years. Production must commence within that eight-year window, after which successful bidders will hold the asset for 20 years.\n\nPDASL Director General Dr. Neil De Silva has said commercial production is being targeted by 2032, contingent on seismic surveys and drilling establishing commercially recoverable resources. Sri Lanka already has two gas discoveries in the Mannar Basin, Dorado and Barracuda, both made in 2011, with combined P50 resource estimates of 839 billion cubic feet (314 bcf and 525 bcf respectively). Dr. De Silva has said the upside potential at Barracuda alone could be at least four times its current estimate.\n\nThe bidding process is being supported by an international investor campaign led by UK-based Frontier Energy Network, appointed as specialist international marketing partner for the round through its PetroInvest platform. The campaign includes investor engagement at the World Energies Summit in London on 29 and 30 September, a virtual investor briefing on 21 October, and further engagement at the Asia Petroleum Geoscience Conference and Exhibition in Kuala Lumpur on 16 and 17 November."
  },
