    "md5": "4fa550c6181638bc6759e264c423416c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1810,
    "chunk_text": "PureHydro powers Maxxis Ceylon Open 2026 Padel Finals\n\nPureHydro served as the Powered Partner of the Maxxis Ceylon Open 2026 Padel Finals, bringing its brand promise, \u201cPure Is a Standard,\u201d courtside while providing players and visitors with convenient access to purified drinking water throughout the Grand Finale.\n\nOrganised by Padel Chief, the competitive doubles tournament was held over two months and featured three divisions and nine categories. It culminated in a Grand Finale comprising the semi-finals and finals, bringing together players, families, spectators and event partners as Sri Lanka\u2019s padel community continues to grow.\n\nAs part of the partnership, PureHydro installed a Hot and Cold-Water Dispenser with a Reverse Osmosis water purification system courtside. The activation allowed players and visitors to experience the product between matches, transforming the sponsorship from conventional brand visibility into a meaningful experience connected to hydration, wellness and sporting performance.\n\n\u201cWe did not want PureHydro to simply be a logo at the venue. By placing the PureHydro Hot and Cold-Water Dispenser courtside, we gave players, families and spectators the opportunity to experience our standard for themselves between matches,\u201d said Rumesh Jayasekara, Senior Marketing Manager at PureHydro.\n\n\u201cPadel brings together sport, wellness, networking, competition and premium leisure. These qualities align naturally with PureHydro and with the standards people increasingly expect from the water they choose for their homes and lifestyles,\u201d he added.\n\n\u201cThe Maxxis Ceylon Open 2026 demonstrates what can be achieved when players, clubs and partners come together around a structured competitive platform,\u201d said Nisal Sudila, Chief Operating Officer of Padel Chief."
  },
