    "chunk_text": "\u201cThe Maxxis Ceylon Open 2026 demonstrates what can be achieved when players, clubs and partners come together around a structured competitive platform,\u201d said Nisal Sudila, Chief Operating Officer of Padel Chief.\n\nThe partnership forms part of PureHydro\u2019s wider commitment to connecting water quality and hydration with active, health-conscious lifestyles. Through its 2026 campaign, \u201cPure Is a Standard,\u201d the brand seeks to reinforce the importance of quality, reliability and better water standards across homes, workplaces and everyday life.\n\nPureHydro is a water purification brand of St. Anthony\u2019s Hydro, backed by the trusted legacy of the St. Anthony\u2019s Group, which has served Sri Lankan consumers and businesses for more than 80 years. Building on the Group\u2019s reputation for quality, reliability and customer trust, St. Anthony\u2019s Hydro offers domestic and industrial water purification solutions, including Reverse Osmosis water purifiers, filtration systems, and hot and cold-water dispensers."
