    "language": "en",
    "md5": "a72a00d33ecab93d7ac5bc9e034aa84a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1263,
    "chunk_text": "CCC urges targeted poverty relief after Fitch upgrade\n\nSri Lanka must ensure its economic recovery reaches the poorer households while preserving the fiscal discipline behind its latest sovereign rating upgrade, the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce (CCC) said.\n\nReacting to Fitch Ratings\u2019 decision to raise Sri Lanka\u2019s long-term foreign-currency rating from \u2018CCC+\u2019 to \u2018B-\u2019, with a Stable Outlook, the CCC called for targeted poverty reduction alongside measures to strengthen public finances.\n\n\u201cA targeted approach to poverty reduction should also remain a priority to ensure that the benefits of economic recovery and growth are broadly shared across society,\u201d it said in a statement.\n\nThe CCC said Sri Lanka must maintain the primary budget surpluses and sustain revenue mobilisation, while gradually reducing debt and debt-service ratios to create more fiscal space.\n\nIt also called for stronger foreign exchange reserves to protect the gains made since the economic crisis.\n\nThe upgrade recognised progress on fiscal consolidation, debt restructuring and structural reforms, the CCC said.\n\nIt urged the government to build on that stability through trade facilitation, digital and labour reforms aimed at attracting investment and supporting growth."
