    "md5": "8fae03e740a76c2e68c3da9030fcf23c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1635,
    "chunk_text": "This applies to three-wheeler drivers and bus drivers as well. The Ella-Wellawaya bus accident in September 2025 claimed the lives of 16 people while injuring 18 others. In June this year, a head-on private bus collision in Lunugamwehera injured 15 people. On September 19, a road accident claimed the life of the Dambulla National School principal.\n\nRecords indicate that people between 15-45 years of age are more vulnerable to road accidents. This in other words is the working population. Sometimes it could be the sole breadwinner of a family. Sometimes they may die or they may be disabled their entire life adding more responsibilities to their spouses and children. If the injured individual has no guardian or caretaker, then it becomes another issue altogether.\n\nIn terms of the healthcare strain around 50% of patients are admitted to Intensive Care Units (ICUs). It is a known fact that sometimes there is a waiting list to obtain a bed at hospital ICUs due to the spike in admissions for various other illnesses as well. In terms of treatment costs, treating complex trauma injuries and fractures require specialised surgical plates or sutures. Medical experts opine that this costs up to ten times more than managing chronic medical conditions like diabetes or hypertension.\n\nAnother observation by medical experts and those studying road accidents is the lack of provision of helmets for children. In most instances, children who travel in motorcycles do not wear helmets and in case of an unfortunate incident, the child\u2019s life is at risk. Therefore the need for a behavioural and attitudinal shift has been observed."
