    "md5": "f1ee5c56499a3def23db3ad4c94b2045",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1915,
    "chunk_text": "The Court also paid special attention to a video recording contained in a pen drive, which was produced before the Court by the prosecution.\n\nIt was revealed before the Court that eight persons, including Zahran, were present in the relevant video recording and that they had been clearly identified from the footage.\n\nIt was also revealed before Court that, in the relevant video recording, they had stated that they would take revenge for incidents that had happened to Muslims in Sri Lanka, that they were coming with bombs, that they would do this the following day and that they were coming smiling.\n\nThe Court revealed that the video had been recorded between around 1.30 p.m. on April 20, 2019, the day before the attacks that took place on April 21, 2019.\n\nIt was also revealed before the Court that the persons in the video contained in the relevant pen drive had made a pledge of allegiance while an ISIS flag was present.\n\nThe prpresident of the Trial-at-Bar further explained to the Court that one person was seen holding a T-56 firearm while another person was holding a sword.\n\nIt was revealed that the video had been recorded in the Mount Lavinia \u201cSpam Tower\u201d area.\n\nThereafter, Counsel Anil Maddumage, appearing for accused Nos. 2, 7, 8, 10, 15, 18 and 19, requested the Court to impose lenient sentences on the accused.\n\n\"All these accused have been in prison for approximately seven and a half years. During this period, they have also lost their freedom.\n\nWe also do not want something like what happened on April 21, 2019, to happen again. Therefore, considering these facts, I request Your honor to impose lenient sentences.\u201d\n\nThe first accused, Mohamed Ibrahim Mohamed Naufer alias Naufer Moulavi, stated that according to the teachings of Islam, it was not appropriate to make requests from authorities. Therefore, he said that he would accept any sentencing order imposed by the Court."
  },
  {
