    "chunk_size_bytes": 1085,
    "chunk_text": "Urgent treatment begins for \u2018Kavantissa\u2019 elephant in Galgamuwa\n\nColombo, Sep. 24 (Daily Mirror) - Urgent veterinary treatment has commenced for \u2018Kavantissa\u2019, the elephant roaming in the Galgamuwa area, following an operation carried out by a special team of the Department of Wildlife Conservation this morning.\n\nThe treatment was launched near the Usgala Siyabalangamuwa Lake, where the elephant has been roaming, under the direction of Nikaweratiya Veterinary Officer Pubudu.\n\nThe operation is being carried out under the guidance of Director of Veterinary Medicine Dr. Ganga and Veterinary Officer Isuru, with the intervention of Environment Minister Dhammika Patabendi and the Ministry Secretary.\n\nVeterinarians and wildlife officers from the Department of Wildlife Conservation, together with a special medical team, are providing the necessary treatment based on the elephant\u2019s current condition.\n\nThe veterinary teams are continuing to monitor Kavantissa closely, while all necessary measures are being taken to safeguard the elephant\u2019s health and ensure its safety."
