    "chunk_text": "Vijitha Herath to address UN General Assembly on September 28\n\nColombo, Sep. 24 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka\u2019s Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Minister Vijitha Herath is scheduled to travel to New York on September 26 to represent Sri Lanka at the 81st United Nations General Assembly and deliver the country\u2019s national statement on September 28.\n\nThe 81st session of the UN General Assembly opened on September 8, while its High-Level Week and General Debate are being held from September 22 to 28 in New York. The session is being conducted under the theme, \u201cRestoring Trust, Managing Transformation: A United Nations That Delivers for All.\u201d\n\nThe General Debate is taking place against a backdrop of ongoing conflicts, humanitarian crises, climate change, widening inequalities and growing concerns over the effectiveness of the multilateral system. The UN programme also places emphasis on sustainable development, sea-level rise, pandemic preparedness, nuclear disarmament, human rights and the governance of emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence.\n\nMinister Herath\u2019s address on September 28 will provide an opportunity for Sri Lanka to present its position on key international issues and outline its foreign policy priorities at the global forum.\n\nAhead of the General Assembly, Herath met with UN Resident Coordinator in Sri Lanka Marc-Andr\u00e9 Franche on September 7 to discuss matters relating to the upcoming session and Sri Lanka\u2019s priorities. The discussions also covered Sri Lanka\u2019s more than 70-year partnership with the UN, the UN80 process, the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework and the country\u2019s Third Voluntary National Review on the Sustainable Development Goals.\n\nThe visit is also expected to provide opportunities for Sri Lanka to engage with foreign ministers and senior UN officials through bilateral and multilateral meetings on issues of mutual interest."
