    "chunk_size_bytes": 1978,
    "chunk_text": "Justice must be accessible to all without discrimination: PM\n\nColombo, Sep. 24 (Daily Mirror) - Justice must be accessible to all without discrimination, while establishing the rule of law and ensuring equal access to justice remain among the Government\u2019s key commitments, Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya said today.\n\nAddressing Parliament today (24), the Prime Minister said the proposed constitutional amendment on the judiciary should be considered as part of a broader programme to strengthen the justice system.\n\nShe stressed that improving access to justice could not be achieved through a single constitutional amendment or by reforming one institution alone, but required comprehensive reforms across the justice system.\n\nThe Prime Minister said steps had been taken over the past two years to strengthen independent investigations and improve the capacity of the Police and Criminal Investigation Department (CID) to conduct investigations fairly and impartially. Measures had also been introduced to improve impartiality in recruitment, promotions and appointments.\n\nShe said the Government was also working to improve the efficiency of the justice system by filling vacancies, increasing opportunities for hearings, directing resources towards courts with heavy caseloads, introducing technological support and providing additional staff.\n\nThe Government Analyst\u2019s Department, which has faced longstanding vacancies contributing to delays in investigations, was also being strengthened, she said.\n\nAccording to the Prime Minister, the proposed constitutional amendment would allow Courts of Appeal to be established in provinces where necessary, thereby improving access to justice for people outside Colombo.\n\nShe said delays in justice had affected the lives of ordinary citizens while also benefiting an elite, as prolonged investigations and legal proceedings had contributed to a cycle in which accountability was weakened whenever governments changed."
  },
