    "chunk_size_bytes": 1994,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka, UAE discuss Trincomalee regional energy hub\n\nColombo, Sep. 24 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka and the United Arab Emirates have discussed the ongoing UAE-India-Sri Lanka tripartite initiative to develop Trincomalee as a regional energy hub, during a meeting between UAE Ambassador to Sri Lanka Khaled Nasser Al Ameri and Deputy Speaker of Parliament Dr. Rizvie Salih.\n\nThe Ambassador paid a courtesy call on the Deputy Speaker at Parliament on September 23, with the discussions focusing on further strengthening bilateral relations and cooperation between the two countries.\n\nThe Deputy Speaker highlighted the longstanding and cordial relations between Sri Lanka and the UAE and expressed appreciation for the UAE\u2019s support to Sri Lanka, particularly the economic contribution of the large Sri Lankan workforce employed in the UAE.\n\nHe also welcomed the increasing number of tourists travelling from the UAE to Sri Lanka and stressed the importance of further strengthening cooperation in the tourism sector.\n\nThe Deputy Speaker said the Sri Lanka-UAE Parliamentary Friendship Association is expected to be revived in the Tenth Parliament, with the aim of strengthening parliamentary relations and expanding cooperation across various sectors.\n\nAmbassador Al Ameri praised the contribution of Sri Lankan workers to the economies of both countries, noting that Sri Lankan workers in the UAE are highly valued for being skilled, peaceful and respectful.\n\nHe also highlighted the strong trade relations between Sri Lanka and the UAE and stressed the importance of maintaining strong air connectivity between the two countries.\n\nThe discussions further focused on enhancing cooperation in education and higher education, as well as opportunities to strengthen cooperation in security.\n\nThe Ambassador also commended Sri Lanka\u2019s natural beauty, cultural richness and the hospitality of its people, and reaffirmed the UAE\u2019s continued support for Sri Lanka as a close and trusted friend."
