    "chunk_size_bytes": 1714,
    "chunk_text": "Fake website misuses Foreign Bureau name to collect job seekers\u2019 personal data\n\nColombo, Sep. 24 (Daily Mirror) - The Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment (SLBFE) has warned the public about a fake website that is illegally using the Bureau\u2019s name, official logo and photographs to collect personal information from people seeking employment opportunities in Israel.\n\nThe Bureau said the fraudulent website is being circulated through social media and is designed to make users believe that it is an official SLBFE website or an authorised online recruitment process offering free job opportunities in Israel.\n\nAccording to the Bureau, those who access the fake link are directed to an online application form requesting sensitive personal details, including their full name, date of birth, National Identity Card (NIC) number, gender and mobile phone number.\n\nThe SLBFE warned that providing such information through an unauthorised website could expose individuals to risks including phishing, identity theft, impersonation, fraudulent data collection, social engineering and misuse of personal information.\n\nThe Bureau said the scam appears to particularly target young people seeking employment opportunities in Israel.\n\nIt urged the public, especially Israeli job seekers, not to provide personal information through suspicious websites, links or online application forms.\n\nThe SLBFE has already lodged a complaint with the Sri Lanka Computer Emergency Readiness Team (CERT) regarding the fraudulent activity, while further action is being taken.\n\nThe Bureau advised the public to rely only on information officially issued by the SLBFE when seeking information about employment opportunities in Israel."
  },
