    "md5": "0a7448453deb36a26ba5770559fd6629",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1951,
    "chunk_text": "PickMe connects Book Fair visits with QR tickets, rides and easier pickups\n\nDigital ticketing, dedicated pickup facilities and a free Borella\u2013BMICH shuttle bring greater convenience to the Colombo International Book Fair\n\nFrom buying an entry ticket to finding a ride home with bags full of books, PickMe is bringing together digital ticketing, transport and on-site assistance to make visits to the Colombo International Book Fair 2026 more convenient.\n\nVisitors can purchase their Book Fair tickets through PickMe Explore and present the QR code at designated entry counters at the BMICH. Through PickMe\u2019s unified digital platform (PickMe Explore, Flash, and Rentals), visitors unlock an end-to-end event experience, connecting e-ticketing, dynamic transit routing, and vendor logistics in a single app interface\n\nA key addition this year is a dedicated vehicle waiting area at Gate 3, at the BMICH supported by on-site assistance to guide visitors to the pickup point and help them arrange rides. The facility addresses one of the most familiar challenges at the popular annual event: finding a vehicle and meeting the driver amid crowded exits and busy surrounding roads. The Fair, which runs from 25 September to 4 October at the BMICH, brings together readers, students, families, publishers and booksellers from across the country.\n\nPickMe CEO Jiffry Zulfer said the company\u2019s focus was on making the different parts of a Book Fair visit work together more smoothly. \u201cFor visitors, the experience begins before they reach the BMICH and continues until they get home. Being able to buy an entry ticket through PickMe, use a QR code to enter the fair and arrange transport through the same app brings greater convenience to that entire journey. This year, we are strengthening that experience with a dedicated pickup arrangement at Gate 3, making it easier for visitors and drivers to find each other when it is time to leave,\u201d he said."
  },
