    "md5": "dded2c20a66743bc85e8094a12d8eb9e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1555,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cAfter spending time browsing and buying books, visitors may be leaving with several bags, children or elderly family members. A clearly identified pickup point, with support on the field available to guide them, can make a meaningful difference. It also helps the drivers registered on the PickMe app collect passengers with greater ease,\u201d Zulfer said.\n\nA dedicated PickMe stall will provide assistance with the app, ride bookings and information about the company\u2019s services. Those interested in earning through the platform will also be able to enquire about registering on the PickMe app and receive assistance.\n\nPublishers, booksellers and other vendors will have access to special savings across PickMe Flash, Truck and Rentals, supporting the movement of books, displays and other materials before, during and after the event.\n\nThe partnership brings PickMe\u2019s Colombo Connect initiative to one of the city\u2019s most popular annual gatherings. By linking ticketing, travel, improving visitors\u2019 experience and vendor logistics, it demonstrates how the city\u2019s events can become more accessible and convenient for the people and businesses taking part.\n\n\u201cThe Book Fair is an important meeting place for readers, writers, publishers and families. Through Colombo Connect and PickMe Explore, we want to help people enjoy more of what the city offers by making the practical arrangements easier. At the Book Fair, that means bringing admission, mobility and support together so visitors can spend more time discovering books,\u201d Zulfer added."
