    "chunk_size_bytes": 1831,
    "chunk_text": "SL and China will further advance strategic cooperative partnership: Ambassador Wei\n\nSri Lanka and China next year will celebrate 70th anniversary of establishment of diplomatic ties and the 75th anniversary of the signing of the Rubber-Rice Pact\n\nThe new Ambassador of the People\u2019s Republic of China Wei Huaxiang on Wednesday stressed that no matter how the international situation evolves, China and Sri Lanka always remain true friends and good partners, standing together through thick and thin and placing trust in each other.\n\nHe made the assertion in his remarks at the reception to mark the 77th anniversary of the founding of the People\u2019s Republic of China at the Shangri-La Hotel, Colombo.\n\nThe Ambassador said next year Sri Lanka and China will celebrate the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and Sri Lanka and the 75th anniversary of the signing of the Rubber-Rice Pact.\n\n\u201cIn advancing China-Sri Lanka relations in the new era, we need to carry forward our traditions while breaking new ground, and uphold fundamental principles while making innovations,\u201d Ambassador Wei told the ceremony at which the Sri Lankan Government was represented by Power and Energy Minister Anura Karunathilaka. A host of Government Ministers, MPs, Opposition Leaders, past and present, ambassadors, professionals and business leaders were also present.\n\nWei assured that China stands ready to work with Sri Lanka to continue carrying forward the spirit of independence, self-reliance, solidarity and mutual assistance enshrined in the Rubber-Rice Pact, uphold the principles of \u2018mutual respect, fairness and justice\u2019, eliminate interference and meet challenges together, and implement the important common understandings reached by the leaders of our two countries with a pragmatic approach."
  },
