    "chunk_text": "Ambeon Capital with Chennai firm to open India-SL investment desks\n\nAmbeon Capital PLC, the Colombo Stock Exchange-listed investment holding company, has signed a memorandum of understanding with Sincere Syndication and Corporate Services LLP and Avyukthi Consulting & Advisory Services LLP to establish collaborative investment desks in Colombo and Chennai.\n\nThe arrangement is designed to channel cross-border capital between Sri Lanka and India across listed equities, private equity and credit, real estate and fixed income, while also supporting mergers and acquisitions and business partnerships.\n\nThe parties intend the desks to act as dedicated points of contact for deal origination, preliminary screening, research coordination, investor introductions and co-investment or referral opportunities.\n\nThe Colombo desk will be hosted by Ambeon (or an affiliate), with a primary focus on facilitating investment into India and other agreed markets, while also originating Sri Lankan opportunities.\n\nThe Chennai desk will be hosted by Sincere Syndication, with Avyukthi providing tax, regulatory, structuring, diligence and transaction-support capabilities.\n\nIn parallel, Ambeon is working with the partners on the launch of a dedicated Sri Lanka fund focused on Sri Lankan companies, structured in partnership with Sincere Syndication\u2019s Bharat Transformation Fund.\n\nThe Bharat Transformation Fund is Sincere Syndication\u2019s flagship pre-IPO and early post-IPO vehicle targeting transformative Indian businesses in sectors aligned with national growth priorities, including advanced manufacturing, defence and aerospace, deep technology, specialty healthcare and medical devices.\n\nThe Sri Lanka fund is intended to create a structured channel for capital into listed and private Sri Lankan companies, leveraging complementary deal flow, research and investor networks on both sides of the Palk Strait."
  },
