    "chunk_size_bytes": 1529,
    "chunk_text": "Introduced in 2015 and endorsed by the Ministry of Agriculture, Govi Mithuru began as a mobile-based agricultural advisory service and was enhanced with AI capabilities in 2025, evolving into Sri Lanka\u2019s first AI-powered agriculture platform. Today, it provides cultivation guidance, weather updates, crop information, market prices, AI-powered chat and voice assistance, pest and disease identification, and agricultural expertise in Sinhala, Tamil and English. The platform can be accessed via the Govi Mithuru app, by dialling 616, or through govimithuru.lk.\n\nPowered by Dialog 5G Ultra, with over 1,000 live 5G sites across all 25 districts, the solution enables real-time transmission of field imagery, live video and AI-generated crop health insights, supporting remote monitoring and data-driven agricultural practices.\n\nOrganised by the Faculty of Agriculture, University of Ruhuna, ISAE 2026 was held under the theme \u201cData-Driven Green Agriculture Transition: From Healthy Soils to Healthy People,\u201d bringing together local and international stakeholders to explore emerging challenges and opportunities across agriculture, sustainability and innovation.\n\nThe presence of Hon. K.D. Lalkantha, Minister of Agriculture, Livestock, Land and Irrigation, at ISAE 2026 further highlighted the growing role of technology in supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s agriculture sector. The collaboration builds on Govi Mithuru\u2019s journey, extending Dialog\u2019s use of AI and connectivity to support knowledge-driven agricultural solutions."
  },
