    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "66d74c3dd7c16bbc38b6bd73165b4a20",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1891,
    "chunk_text": "HNB Bank\u2019s Central Collections Unit receives ISO 9001:2015 Certification\n\nHNB, Senior Manager \u2013 Central Collections, Arjuna Damunupola; HNB, Vice President \u2013 Recoveries, Sampath Vithana; HNB, MD/CEO, Damith Pallewatte; and Bureau Veritas, Country General Manager, Shan Nanayakkara, sharing the MoU alongside representatives from both organisations\n\nHNB PLC has secured ISO 9001:2015 Quality Management System certification for its Central Collections Unit (CCU), covering debt collection and recovery activities within personal financial services. The certification was issued by Bureau Veritas Lanka following an assessment of the unit\u2019s processes, controls and service standards.\n\nThe certification confirms that the CCU\u2019s recovery processes meet an internationally recognized quality standard, covering how the unit engages customers, documents cases and manages recovery timelines. It applies specifically to collections and recovery activities within personal financial services, an area where HNB has aligned its recovery practices with regulatory expectations and customer protection standards.\n\nHNB Senior Manager - Central Collections, Arjuna Damunupola said, \u201cThis certification confirms that our processes meet an internationally recognized standard and gives customers a clear, consistent experience when their accounts are being managed for Collections. It also gives us a structured basis to keep improving how we handle cases, from documentation through to resolution.\u201d\n\nUnder the ISO framework, the CCU applies a risk-based approach to segment accounts by delinquency stage and route them to the appropriate recovery path, from early reminders to structured repayment plans, before any escalation. This supports HNB PLC\u2019s efforts to resolve under-performing and non-performing accounts through documented repayment agreements while managing impairment levels."
  },
