    "md5": "6028f51edaf48bf2cb2eb7e149acdfd0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1668,
    "chunk_text": "Jetwing Travels adopts new-energy mobility solution with Hayleys tie-up\n\nMohan Pandithage, Chairman & Chief Executive of Hayleys PLC, and Shiromal Cooray, Chairman and Managing Director of Jetwing Travels (Private) Limited, together with representatives of Hayleys Mobility, Jetwing Travels and Jetwing Journeys, at the handover of 21 JAECOO J7 Plug-in Hybrid Electric Vehicles\n\nAs Sri Lanka strengthens its position as a responsible tourism destination, Hayleys Mobility Limited and Jetwing Travels are advancing a more sustainable approach to travel across the island through the adoption of new-energy mobility solutions.\n\nThe initiative reflects a shared commitment to reducing the environmental impact of ground transportation, an essential yet often overlooked part of the tourism experience, while maintaining the comfort, reliability and service standards expected by local and international travellers.\n\nShiromal Cooray, Chairman and Managing Director of Jetwing Travels stated, \u201cThis investment is part of our continued effort to make responsible travel more tangible across every stage of the guest journey. By introducing plug-in hybrid technology to our fleet, we are taking a practical step towards reducing the environmental impact of ground transportation, while continuing to deliver the comfort, reliability and flexibility our guests expect when travelling across\n\nAs part of this transition, Hayleys Mobility has delivered 21 JAECOO J7 Plug-in Hybrid Electric Vehicles (PHEVs) to Jetwing Travels. The vehicles will be deployed across Jetwing Travels and Jetwing Journeys for airport transfers, excursions and extended tours throughout the island."
