    "chunk_text": "Auction offerings fall to two-year low of 4.8 M/Kgs\n\nAuction offerings totalled 4.8 M/Kgs and the lowest quantity on offer since Sale No. 16 of\u00a0 22/24 April 2024 (4.7 M/Kgs). Overall market sentiment remained fairly similar to the previous week, notwithstanding a much smaller volume on offer.\n\nEx-Estate offerings comprised of 0.6 M/Kgs, down from the 0.7 M/Kgs on offer the previous week. A selection of the better teas continued to sell well although select high prices of last week were not maintained.\n\nBetter Westerns continued to command a premium over the fair average quality teas. Nuwara Eliya BOP/BOPF\u2019s continued sluggish together with the Uda Pussellawas\u2019 which sold poorly following quality. Uva\u2019s \u2013 Better BOP\u2019s which had limited availability appreciated by up to Rs. 50 per kg, whilst the corresponding BOPF\u2019s declined by a similar margin.\n\nHigh & Mid Grown CTC teas \u2013 Overall improved market outlook and a Rs. 20-40 per kg appreciation in prices, particularly for the better teas. Low Growns continued to sell well although the Select Best declined by Rs. 20 per kg.\n\nLiquoring teas lacked the support of the Western markets, perhaps due to the limited availability of better teas, whilst shippers to Japan, China, the Middle East and the CIS continued to dominate the sale.\n\nLow Growns totalled approximately 2.2 M/Kgs. Fair demand was witnessed in the Leafy, Semi-Leafy and Tippy categories, whilst the Premium category met with good demand.\n\nIn the Leafy and Semi-Leafy catalogues, well-made BOP1\u2019s were firm, whilst the balance were easier. Select Best OP1\u2019s together with the Below Best and teas at the bottom sold around last levels, whilst the Best varieties were lower. OP/OPA\u2019s, in general, declined. Select Best and Best PEK\u2019s were selectively dearer, whilst the balance together with the mixed/open varieties were easier. Teas at the bottom and the PEK1\u2019s, in general, were firm."
