    "md5": "c7799b3a2fda8a3f966117574863195b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1918,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cThere was a huge opportunity for Sri Lanka when companies like HCL came here, and there were other companies looking at Sri Lanka. We then put a tax on it and they kind of slowed down in terms of the number of desks,\u201d he pointed out, adding that the matter needs to be negotiated with the IMF.\n\nEven so, ICT and BPM export revenue rose 8.8 percent to US$ 1,645 million in 2025, as per Export Development Board (EDB) data. It grew a further 17.63 percent year-on-year to US$ 885.42 million in the first half of 2026, though Thewarathanthri\u2019s remarks suggest the growth has yet to translate into jobs on the scale needed.\n\nBeyond taxation, he insisted that Sri Lanka would struggle to capture such investment without the supporting infrastructure in place.\n\n\u201cIf you don\u2019t bring the National Single Window for trade and things like that, on the trade treaties with China and India, we will have significant challenges capturing that opportunity,\u201d he cautioned.\n\nFellow panellist and DFCC Bank Director/Chief Executive Officer Thimal Perera noted that young entrepreneurs face a parallel barrier in accessing finance. He urged banks to move from collateralised lending towards cash flow-based lending, and pointed to opportunities in fintech, agritech and pharmatech.\n\n\u201cIf you look at a start-up today, they\u2019ll find it impossible to walk into a bank and get a facility,\u201d Perera stressed.\n\nAdvocata Institute Chief Executive Officer Dhananath Fernando placed the graduate problem within a broader demographic shift, estimating that around 1.8 million young people would join the labour force in the coming years. That is roughly one and a half times the 1.18 million public sector employees recorded by the DCS in the first quarter of 2026.\n\n\u201cThere\u2019s about 1.8 million youth joining the labour force in the next few years. 1.8 million compared to our population, that\u2019s massive,\u201d Fernando warned."
  },
