    "md5": "789c8e5ddfaf4ba7c3994b0e552a392b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 785,
    "chunk_text": "Sarana Gunawardena\u2019s wife arrested over Rs. 50,000 bribe\n\nColombo, Sep. 25 (Daily Mirror) - The Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption (CIABOC) has arrested Chinari Lakmanthi Hettiarachchi, the wife of former Deputy Minister Sarana Gunawardena, over an alleged attempt to influence ongoing court proceedings involving her husband.\n\nAccording to CIABOC, Hettiarachchi allegedly offered a Rs. 50,000 bribe to an office assistant attached to Colombo High Court No. 11.\n\nThe alleged bribe was offered in an attempt to influence the proceedings in a case currently being heard against the former Deputy Minister and to secure a suspended prison sentence, according to the allegations.\n\nShe is scheduled to be produced before the Colombo Chief Magistrate\u2019s Court."
