    "chunk_size_bytes": 1079,
    "chunk_text": "Further, reduced physical activity can increase the risk of overweight and obesity and contribute to non-communicable diseases such as diabetes, high blood pressure and heart diseases later in life, she said.\n\nShe also identified eye-related problems as another possible concern associated with excessive screen exposure among young children.\n\nThe survey has now formed the baseline for a new social and behaviour change communication programme under the Health Promotion Bureau\u2019s National Preschool Health Promotion Programme. Dr Wickramasinghe said the programme aims to improve eight key health behaviours among preschool children and their caregivers, including parents, teachers and other family members, with reduced screen time identified as one of the eight behaviours requiring attention. She further added that parents and caregivers are encouraged to provide children with toys, storybooks and other age-appropriate activities to keep them engaged and entertained without relying on screens, while spending more time playing and interacting with children themselves."
