    "md5": "6b0b5685cd24b525a641ae6ae62fc1f0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2028,
    "chunk_text": "Deciphering NPP\u2019s mandate\n\nTo govern sustainably, the NPP must respect the nuances of this mandate. Treat the supermajority not as a blank check from a unified populace, but as a fragile window of opportunity granted by an electorate waiting to see if the rhetoric of change can survive the reality of governance.\n\nOn moral issues there can be no left or right.\u00a0 It is either right or wrong\n\n\u201cAll power is trust, and we are accountable for its exercise; from the people, and for the people, all springs, and all must return.\u201d \u2014 Benjamin Disraeli\n\nPresident AKD is attuned to the rhythm of the universe. He has pronounced that only a group better than the NPP would be trusted by people to replace the NPP, come next elections. On 23 September President AKD completed two years in office. Two years in office President AKD\u00a0 remains committed to a Social Contract of State Accountability and Good Governance.\n\nHis reading of power is in sharp contrast to his Agriculture Minister K.D. Lal Kantha who speaks of refashioning the state apparatus as a mirror image of the party in power.\n\nThroughout history, the fleeting nature of political authority has been captured by philosophers, leaders, and writers. \u2018Political Power is like a wave of the sea; it rises, it reaches its crest, and then it breaks and disappears.\u2019\n\nThis missive is intended to provoke a closer look at the shifting political landscape and discover what lies ahead.\n\nParliamentary election of 14 November, 2024, resulted in an unprecedented political milestone in the history of representative governance since Independence.\n\nThe Election of President AKD and parliamentary elections that followed ended a happy era of \u2018politics as usual\u2019 where rival political parties assumed that periodic elections ensured continuity of unabashed patron-client politics.\n\nThe NPP led by President AKD promised \u2018reform and a renaissance\u2019. Together President AKD and the NPP, secured a historic two-thirds supermajority. They captured 159 out of 225 seats."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
