    "language": "en",
    "md5": "04ae86c587072971af601073d1953232",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2029,
    "chunk_text": "The Election of President AKD and parliamentary elections that followed ended a happy era of \u2018politics as usual\u2019 where rival political parties assumed that periodic elections ensured continuity of unabashed patron-client politics.\n\nThe NPP led by President AKD promised \u2018reform and a renaissance\u2019. Together President AKD and the NPP, secured a historic two-thirds supermajority. They captured 159 out of 225 seats.\n\nUnder our complex system of deciding proportional representation in vote counting, assigning\u00a0 \u00a0bonus seats, a single-party\u2019s supermajority was historically deemed possible but nearly impossible.\n\nWhen the NPP achieved the impossible, this computed system arrived at a landslide for the NPP.\n\nThey seized it as an ostensible mandate for radical systemic change. Veteran JVP ideologue Bimal Ratnayake deemed it as a People\u2019s collective crossing of the Rubicon!\n\nHe should brush up on his Shakespeare. Crossing the Rubicon is a momentous moment. Even Caesar spurred his horse with his historic epigram \u2018Let the dice fall.\u2019\n\nDazed by the rapid shift in fortunes, the defeated political factions appear to be sleepwalking through the political landscape.\n\nThe recent JRJ commemoration, which saw SP and RW pledge unity and collective resolve, exposed the profound hypocrisy embedded within the Grand Old Party and its prodigal offshoot.\n\nIndeed, JRJ opened the economy. Under his watch the 1983 pogrom unfolded. A Separatist war intensified in the north. We watched another uprising in the south.\n\nIn response the State Apparatus was made an instrument of terror. Under his successor Ranasinghe Premadasa systemic abuse of power reached proverbial proportions.\n\nUnder the Common Man\u2019s President R. Premadasa, the national carrier AirLanka ordered two Airbus A320 narrowbody jets and five Airbus A340-300 widebody jets.\n\nThe CBK administration reduced the order. It was a different time and a different world. Airbus Industries, a consortium of several European Countries, was competing with Boeing."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-25-dailyftlk-0a58c202",
    "num": "dailyftlk-0a58c202",
    "date_str": "2026-09-25",
    "description": "Deciphering NPP\u2019s mandate",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/columns/Deciphering-NPP-s-mandate/4-797770",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
