    "md5": "0143e5cb8e3fd475fbd3aa8b98591b45",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1910,
    "chunk_text": "Under the Common Man\u2019s President R. Premadasa, the national carrier AirLanka ordered two Airbus A320 narrowbody jets and five Airbus A340-300 widebody jets.\n\nThe CBK administration reduced the order. It was a different time and a different world. Airbus Industries, a consortium of several European Countries, was competing with Boeing.\n\nCrawling back out of an abyss is no easy task. The NPP victory passed the torch to a new generation of mostly monolingual yet politically savvy activists.\n\nThe parliamentary election despite its quirks in the form of national list members of Opposition groups decisively finalised the collapse of traditional political dynasties and crony networks.\n\nMost notably the Sri Lanka Podujana Peramuna (SLPP) the Rajapakse Family\u2019s political machine was reduced to near oblivion.\n\nHowever, beneath the surface of this historic victory lies a complex electoral reality.\n\nRather than indicating an absolute consensus across the population, the NPP\u2019s supermajority was heavily amplified by opposition voter fatigue, strategic fragmentation, and the collapse of the traditional base of clientelist politics that greased successive governments since Independence.\n\nIf the NPP assumes that their parliamentary dominance equates to a permanent, rock-solid nationwide consensus, it would be a dangerous political miscalculation.\n\nStrange math of calculating proportionality and voter turnout accounts for the NPP\u2019s super majority.\n\nA nuanced analysis of the data reveals that the NPP\u2019s leap from a 42.31% vote share in the September Presidential election to a 61.56% vote share in the November Parliamentary election was not solely driven by a massive influx of new converts.\n\nInstead, a major catalyst was the collapse of the voter bases of Sajith Premadasa, Ranil Wickremesinghe and of course Mahinda Rajapakse. Politics as usual has ended with the election of President AKD."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-25-dailyftlk-0a58c202",
