    "language": "en",
    "md5": "ba9cb60f4b64d0bb570015a6f79f0f36",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1780,
    "chunk_text": "Instead, a major catalyst was the collapse of the voter bases of Sajith Premadasa, Ranil Wickremesinghe and of course Mahinda Rajapakse. Politics as usual has ended with the election of President AKD.\n\nJust two months later, the SJB\u2019s raw vote count plummeted drastically to just 1,968,716 votes (17.66%), while Wickremesinghe led New Democratic Front (NDF) managed only 500,835 votes (4.49%)\n\nThis steep decline highlights a critical phenomenon: a vast portion of the electorate that voted against President AKD in September chose to stay home in November.\n\nDemoralised by the presidential defeat and foreseeing a similar setback as a foregone conclusion, those voters who opposed the AKD candidacy defected via non-participation.\n\nBecause the proportional representation system allocates seats based on the percentage of ballots cast, this selective apathy artificially inflated the NPP\u2019s seat conversion rate, granting them 70% of parliamentary seats on roughly 61% of the vote.\n\nA disorganised Opposition must not be mistaken for a permanent expansion of the NPP\u2019s ideological base. The collapse of the SLPP to a meagre 3.14% and the division of centrist voter base between the SJB and NDF left a vacuum that the NPP easily swept through.\n\nThe last parliamentary election was a \u201crejection of the old guard\u201d and a conditional \u201cacceptance of the new.\u201d\n\nThe NPP masterfully exploited post-Aragalaya anti-corruption sentiments and the desire to break free from the ruling elites accumulated folly that culminated with the 2022 economic crisis and sovereign default.\n\nHowever, a significant portion of their parliamentary support is a \u201cprotest vote\u201d rather than a deeply rooted ideological alignment with any left-leaning socioeconomic policies. The NPP knows it."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-25-dailyftlk-0a58c202",
    "num": "dailyftlk-0a58c202",
    "date_str": "2026-09-25",
    "description": "Deciphering NPP\u2019s mandate",
