    "md5": "844540ed63d11c992eaff8dd32f66960",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1015,
    "chunk_text": "That record remains largely unwritten. And here lies the acid test. The NPP was elected because Sri Lankans wanted to smash an odious system. Its greatest achievement so far has instead been learning to operate that system without immediately wrecking it.\n\nIf it builds institutions capable of constraining NPP governments as effectively as any other government, then something genuinely fundamental will have changed.\n\nIf it merely replaces the people operating the old machinery, then \u2018system change\u2019 will eventually reveal itself to have been little more than system succession.\n\nThe proposed judicial changes make that question particularly urgent. The NPP still has time.\n\nWhat it does with the extraordinary power Sri Lanka gave it will determine whether these first two years become merely the prologue to system change, or the beginning of another turn of the political wheel.\n\n(The writer is the Editor-at-large of LMD and is a senior journalist with a Post-graduate Diploma in Politics and Governance)"
