    "md5": "152f77778e0c4ab36d18264796237e0d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1811,
    "chunk_text": "BASL and WNPS sign MoU to strengthen environmental protection and enforcement\n\nBASL President Rajeev Amarasuriya (left) and WNPS General Secretary Rapti Dirckze with the MoU signed between the two organisations.\u00a0 Others from left Nethmi Silva AAL, Suranee Samarasekara, Charaka Jayaratne AAL, Revan Weerasinghe AAL, Yohan Cooray AAL and Sachini Boraluwa AAL\n\nThe Bar Association of Sri Lanka (BASL) and the Wildlife and Nature Protection Society (WNPS) being Sri Lanka\u2019s oldest environmental conservation organisation have entered into a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) to establish a framework for cooperation aimed at enhancing the enforcement of environmental law and promoting the protection and conservation of Sri Lanka\u2019s natural resources.\n\nThe MOU was signed on behalf of the BASL by its President Rajeev Amarasuriya, and Secretary Nalin De Silva, and on behalf of the WNPS by its President Graham Marshall, and Secretary Rapti Dirckze.\n\nThrough this partnership, the two organisations will work together to increase awareness and education among lawyers on environmental law, encourage greater interest in environmental legal practice, and enhance understanding of environmental challenges facing the country.\n\nThe collaboration will include a range of initiatives, including orientation programs and workshops for lawyers, webinars on environmental issues, engagement with the Junior Bar, support for litigation involving significant environmental and wildlife matters, and regional awareness programs aimed at promoting environmental rights and responsibilities.\n\nThe MOU also provides for cooperation in responding to wildlife crimes, environmental incidents, and nationally significant environmental issues through legal guidance, professional support, and liaison with relevant authorities."
