    "chunk_size_bytes": 1850,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka and Indonesia conclude inaugural political consultations opening new chapter of bilateral ties\n\nYear-round activities planned in 2027 to mark 75th anniversary of diplomatic relations\n\nSri Lanka reiterates request for support of Indonesian side for bid to obtain ASEAN Sectoral Dialogue Partnership status and to accede to Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership\n\nThe inaugural round of Political Consultations between the Ministries of Foreign Affairs of Sri Lanka and the Republic of Indonesia was held on 22 September 2026 in Colombo, marking a significant milestone in the longstanding and friendly relations between the two countries.\n\nThe Consultations commenced with the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU), establishing a formal framework for regular bilateral dialogue and enhanced cooperation between the two Ministries. The MoU reaffirms commitment of both sides to elevate engagement and strengthen institutional ties in key areas of shared interest.\n\nThe Sri Lankan delegation was led by Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Ministry Secretary Aruni Ranaraja, while the Indonesian delegation was headed by Deputy Minister for Asia-Pacific and African Affairs of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Indonesia, Dr. Santo Darmosumarto.\n\nForeign Secretary Ranaraja, in her opening remarks highlighted the enduring partnership between the two countries, recalling the foundational role both nations played in advancing major diplomatic initiatives most notably Non-Aligned Movement. Deputy Minister for Asia-Pacific and African Affairs Dr. Darmosumarto, in his response, welcomed the signing of the MoU as a structured framework for regular engagement and deepen cooperation between the two countries, while highlighting opportunities to expand collaboration across mutually beneficial areas."
  },
