    "chunk_size_bytes": 1994,
    "chunk_text": "Amana Bank strengthens footprint with 49th Self Banking Centre in Eravur Pattu\n\nOpening of the Eravur Pattu Self Banking Centre by Amana Bank\u2019s Assistant Vice President Arshad Adhnan (right) along with Eravur Pattu Pradeshiya Sabha Chairman\n\nM. Muralitharan, Eravur Pattu Pradeshiya Sabha Member A.S.M. Rasmi, and Eravur Branch Manager B.M. Mahir\n\nAmana Bank recently opened its 49th Self Banking Centre in Eravur Pattu, further strengthening the bank\u2019s presence in the region and bringing greater banking convenience to customers in the area. Strategically located at Meerakerny Road, Michnagar, Eravur, the new Self Banking Centre provides convenient 24x7 access for cash withdrawals, cash deposits and cheque deposits for individuals, businesses and the wider community in and around Eravur Pattu.\n\nWith this opening, Amana Bank\u2019s presence in the Eastern Province has expanded to 14 Self Banking Centres, complementing its nine fully fledged branches across the province.\n\nThe opening ceremony was attended by distinguished guests including Eravur Pattu Pradeshiyasaba Chairman M. Muralitharan, together with community leaders, business representatives, customers, and well-wishers from the area. Representing Amana Bank at the occasion were Assistant Vice President - SME and Regional Branches Arshad Adhnan, Head of Retail Sales and Acquisition Channels Mohamed Asmil, Manager \u2013 Offsite SBC Operations Imran Mohamed, Branch Manager Eravur Mahir Badurdeen,\u00a0 Branch Manager Kaduruwela Jiffry Razik, and other officials of the Bank.\n\nSpeaking at the event, Assistant Vice President \u2013 SME and Regional Branches Arshad Adhnan stated, \u201cThe opening of our 49th Self Banking Centre in Eravur Pattu marks another step in bringing convenient and accessible banking services closer to the communities we serve. With this facility, we aim to support the evolving banking needs of individuals and businesses in the region and strengthen our relationship with the people of Eravur Pattu.\u201d"
