    "md5": "cad80472f8367fe9a508f08129cbfe10",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1210,
    "chunk_text": "Whither UN  sanctity when Trump and Netanyahu take the podium?\n\nThe busiest week in the international political calendar turned out to be its most appalling.\n\nAs expected, Iran, Palestine, Yemen, Sudan, and Ukraine figured prominently during the ongoing debate, yet none expected the speakers to perform a miracle and spring a peace surprise that would end more than 50 wars happening around the world today. The sessions, as a matter of routine, simply offer world leaders an opportunity at the world\u2019s largest diplomatic forum to express their views on war, peace, and global concerns such as poverty, climate change, artificial intelligence, and nuclear proliferation.\n\nDecorum, however, demands that world leaders recognise the UN as a sanctum sanctorum, since it was established with the hallowed intention of preventing wars. Yet, world leaders have repeatedly desecrated its sanctity.\n\nWith fabrications and false narratives, Israel\u2019s Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has used the platform to demonise Iran and Palestinians to justify illegal wars, genocide, and annexations. On Thursday, he was once again using the UN platform to play victim and defend his crimes. It was the height of deception."
  },
