    "description": "Whither UN  sanctity when Trump and Netanyahu take the podium?",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/opinion/Whither-UN-sanctity-when-Trump-and-Netanyahu-take-the-podium/172-351189",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1790396656.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-26-dailymirrorlk-6766c835-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "efea3e19810f46c632d12ecc2534e738",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1792,
    "chunk_text": "With fabrications and false narratives, Israel\u2019s Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has used the platform to demonise Iran and Palestinians to justify illegal wars, genocide, and annexations. On Thursday, he was once again using the UN platform to play victim and defend his crimes. It was the height of deception.\n\nOn Iran, he was equally deceptive. Semantics can be satanic. Netanyahu was at his satanic best when he delivered his speech, which analysts say was also aimed at propping up his image during the ongoing election campaign, where the opposition has been flaying him over corruption allegations.\n\nThat is Netanyahu. Equally preposterous was Trump. He desecrated the pacifist forum on Tuesday and used it to threaten Iran, a nation of 92 million people, with annihilation. Unprecedentedly shocking, indeed.\n\nSurely, a leader of an English-speaking country must know the meaning of the word \u201cannihilation\u201d. According to the Merriam-Webster dictionary, \u201cannihilation\u201d means \u201cthe state or fact of being completely destroyed or obliterated: the act of annihilating something or the state of being annihilated.\u201d\n\nDoes Trump want to be counted among the wicked\u2014in the company of Adolf Hitler, Genghis Khan and Pol Pot? The America that its Founding Fathers envisioned does not. But that America has long been lost. In the context of modern warfare, annihilation cannot be carried out except with a nuclear weapon. If Trump is implying that he would nuke Iran, then it is the moral duty of Congress to stop him.\n\nTo be fair to Trump\u2014even though he is rarely fair to anyone, not even himself\u2014he qualified his outrageous statement. He said he would annihilate Iran if no deal was reached to end the war, while adding in the same breath that an agreement could come soon."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
