    "md5": "0c9773dfd84d068ff29c4da6a648a38a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1409,
    "chunk_text": "Trump claimed the talks US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner held with Araghchi made progress, but reports indicated Iran insisted that the Islamabad Memorandum of Understanding be revived and its provisions honoured, adding that peace could be just days away.\n\nDisplaying diplomatic courage\u2014symbolising a walk into enemy territory\u2014Iran\u2019s President Masoud Pezeshkian and his delegation arrived in the very country with which their nation has been at war for the past seven months. Trump, in his speech, blasted Iran as a terrorist state and the biggest threat to world peace. Pezeshkian\u2014covered by the UN host country agreement\u2014hit back. In his UNGA speech on Wednesday, he turned the tables on Trump, describing the US as the true bully and terrorist in West Asia. Vowing Iran would never bend the knee to the US, he said, \u201cIt must be understood by President Trump and those who seek to bully us that we are ready for dialogue and diplomacy and negotiations, but without the language of force.\u201d\n\nAs Iran remains defiant, on the sidelines of the UNGA sessions, Trump held a meeting with Middle Eastern leaders without the elephant in the room\u2014Israel. At the UNGA session, some of these leaders, particularly Jordan\u2019s King Abdullah and Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan, made thundering speeches critical of Israel. But fiery speeches count for nothing if they do not walk the talk."
  },
