    "md5": "7bba077f9c7fc61c14705344d9c988bd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1077,
    "chunk_text": "No move to curtail rooftop solar: Energy Minister\n\nColombo, September 26 (Daily Mirror)- The government has dismissed reports alleging that it is taking steps to curtail rooftop solar power while promoting other energy sources.\n\nEnergy Minister Anura Karunathilake, speaking at a news briefing today, said the allegations were baseless and pointed to the government\u2019s efforts to expand solar power generation across the country.\n\nAccording to the Minister, the government has facilitated the addition of 1,513 MW of rooftop and ground-mounted solar capacity to the national grid over the past two years.\n\nHe said rooftop solar accounted for 1,141.1 MW of the capacity added to the grid during 2025 and 2026, while a further 534 MW came from ground-mounted solar projects.\n\nThe government plans to increase solar power capacity connected to the national grid by a further 4,585.7 MW by 2029, the Minister said.\n\nFor 2027, plans are in place to add 1,392 MW of solar power to the national grid, including 500 MW from rooftop solar and 642 MW from ground-mounted solar projects."
  },
