    "md5": "df791d251de0fb4a3b9cbe2e5d08de30",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 855,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cDuring Leader Mano Ganesan\u2019s ministerial tenure, many organisations, including Amnesty International, secured NGO registration after previously being refused under the earlier Rajapaksa administration. That was an opening of democratic space. Regulation must not become a mechanism through which governments decide what civil society may say, advocate or question,\u201d Arullsamy said.\n\nHe called for the removal of the policy-alignment requirement, simpler obligations for small organisations, meaningful public consultation and effective judicial safeguards against arbitrary interference.\n\n\u201cThe two-thirds mandate carried an expectation of democratic change. Gotabaya Rajapaksa also had a supermajority, yet public protests during the 2022 economic crisis forced him from office. An iron fist proved a poor substitute for public trust,\u201d he said."
