    "md5": "18e2c7cf3862a6ba307f33104f91d1b2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1589,
    "chunk_text": "England change ODI squad before Sri Lanka decider\n\nSEP.27 (Mirror Sports) - England have called up Dan Lawrence to replace Jos Buttler for the third and final ODI against Sri Lanka at The Kia Oval today, September 27, with the three-match series level at 1-1.\n\nButtler has been ruled out after suffering a left hamstring injury during England\u2019s chase in the second ODI at Headingley.\n\nThe England wicketkeeper-batter was playing a key role in the chase after scoring 66 when he felt discomfort while completing a second run in the 38th over. He briefly left the field before returning later in the innings and adding three more runs to finish with 69. England eventually fell 16 runs short of Sri Lanka\u2019s 321 for nine.\n\nHis absence leaves England without one of their key white-ball players for a match that will decide the ODI series.\n\nLawrence has now been brought into the England squad as Buttler\u2019s replacement. The Surrey batter is yet to make his England debut in limited-overs cricket and was withdrawn from Surrey\u2019s County Championship match against Somerset to join the national squad.\n\nEngland also have wicketkeeping options in Jordan Cox and Tom Banton. Cox is expected to be the leading option to take over the gloves in Buttler\u2019s absence.\n\nCox has played three ODIs for England and could now be handed the opportunity in a high-pressure series decider at The Kia Oval.\n\nSri Lanka levelled the series with a 16-run victory at Headingley, setting up a winner-takes-all clash at The Kia Oval.\n\nThe third ODI is scheduled to begin at 10.30am local time on September 27."
  },
