    "md5": "98218533382f55e536e71e78554e1dda",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 625,
    "chunk_text": "Thileepan statue installed in Nallur removed by police\n\nSep. 27 (Daily Mirror) - A memorial statue of Thileepan, who died after undertaking a hunger strike over demands related to the aspirations of the Tamil people, was removed and taken away by police a short while ago from Nallur, Jaffna.\n\nA statue was erected in Nallur in his memory following the commemoration last week of the 39th anniversary of Thileepan\u2019s death, after he undertook a hunger strike.\n\nFollowing the conclusion of the final day of the commemoration yesterday, the statue was removed by police this morning, September 27, and taken away in a vehicle."
