    "chunk_text": "Champika Ranawaka cautions against Sri Lanka becoming part of geopolitical counter-alliance\n\nColombo, Sep. 27 (Daily Mirror) - United Republican Front (URF) leader Patali Champika Ranawaka, speaking at a public discussion on his latest book, 'Ekata Getuma', cautioned that several geopolitical alliances had been formed across the region and warned that it would be dangerous if the MoU signed among the UAE, India and Sri Lanka turned out to be a stepping stone towards, or a counter-formation to, any of them.\n\nRanawaka, who has delved extensively into the evolution of power struggles in world history in his book written in Sinhala, referred to a number of such alliances, such as QUAD, or the Quadrilateral Security Dialogue, involving the United States, India, Japan and Australia, and AUKUS, which is a security partnership among Australia, the United States and the United Kingdom.\n\nHe said another security partnership among Turkey, Pakistan and Saudi Arabia had been formed in recent times under the name 'Mecca Agreement' as a counter-formation.\n\nAsserting that Sri Lanka should be cautious about these developments, he said it would be serious if the MoU among the UAE, India and Sri Lanka were heading towards such a formation to counter any of these alliances.\n\nLike international relations scholars, he invoked the 'Thucydides Trap', a theory that explains how nine out of 12 struggles for world supremacy ended in wars to determine the winner.\n\nHe said Chinese President Xi Jinping had referred to it during his bilateral meeting with U.S. President Donald Trump.\n\nDetailing the reasons for authoring his book, he said he decided to write it following the collapse of global unity on health security during the pandemic and the eruption of the Russia-Ukraine war."
