    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "d9cc169a7afe89203207fe28f17c1c06",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1421,
    "chunk_text": "Super agri-profit investors: Central Bank has no medicine for greed\n\nThe Central Bank has issued continuous public warnings about the extreme dangers of these pyramid schemes, but it appears the message has failed to reach the wider public. The ultimate cause of this failure is clear: a wave of intense financial greed has completely overcome the public\u2019s basic ability to assess everyday investment risks\n\nA disturbing audio clip has been circulating widely on various social media platforms in Sri Lanka. In the recording, an over-bearing and aggressive male speaker is heard talking to a lady purported to be a Central Bank of Sri Lanka (CBSL) officer.\n\nThe man launches a bitter attack on the Central Bank, accusing it of destroying his family\u2019s livelihood. He loudly blames the bank for throwing his wife and children onto the street by cutting off a regular, lucrative monthly income. This income, he explains, had been flowing continuously from a profit-sharing investment in a modern agricultural project. The disruption occurred because the bank accounts of the agricultural business were abruptly frozen.\n\nThe lady officer responds with exemplary politeness, calmly explaining that the freezing of the accounts was not an arbitrary action by the Central Bank, but a legal directive issued by the courts. She gently reminds him that the bank has no power to override it now without going back to the courts."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-28-dailyftlk-aa463772",
    "num": "dailyftlk-aa463772",
    "date_str": "2026-09-28",
    "description": "Super agri-profit investors: Central Bank has no medicine for greed",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/columns/Super-agri-profit-investors-Central-Bank-has-no-medicine-for-greed/4-797834",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
