    "chunk_text": "The Sigenergy inverter is perhaps the first available in stock in Sri Lanka that can grow with your demand. Whilst traditional battery-based solar systems do not offer future upgradability of batteries of different sizes during different stages, Storex offers a premium future-proof solution. The Storex Sigenergy system switches to backup power with zero disruption to connected loads, and allows power to be drawn efficiently from panels installed at different angles or orientations.\n\nThe product is available for both residential and commercial installations with all leading installers such as SOLAR THERM, AIRO Engineering and selected partners / resellers.\n\n\u201cAs part of the Windforce PLC Family, we have over two decades of experience in renewable energy and have delivered the largest battery and solar projects in the market. SigenStor Neo will not be just another product on the shelf. It is a premium product integrated and genuinely easy to use, and that is what we are bringing to Sri Lankan homes and businesses,\u201d said Lasith Wimalasena, Director, Storex Renewables.\n\nFurther elaborating on the subject, Praboda Welagedera, Manager, Storex Renewables, explained that \u201cThis is the only solution of its kind fully integrated with inverter, battery and solar, where customers have peace of mind in terms of installation or compatibility issues. It simply works with any existing solar installation as an internal capacity enhancement with battery storage that can also grow.\u201d\n\nStorex Renewables (Pvt) Ltd is a Sri Lankan renewable energy company specialising in the trading of solar and battery storage systems. The company is a subsidiary of Windforce PLC, the largest renewable energy developer in Sri Lanka. Storex Renewables (PLC) is the authorised master distributor for Sigenergy products in Sri Lanka."
