    "md5": "daeb20dd8047593c082dfadf0d9eed20",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1692,
    "chunk_text": "DIMO Care Camp strengthens after-sales support for farming community\n\nDIMO Agribusinesses successfully concluded DIMO Care Camp 2026, completing 38 activations across 38 locations islandwide from August 08 to September 15, 2026.\n\nOpen to tractors of any brand or model, the initiative reinforced DIMO Agri Machinery\u2019s commitment to providing reliable after-sales support while strengthening engagement with farming communities across Sri Lanka.\n\nThe DIMO Care Camps were conducted across key agricultural regions, with prominent locations including Kurunegala, Anuradhapura, Vavuniya, Kilinochchi, Ampara, Monaragala, Polonnaruwa, Batticaloa and Matale.\n\nBy taking essential services closer to the farming communities, the initiative highlighted the strength and accessibility of DIMO Agri Machinery\u2019s islandwide after-sales service network.\n\nThe participants benefited from comprehensive tractor inspections, servicing and repairs, technical consultations and access to essential spare parts. DIMO\u2019s experienced technical teams also provided tractor owners with practical guidance on proper maintenance, helping them improve the performance, efficiency and longevity of their machinery.\n\nBeyond machinery-related services, the participants were offered free health checks, including blood pressure checks, BMI assessments and blood glucose testing.\n\nThe activations also created an engaging experience for participants through games and gifts, making the DIMO Care Camp more than just a service initiative. The participants were also encouraged and educated on ways to improve productivity and uplift their livelihoods through better machinery care and informed agricultural practices."
  },
