    "chunk_text": "CA Sri Lanka\u2019s newly launched Forensic Accounting Faculty a timely national initiative, says IGP\n\nInspector General of Police (IGP) Priyantha Weerasooriya on Thursday commended the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka (CA Sri Lanka), highlighting that the newly launched specialised Forensic Accounting and Investigation Faculty was a timely national initiative.\n\nSpeaking at the launch ceremony held at the institute, Weerasooriya, who was the chief guest at the occasion, said, \u201cThe law enforcement agencies, including the Sri Lanka Police, require strong collaboration with highly trained professional accountants and forensic experts. By building specialised human capital, expertise and modern investigative competencies, CA Sri Lanka is directly contributing to strengthening our nation\u2019s resilience against economic crimes.\u201d\n\nSpeaking further, he said modern financial crimes, cyber fraud, money laundering and complex corporate irregularities are no longer confined within the local boundaries. They have become sophisticated, highly networked and highly globalised.\n\n\u201cIn our present Sri Lankan context, as our country moves steadily towards economic recovery and long-term financial stability, safeguarding our financial infrastructure is paramount. Criminal activities such as financial fraud not only drain economic resources but also damage institutional integrity and investor confidence.\u201d\n\nHe made these comments in the presence of guest of honour Financial Crimes Investigation Division Deputy Inspector General of Police M.D.P. Dayaratne as well as CA Sri Lanka President Tishan Subasinghe, Vice President Anoji de Silva, Forensic Accounting and Investigation Committee Chairman Ashane Jayasekera, members of the council and Chief Executive Officer Lakmali Priyangika."
  },
