    "md5": "56cddee44f918e0f9cabce4e147c1047",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1915,
    "chunk_text": "He made these comments in the presence of guest of honour Financial Crimes Investigation Division Deputy Inspector General of Police M.D.P. Dayaratne as well as CA Sri Lanka President Tishan Subasinghe, Vice President Anoji de Silva, Forensic Accounting and Investigation Committee Chairman Ashane Jayasekera, members of the council and Chief Executive Officer Lakmali Priyangika.\n\n\u201cWithout rigorous forensic accounting capabilities integrated at the early stage of an investigation, crucial evidence may be overlooked or rendered inadmissible,\u201d Weerasooriya explained.\n\n\u201cI\u2019m warmly commending CA Sri Lanka for taking this forward-thinking approach to create a platform dedicated to fostering expertise, knowledge sharing and professional collaboration in forensic investigation. May this initiative play an important role in ensuring transparency, accountability and financial security across Sri Lanka,\u201d Weerasooriya added.\n\nAs part of its inaugural offering, the faculty will introduce two programmes in October 2026: Certified Professional Forensic Investigator and Digital Forensics for Finance Professionals, both designed to build specialised capabilities in investigating financial crime and addressing the growing complexity of digital evidence.\n\nDayaratne also echoed the sentiments of Weerasooriya, reiterating that the establishment of the faculty by CA Sri Lanka is not merely a milestone but a timely national imperative.\n\n\u201cFor decades CA Sri Lanka has stood as the guardian of financial integrity and corporate governance in our nation. Today, by inaugurating this specialised faculty, we are sharpening our national defences against one of the most insidious threats of the modern era, which is financial crime, corruption and money laundering,\u201d he said.\n\nSpeaking further, Dayaratne emphasised that accountants, auditors and financial managers are the true gatekeepers of our economy."
  },
