    "chunk_text": "However, although the lease is now secured, the project must still obtain clearances from as many as 23 state institutions before construction can begin, alongside consultations with village societies and temple committees.\n\n\u201cThey collect 23 institutions again and again. This is the problem,\u201d he lamented, suggesting such approvals be completed within around six months, depending on the sensitivity of the land.\n\n\u201cIn a way it\u2019s good, you protect the environment before I even put a brick down there,\u201d he added.\n\nMeanwhile, in Kalpitiya, the group is shaping a beachfront concept that seeks to recast a destination long synonymous with kitesurfing and island excursions as one where travellers linger by the sea.\n\n\u201cNo one is going there for five, six days just to stay on the beach,\u201d Thema Collection Director of Marketing and Business Development Maxime Wickramasinghe noted.\n\nIn Ella, the group is crafting a resort inspired by the Ravana legend woven into the surrounding hills, drawing on temple architecture and traditional havelis, a theme Maxime Wickramasinghe stressed would be interpreted with due reverence. Both projects remain at the design stage."
