    "chunk_size_bytes": 891,
    "chunk_text": "Yoshitha Rajapaksa, Daisy Forrest money laundering case fixed for pre-trial conference\n\nColombo, Sep. 28 (Daily Mirror) - The Colombo High Court today ordered that the case filed against Yoshitha Rajapaksa and Daisy Forrest, over allegations that they committed an offence under the Prevention of Money Laundering Act by depositing nearly Rs. 57 million, allegedly earned through unlawful means, into three bank accounts, be called on November 3 for a pre-trial conference.\n\nWhen the case was taken up today, accused Yoshitha Rajapaksa appeared before court. The second accused, Daisy Forrest, was not present in court.\n\nPresident\u2019s Counsel Anil Silva, who appeared on her behalf, submitted a medical report to court.\n\nMoney laundering charges Indictment filed against Yoshitha Rajapaksa, Daisy Forrest\n\nCourt of Appeal rejects Yoshitha Rajapaksa\u2019s revision plea in money laundering case"
