    "md5": "8af9306d1826e89c58e52bf86573b1d7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1622,
    "chunk_text": "Irregularities in tender process for purchasing body cameras for police\n\nColombo, Sep. 28 (Daily Mirror) - There are suspicions of serious irregularities in the tender process for purchasing body cameras for police officers, Member of the People's Struggle Wasantha Mudalige said.\n\n\"A procurement process has been initiated to purchase 500 body cameras for the police. That is a necessary step. However, to ensure public safety, equipping only police officers engaged in duties outside police stations with cameras is not sufficient; security cameras are also needed inside police stations. Incidents of torture and beatings leading to death inside police stations continue to be reported. Nevertheless, despite taking a good decision regarding these body cameras, the government is executing this good work in a bad way\" he told a media briefing.\n\nThis tender document has not been prepared properly. There are issues with several of its technical specifications. Anyone reading this TOR (Terms of Reference) document can clearly see that it was prepared using Artificial Intelligence. Even the lines generated when using ChatGPT have been left as they are without being removed. Instead of carefully drafting procurement documents considering the technical requirements suitable for Sri Lanka Police and the technical standards used in other countries, this is the kind of farce that happens when you hastily throw things into ChatGPT. Did they not at least re-read, inspect, and correct the shortcomings of a document generated by AI? If they had done so, why didn't they even think to erase those lines? he questioned."
  },
