    "chunk_text": "This tender document has not been prepared properly. There are issues with several of its technical specifications. Anyone reading this TOR (Terms of Reference) document can clearly see that it was prepared using Artificial Intelligence. Even the lines generated when using ChatGPT have been left as they are without being removed. Instead of carefully drafting procurement documents considering the technical requirements suitable for Sri Lanka Police and the technical standards used in other countries, this is the kind of farce that happens when you hastily throw things into ChatGPT. Did they not at least re-read, inspect, and correct the shortcomings of a document generated by AI? If they had done so, why didn't they even think to erase those lines? he questioned.\n\nThe next question is that 500 cameras are not sufficient for this project. Is this being launched as a pilot project, to be tested first and implemented later? Or is this a test to see if they can ask a favored company to submit lower prices, purchase a small number of cameras initially, and later award a larger order for more cameras to the same company at higher prices? It is reasonable for us to harbor this suspicion. On numerous previous occasions as well, they asked for permission just to put the camel's head inside the tent, and later take over the entire tent.\n\nThe way internet facilities are to be provided for these cameras is also questionable."
