    "chunk_size_bytes": 1963,
    "chunk_text": "\u2018Riverstone\u2019 selected as Sri Lanka\u2019s entry for 2027 Oscars\n\nColombo, Sep. 28 (Daily Mirror) - Lalith Rathnayake\u2019s \u2018Riverstone\u2019 has been selected as Sri Lanka\u2019s official entry in the International Feature Film category of the 99th Academy Awards (Oscars).\n\nAccording to National Film Corporation Chairman Sudath Mahaadivulwewa, who also chairs Sri Lanka\u2019s National Oscar Selection Committee, the film was selected through a newly regulated process introduced in line with the requirements of the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences.\n\nHe said the process included approval by the local selection committee and consideration of the professional qualifications of its members.\n\n\u201cThis is the first time a film selected through such a mechanism will represent Sri Lanka,\u201d Mahaadivulwewa said.\n\nThe National Oscar Selection Committee included veteran filmmakers and industry professionals Asoka Handagama, Ravindra Guruge, Anoma Rajakaruna, Visakesa Chandrasekaram, film critic Aruna Gunarathne, musician Lakshman Joseph De Saram and film festival coordinator Uditha Lakmal Kahandawaarachchi.\n\nA total of six films were considered for the selection, including five Sinhala-language productions and one Tamil-language film.\n\nThe films submitted for consideration were \u2018Vihanga Premaya\u2019 (Peacock Lament), produced and directed by Sanjeeva Pushpakumara; \u2018Ayu\u2019, directed by Chathra Weeraman and produced by Yasas Rathnayake; \u2018Father\u2019, produced by Shantha Geethadeva and directed by Chaminda Jayasuriya; \u2018Anthony\u2019, produced by Ramandas Suganthini and Ramandas Sathyaraja and directed by Sukirthan Christhuraja and Jenosan Rajeswar; \u2018Riverstone\u2019, produced by Prabath Roshan and Nimanthi Porage and directed by Lalith Rathnayake; and \u2018Cricket Sadu\u2019, directed by Dilshara Jayamanna and produced by Rasitha Jinasena.\n\nThe committee said four of the six films met the eligibility criteria stipulated under the Academy\u2019s rules."
