    "md5": "e4613bba4ff4f062227f59a8e2ee14d0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1926,
    "chunk_text": "Tamil and Muslim MPs appeal to Saudi Arabia for clemency for Anojan Sivarasa\n\nSep. 28 (Daily Mirror) - A group of Tamil and Muslim party MPs has jointly appealed to the Saudi Arabian Government to grant royal clemency to Sri Lankan migrant worker Anojan Sivarasa, who is facing a death sentence in the Kingdom.\n\nIn a letter addressed to the Saudi Minister of Foreign Affairs, the MPs described Anojan as a \u201cvictim of circumstances\u201d and urged the Saudi authorities to spare his life.\n\nThe letter said they had learned through national and social media reports that Anojan was facing the death sentence following the enhancement of his original sentence by a higher court, which had recently heard his appeal.\n\nAccording to the MPs, the original sentence imposed by a lower court was five years\u2019 imprisonment and a fine over an offence they said was alleged to have been committed against religion.\n\nThe MPs said they understood that there was scope for a final appeal before the highest court of Saudi Arabia.\n\nThey also called on the Sri Lankan Government to place before Parliament and the public confirmed information regarding the case, including the nature of the offence, the legal and diplomatic approaches taken so far and Anojan\u2019s current situation.\n\nThe MPs said that pursuing a final appeal in Saudi Arabia would involve substantial legal costs that would be beyond the means of Anojan\u2019s family, who they described as being from a low-income and underprivileged background.\n\nThey further appealed for consideration of Anojan\u2019s conduct, saying he had immediately retracted a comment posted on Facebook and deleted it while offering an apology.\n\nThe letter said the MPs collectively vouched for Anojan\u2019s innocence, or his \u201cconsistent pro-peace profile and conduct\u201d, and maintained that it was not in his character to intentionally commit an act with the intention of disrespecting or offending Islam."
