    "chunk_text": "Rumesh Tharanga Pathirage wins Sri Lanka\u2019s first gold at Asian Games\n\nColombo, Sep. 28 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lankan javelin thrower Rumesh Tharanga Pathirage clinched the gold medal in the men\u2019s javelin throw at the 2026 Asian Games in Japan, securing Sri Lanka\u2019s first gold medal at the Games.\n\nPathirage produced his winning throw of 88.55 metres on his final attempt, overcoming the competition to claim the gold medal.\n\nThe performance marks a major achievement for Sri Lankan athletics and gives the country its first gold medal at the 2026 Asian Games."
