    "chunk_text": "\u2018Was he planning to open a restaurant?\u2019: AKD on Ranil\u2019s 16-cook request\n\nColombo, Sep. 28 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake, in an apparent reference to former President Ranil Wickremesinghe, claimed that a former President had requested 16 cooks after retiring from office.\n\nDissanayake said his Government had not provided a single cook to any former President since assuming office.\n\nAddressing a rally in Gampaha yesterday, he said the National People\u2019s Power (NPP) Government had changed the country\u2019s political culture from one based on privileges and benefits to one focused on public service.\n\n\u201cFormer Presidents were provided with residences, offices and large fleets of vehicles. One former President who was in office before me requested 16 cooks after retirement. I wonder whether he was planning to open a restaurant after retirement,\u201d he said.\n\nDissanayake said former Presidents had imposed a considerable burden on the public and that the NPP Government had taken steps to change the system of privileges extended to former leaders."
