    "chunk_text": "BMI Group launches Ahasa TV with focus on education and quality content\n\nColombo, Sep. 28 (Daily Mirror) - Business Media International (BMI) Group has launched Ahasa TV, a new television channel dedicated to education, quality programming and family-oriented content, with the aim of offering Sri Lankan viewers an alternative to the increasingly fragmented media environment.\n\nAnnouncing the launch at a gathering, BMI Group Chairman Nilanga Karunarathne said the new channel was conceived following extensive research and consultations conducted across the country. According to Karunarathne, the BMI team engaged with more than 10,000 viewers to understand their expectations and identified a strong demand for a dedicated educational television platform that could appeal to viewers of different generations.\n\nHe said Ahasa TV has been designed around the concept of bringing families together rather than encouraging individuals to consume content in isolation. The channel intends to provide educational and entertaining programmes that children, parents and other family members can watch and discuss together, creating what its founders describe as a shared learning environment.\n\nKaranunarathne said the channel would distinguish itself by placing emphasis on the quality and value of its programming rather than following conventional broadcasting formulas.\n\nAddressing concerns regarding the network's use of frequencies previously allocated to the CSN channel, Group Chairman Karunarathne clarified that utilizing available airtime and technical infrastructure is a standard industry practice. He said that acquiring these frequencies\u2014which have been used by multiple channels over the years\u2014does not imply any political affiliation or hidden agenda tied to former operators.\n\nHe assured the public that Ahasa TV's news operations will be 100% independent, focusing strictly on national interests and discussing issues pertinent to the citizens, rather than serving political entities."
  },
