    "chunk_size_bytes": 1782,
    "chunk_text": "He assured the public that Ahasa TV's news operations will be 100% independent, focusing strictly on national interests and discussing issues pertinent to the citizens, rather than serving political entities.\n\nThe channel's leadership team includes Chairperson Sabeetha Hettiarachchi, while Ajith Ranasinghe serves as Chief Executive Officer. Ranasinghe brings more than 35 years of senior-level experience in finance and business administration and is a Fellow Member of the Institute of Chartered Accountants.\n\nEngineer Nilupa Ranaweera has been appointed Chief Operating Officer, bringing more than 28 years of experience in broadcasting and transmission engineering. He is recognised for his work in pioneering tapeless high-definition broadcasting workflows in Sri Lanka and has held technical leadership positions across several major media organisations.\n\nKisho Vithanage, who has 25 years of experience in broadcast marketing and media revenue generation, serves as Chief Revenue Officer, completing the core executive team behind the new channel.\n\nMeanwhile, veteran journalist Upendra Herath has taken charge as Head of News and Current Affairs. Having been involved in several media start-up projects throughout his career, Herath said he viewed the news division as one of the most influential components of any television station.\n\nThe channel also plans to introduce discussion programmes and new formats that move beyond conventional television news presentation.\n\nAccording to the Ahasa TV team, the objective is not simply to add another channel to Sri Lanka's broadcasting landscape, but to develop a media platform capable of responding to changing audience expectations while maintaining a strong emphasis on education, information and responsible entertainment."
