    "chunk_size_bytes": 2014,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka urges world to put humanity before weapons\n\nSri Lanka has called for strict adherence to international law and international humanitarian law amid the continuing conflicts in West Asia, while reaffirming its support for the Palestinian people's right to self-determination.\n\nAddressing the international community, Sri Lanka said the conflicts in West Asia and elsewhere were having direct security, economic and social implications for the country, particularly given its geographical position in the Indian Ocean and the large number of Sri Lankan migrant workers in the region.\n\nSri Lanka said it had continued to uphold its international commitments and protect human life and dignity despite the difficult geopolitical environment.\n\nReferring to an incident in March this year, Sri Lanka said it had rescued sailors from a vessel belonging to a party to a conflict after the ship ran into distress close to Sri Lankan territorial waters.\n\n\u201cWhile safeguarding our neutrality, we placed humanity above all else,\u201d Sri Lanka said, recalling how the country mobilised its limited resources to rescue and care for wounded and sick sailors and subsequently rescued hundreds more.\n\nSri Lanka said the decision was guided by international law and humanitarian principles.\n\n\u201cAs President Disanayaka has reiterated, \u2018we will never hesitate to protect humanity. If there are actions that must be taken to protect human lives, we will not hesitate to take them under any circumstance\u2019,\u201d it said.\n\nSri Lanka said it wished to present itself to the world as a small island nation that believed there was always space for humanity, even amid conflict and deep divisions.\n\n\u201cWe need a world where our capacity to uphold humanity grows faster than our capacity to destroy it. That is the transformation we should seek,\u201d Sri Lanka said.\n\nExpressing particular concern over the situation in Gaza and the Occupied Palestinian Territories, Sri Lanka said it was \u201cpained\u201d by the continuing developments."
