    "chunk_text": "\u201cWe need a world where our capacity to uphold humanity grows faster than our capacity to destroy it. That is the transformation we should seek,\u201d Sri Lanka said.\n\nExpressing particular concern over the situation in Gaza and the Occupied Palestinian Territories, Sri Lanka said it was \u201cpained\u201d by the continuing developments.\n\n\u201cSri Lanka remains deeply concerned by the conflicts in West Asia and by the heavy cost being borne far beyond the region,\u201d it said.\n\nSri Lanka reiterated that international law, including International Humanitarian Law, must be respected by all parties, stressing that dialogue remained the only viable way forward.\n\nThe country also reaffirmed its support for the inalienable rights of the Palestinian people, including their right to self-determination.\n\nSri Lanka said it was among the countries that had recognised Palestine as a distinct State in the 1980s and reiterated its support for an independent and sovereign Palestinian State existing alongside Israel in peace, within the pre-1967 borders.\n\nIt also welcomed the UN Security Council resolution calling for a ceasefire in Gaza and urged all parties to uphold it.\n\n\u201cHumanitarian assistance must reach civilians without obstruction,\u201d Sri Lanka said, adding that the recovery and reconstruction of Gaza should be treated as an urgent priority."
