    "md5": "3b018e93ebcbac79cb3760224694aa49",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 581,
    "chunk_text": "In 2024, Sri Lanka was emerging from a severe crisis, but many households had yet to feel the benefits of recovery. By 2026, the country had made real progress in several areas. The next test is whether that progress leads to lower poverty, stronger real incomes, better employment, more affordable essentials and greater confidence among households and businesses.\n\nA promise made in 2024 should be judged in 2026 by what has been implemented, what it has achieved and whether people can feel the difference.\n\n(The author is Emeritus Professor of Economics, University of Colombo)"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
