    "md5": "e3b3cbbd2fdb0f43f5a45b3286573a62",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1684,
    "chunk_text": "He also said work was progressing on a contributory pension scheme for migrant workers, while preparations were underway for a new Foreign Employment Bill aimed at strengthening the policy and regulatory framework governing overseas employment.\n\nThe Government is also preparing a mechanism to enable Sri Lankans living overseas to exercise their voting rights, he said.\n\nHe said Sri Lanka\u2019s foreign employment strategy must also move beyond simply increasing the number of workers leaving the country for overseas employment.\n\nThe policy focus, he stressed, should include skills development, better employment opportunities, safe and regular migration, stronger worker protection and long-term economic security for workers and their families.\n\nHemachandra also called for closer cooperation between migrant-sending and destination countries, particularly on social security arrangements, recruitment regulation, family protection and the reintegration of returning workers.\n\nWith migrant workers making a significant contribution to household incomes and the national economy, he said their rights, dignity and security must remain at the centre of Sri Lanka\u2019s foreign employment policy.\n\nHemachandra acknowledged the continued support of the ILO, its Country Office for Sri Lanka and the Maldives, the STREAM Program team and development partners in strengthening social protection and security mechanisms for migrant workers.\n\nThe STREAM initiative seeks to bring origin and destination countries together to address gaps in social protection for workers moving across borders, an issue of particular importance to Sri Lanka given the scale of its overseas employment sector."
