    "chunk_size_bytes": 1628,
    "chunk_text": "Blink International acquires Wrist Lab\n\nBlink International has acquired Wrist Lab as part of a long-term strategy to elevate the watch retail experience in Sri Lanka. The acquisition brings together Wrist Lab's established presence in the wristwatch market with Blink\u2019s scale, expertise and market presence, creating a stronger platform to unlock new opportunities for growth, expand the offering and deliver a more comprehensive retail experience to consumers.\n\nFounded in 2019 under Orbit Worldwide Ltd., Wrist Lab was created to fill the market vacuum for a one-stop retail experience. Instead of searching multiple single-brand sites, Sri Lankan consumers gain effortless access to leading global watch brands, fulfilling the founders\u2019 vision of ultimate choice under one roof.\n\nFollowing the acquisition, Wrist Lab will be developed as Blink\u2019s dedicated consumer-facing retail platform, with the ambition of evolving it into a stronger and more comprehensive multi-brand watch destination in Sri Lanka. This will include an expanded international brand portfolio, an enhanced retail experience and a stronger service proposition, giving consumers greater choice and a more compelling overall experience.\n\nThe move will also allow Blink to sharpen its focus as the official brand principal for Casio, G-Shock and Edifice in Sri Lanka, with greater emphasis on building and managing these brands, while further strengthening its authorised retail network, distribution and after-sales support. By establishing specialised focus areas, both entities are positioned to scale independently while complementing each other."
  },
