    "md5": "3afa08d179befac8b270aa4730ad6737",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1628,
    "chunk_text": "Abanchy Ceylon expands into Kenya with the incorporation of Abanchy Africa\n\nFrom left: Ghareeb Mazrui \u2013 Head of Kenya Operations, Anupa de Silva \u2013 Senior Executive Business Development, and Seth Manickam \u2013 Head of Africa Region at Abanchy Africa, and\u00a0 Asker Mohemad \u2013 General Manager, Abanchy Ceylon\n\nAbanchy Ceylon (Pvt) Limited, the logistics arm of Pink Eagle Holdings, recently marked a significant milestone in its African expansion journey with the incorporation of Abanchy Africa Limited in Kenya.\n\nAbanchy\u2019s operation in the area is the latest amplification of the Group\u2019s presence in Africa, strengthening an international network and operations that began with the launch of sales offices in Ethiopia and Dubai in 2024.\n\nThe establishment of Abanchy Africa Limited signals an important breakthrough in the Group\u2019s regional expansion strategy. Expanding the portfolio of Pink Eagle Holdings, Abanchy Africa Limited will operate as a fully-fledged logistics and freight-forwarding company, providing comprehensive logistics solutions to customers across Kenya.\n\nDiscussing the incorporation of Abanchy Africa Limited, Asitha Silva, Group Chairman and Managing Director at Pink Eagle, said \u201cBy establishing our presence in Kenya, we\u2019re reaffirming our commitment to creating a resilient and futureready business group with the potential for competitive growth in new directions. Having established a presence in Africa, our goal is to deliver sustainable value and drive innovation by uniting bold, strategic thinking with a modern, global mindset to pursue excellence in innovation and performance.\u201d"
  },
