    "md5": "27e568453436c3fb2f17d9a58b0c6176",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2018,
    "chunk_text": "SLEIS 2026 to explore new opportunities in SL\u2019s health economy\n\nAs Sri Lanka looks to expand the sources of economic growth, healthcare is increasingly relevant not only as a social priority but also as an area with potential for investment, innovation and economic development.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s potential in the health economy will be explored at Sri Lanka Economic and Investment Summit 2026 (SLEIS 2026), organised by The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce, on October 12 and 13, 2026.\n\nThe session \u2018Reimagining Healthcare for a Modern Health Economy\u2019 will explore how Sri Lanka can strengthen its healthcare ecosystem while developing new opportunities across healthcare services, pharmaceuticals, medical technology and related sectors.\n\nIt will also consider the role of private sector investment and innovation in improving healthcare delivery and outcomes.\n\nThe panel will feature a keynote address by Zydus Lifesciences Limited Chief Financial Officer Tushar Shroff. He will be joined at the discussion by Hettigoda Group of Companies Director Vidyani Hettigoda, Association of Private Hospitals and Nursing Homes President and Ruhunu Hospital Chief Executive Officer Raveen Wickramasinghe, Hemas Holdings PLC Deputy Chairman and Non-Executive Director Murtaza Esufally and Institute for Health Policy Director Prof. Ravi Rannan Eliya. The discussion will be moderated by Sunshine Holdings PLC Group Chief Executive Officer Shyam Sathasivam.\n\nThe session will examine how the developments in healthcare can contribute to productivity, investment and economic growth, while addressing the opportunities and challenges involved in building a modern health economy.\n\nIt forms part of Day 2 of SLEIS 2026, held under the theme \u2018Positioning Sri Lanka in a Changing Global Economy: Resilience, Reform and the Future of Economic Policy\u2019.\n\nRegistrations are now open at https://sleis.chamber.lk/. For more information, contact Alikie on 011 558 8805 ([email\u00a0protected]) or Shanuka on 0701082541 ([email\u00a0protected])."
  },
