    "description": "HayWind commences turbine tower erection at Mannar Wind Farm",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-news/HayWind-commences-turbine-tower-erection-at-Mannar-Wind-Farm/273-351319",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1790656447.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-29-dailymirrorlk-674e01bc-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "f0c062fe85a7bda9d7ca41b4c8740652",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1851,
    "chunk_text": "HayWind commences turbine tower erection at Mannar Wind Farm\n\nHeavy lifting operations underway as HayWind nacelle is positioned atop the tower at Mannar site\n\nA fully assembled 5MW HayWind turbine stands tall against Mannar coastline as the project advances toward full commissioning\n\n50MW project enters major turbine installation phase as tower erection gets underway\n\nHayWind One Limited, the wind energy arm of Hayleys Fentons Limited, has marked a major milestone in the development of its 50MW Mannar Wind Farm, with the turbine installation now in full swing and the first two 5MW wind turbines fully erected.\n\nThe milestone sets the pace for the continuous installation of all 10 turbines across the utility-scale project.\n\nEach complete wind turbine reaches an impressive tip height of approximately 186.5 metres. The structure comprises a 110-metre tower, assembled in four sections, anchored to a heavy-duty concrete foundation, reinforced with piles, an anchor cage, foundation bolts and a high-strength grout layer.\n\nMounted atop the tower is the nacelle, housing the main bearing, drive shaft, gearbox, generator and an active yaw system to keep the rotor aligned with the prevailing winds fitted with the hub and three 76.5-metre rotor blades.\n\nGiven Mannar\u2019s coastal conditions, all turbine components are equipped with specialised marine-grade anti-corrosion coatings and filtration systems.\n\nThe heavy lifting operations are carried out using a massive 900-tonne crawler crane, the largest ever deployed for a wind energy project in Sri Lanka, supplied by Hayleys Advantis Limited in partnership with Sarans India.\n\nPrior to positioning the crane, the engineering teams executed extensive ground stabilisation, including aggregate base course preparation, soil compaction and rigorous load-bearing tests to ensure platform safety."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-29-dailymirrorlk-674e01bc",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-674e01bc",
    "date_str": "2026-09-29",
    "description": "HayWind commences turbine tower erection at Mannar Wind Farm",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-news/HayWind-commences-turbine-tower-erection-at-Mannar-Wind-Farm/273-351319",
    "lang": "en",
