    "chunk_size_bytes": 1336,
    "chunk_text": "CSE\u2019s 2025 annual report ranked as Sri Lanka\u2019s No. 1\n\nThe Colombo Stock Exchange\u2019s (CSE) 2025 annual report has been ranked as Sri Lanka\u2019s top annual report for 2025, winning Gold for the third consecutive year at the USA\u2019s League of American Communications Professionals (LACP) 2025 Vision Awards, in the Annual Report and Integrated Report (IR) Categories.\n\nThe CSE\u2019s IR, themed \u2018Where Confidence Meets Capital\u2019, was ranked as Sri Lanka\u2019s No. 1 annual report and earned a place among the Asia-Pacific region\u2019s top 100 reports and secured the global Gold Industry Award for the third consecutive year.\n\nThe 2025 annual report highlighted the CSE\u2019s strategic priorities, key achievements and long-term vision, demonstrating its leadership in navigating the evolving market conditions and embracing technological innovation.\n\nThe recognition reaffirmed the CSE\u2019s position as a leading force in Sri Lanka\u2019s financial sector and a benchmark for reporting excellence across the region.\n\n\u201cBeing ranked as Sri Lanka\u2019s No. 1 annual report and receiving the LACP Gold award for the third consecutive year is a proud affirmation of the CSE\u2019s commitment to transparent, accountable and forward-looking reporting,\u201d said Executive Vice President Finance, Listed Entity Compliance and Sustainability Kusal Nissanka."
