    "chunk_text": "\u201cBeing ranked as Sri Lanka\u2019s No. 1 annual report and receiving the LACP Gold award for the third consecutive year is a proud affirmation of the CSE\u2019s commitment to transparent, accountable and forward-looking reporting,\u201d said Executive Vice President Finance, Listed Entity Compliance and Sustainability Kusal Nissanka.\n\nThrough the CSE\u2019s introduction of the Green, Social, Sustainable and Sustainability Linked (GSS+) bond framework, the bourse has seen the market collectively raise approximately Rs.82 billion, representing nearly 40 percent of total debt capital raised through the CSE in 2025.\n\nWith a Sri Lankan capital market primed with an attractively competitive price-earnings ratio in a strengthened economy, the CSE continues to innovate in the Sri Lankan capital market. These successive back-to-back awards demonstrate the organisation\u2019s professionalism and dedication to create a transparent and productive capital market, inspiring confidence abroad and domestically.\n\nAs Sri Lanka\u2019s economy continues to strengthen and the capital market remains attractively valued, the CSE remains focused on driving innovation and enhancing market development. This string of prestigious international awards reflects the organisation\u2019s unwavering commitment to transparency, professionalism and the advancement of an efficient capital market that inspires confidence among both the local and global investors."
