    "md5": "8d4ebe59e603efb7bf1c678b900024af",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 835,
    "chunk_text": "President congratulates Rumesh on historic gold\n\nColombo, Sep. 29 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake has congratulated Sri Lankan javelin thrower Rumesh Tharanga Pathirage on winning the country\u2019s historic first-ever Asian Games gold medal in the javelin event.\n\nIn a message shared on social media, the President said Pathirage\u2019s achievement had made the entire nation proud and extended his best wishes for continued success, particularly as the athlete sets his sights on winning Olympic gold.\n\nThe President also reaffirmed the government\u2019s commitment to supporting Pathirage and other Sri Lankan athletes pursuing international success.\n\n\u201cKeep reaching for the skies, Rumesh \u2013 the nation is fully behind you!\u201d the President said.\n\nRumesh Tharanga Pathirage wins Sri Lanka\u2019s first gold at Asian Games"
