    "chunk_text": "Asian Games Cricket: Bangladesh, Sri Lanka reach semifinals without playing a ball\n\nThe Daily Star - The Sri Lankans will meet India in the last four and Bangladesh play Pakistan, with both matches scheduled for Thursday.\n\nSri Lanka progressed when their quarter-final with Nepal was washed out -- higher-ranked teams go through in the event of bad weather.\n\nBangladesh were awarded victory over lower-ranked Malaysia for the same reason.\n\nPakistan and reigning champions India sealed their semi-final spots after rain also washed out both matches on Monday.\n\nThere has been heavy rain in Games host Nagoya and Aichi prefecture in recent days, but better weather is forecast from Wednesday."
