    "md5": "93f4ec760b55111874012d0f1da15d54",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1990,
    "chunk_text": "In a second incident,\u00a0 \u00a0Saudi Arabia executed a Sri Lankan domestic worker, Rizana Nafeek for allegedly killing a baby in her care in 2005. Rizana was convicted in 2007 of murdering four-month-old baby Naif al-Quthaibi and executed in January, 2013, despite an eight year-long effort by international human rights organisations and the Sri Lankan government which made several pleas to the Saudi king for clemency.\n\nAnojan\u2019s case is the fourth incident. Those who politicise everything under the sun seem to compare the cases involving the 45-year-old woman and Anojan for political reasons, even though the four cases were filed under four different charges. The four youth were charged with robbery, while Rizana was charged with homicide. The 45-year-old woman whose identity was not revealed either by the Sri Lankan or Saudi authorities had been sentenced for adultery. Now Anojan has been sentenced to death for blasphemy.\n\nAnojan\u2019s case is a classic example of mishandling social media. The events leading to this sad episode commenced with this year\u2019s Tamil pilgrims\u2019 annual pada yathra from Jaffna to Kataragama. Influenced by the Story of \u2018Aloka\u2019 the dog that accompanied\u00a0 Buddhist monks on an international Walk of Peace, the Tamil pilgrims named a dog that accompanied them to Kataragama \u2018Subramani\u2019.\n\nIt is said that a Muslim in Kalmunai had kicked the dog after it urinated in his garden,\u00a0 and this triggered\u00a0 Facebook\u00a0 religious insults between\u00a0 Sri Lankan Hindus and Muslims. Although it is difficult to find out who started the exchange of derogatory posts;\u00a0 it was Anojan who ultimately faced the worst of the consequences.\u00a0 Now, people attempt to\u00a0 gain political mileage out of this poor man\u2019s misery. Some politicians want to score points in the event of Anojan\u2019s release or\u00a0 commutation of his sentence. Some people attempt to use his sentence to further religious strike. These shortsighted actions might further aggravate the situation."
