    "chunk_text": "It is said that a Muslim in Kalmunai had kicked the dog after it urinated in his garden,\u00a0 and this triggered\u00a0 Facebook\u00a0 religious insults between\u00a0 Sri Lankan Hindus and Muslims. Although it is difficult to find out who started the exchange of derogatory posts;\u00a0 it was Anojan who ultimately faced the worst of the consequences.\u00a0 Now, people attempt to\u00a0 gain political mileage out of this poor man\u2019s misery. Some politicians want to score points in the event of Anojan\u2019s release or\u00a0 commutation of his sentence. Some people attempt to use his sentence to further religious strike. These shortsighted actions might further aggravate the situation.\n\nSocial media users and those obsessed with politics must have two concerns at this juncture: not disrupting\u00a0 efforts to save the life of the man languishing in the Saudi jail, and preserving\u00a0 highly fragile communal harmony.\n\n\u2018Your Thought\u2019 is a space, a right of the readers to support or contradict and discuss the issues highlighted in the editorial and other articles in the editorial and op-ed pages. Designed as the reader\u2019s editorial; our readers can send in their writings, with a word count not exceeding 200, to \u2018Your Thought\u2019, Daily Mirror Political Features Desk, No 8, Hunupitiya Cross Road, Colombo 2 or email to [email\u00a0protected]"
