    "md5": "0cf10a5f8b5474be022c49228b81e268",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1080,
    "chunk_text": "Exhibition highlights surgeon\u2019s good work\n\nThe recently held exhibition by reputed surgeon Dr. Gamini Goonetilleke was\u00a0 like no other. Titled\u00a0 \u201cBeyond the Scalpel: A Unique Visual Chronicle of Surgery, Humanity and Four Decades of Service, \u201c it was a journey through War & Peace depicting man\u2019s inhumanity to man. Land mine disasters was especially sad to see.\n\nCare Concern Compassion toward his patients be it in Colombo,\u00a0 Jaffna,\u00a0 or rural Polonnaruwa was an eye opener to all. A visual chronicle of four decades of surgery humanitarian service and national duty was a wonder to behold.\n\nThe good doctor\u2019s contribution to uphold the highest ethics of\u00a0 medicine must never be overlooked. His contribution to uplift man through surgery need to be recognised by the Government of Sri Lanka.\n\nI suggest he be awarded any of the following awards. Sri Lankabhimanya Deshamanya, Deshabandu, Sri Lanka Shikamani, Sri Lanka Thilaka, Vidya Jothy or Vidya Nidhi.\n\nThe Nation must show gratitude & say Thank You to Dr. Gamini Goonetilleke, one of its distinguished citizens."
  },
  {
