    "chunk_text": "Four injured as pavement caves in near old Kandy Prison\n\nColombo, Sep. 29 (Daily Mirror) - Four people were injured and admitted to Kandy National Hospital this morning (29) after a section of a pavement suddenly collapsed near the old prison in Kandy town.\n\nThe victims, three men and one woman, were walking along the pavement when a section of the walkway in front of a nearby shop gave way beneath them.\n\nLocal residents suspect that severe soil erosion caused by water flowing through a canal behind the commercial shops may have weakened the ground beneath the pavement."
