    "md5": "6efe33993c807c862823d0f6c43ce27b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1244,
    "chunk_text": "Court directs counsel to advise Gnanasara Thera to appear in another contempt case\n\nColombo, Sep. 29 (Daily Mirror) - The Court of Appeal today directed the counsel appearing for Ven. Galagodaaththe Gnanasara Thera to advise him to be present in court in connection with a contempt of court application after the Thera failed to appear before court.\n\nThe matter was taken up before a two-judge Bench comprising Justices Mayadunne Corea and Lakmali Karunanayake.\n\nPresident\u2019s Counsel Anura Meddegoda, appearing for Ven. Gnanasara Thera, informed court that his client was scheduled to undergo surgery. However, he failed to produce any medical certificate before court to substantiate the reason for his absence.\n\nState Counsel appearing for the Attorney General submitted that the presence of the respondent was essential in a contempt of court proceeding. The State Counsel accordingly moved that a warrant be issued against the respondent or that he be directed to appear before court today, if possible.\n\nHaving considered the submissions, the Court of Appeal directed President\u2019s Counsel Anura Meddegoda to advise his client to be present in court.\n\nThe matter was subsequently kept down to enable the respondent to appear before court."
