    "md5": "918f2eb7f4e188593ee654e959f0ef97",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1819,
    "chunk_text": "Full Moon a sign of cultural link between China and Sri Lanka - Ambassador\n\nColombo, Sep. 29 (Daily Mirror) - Chinese Ambassador Wei Huaziang said the full moon day was significant to Sri Lanka and China in terms of culture and it closely links the hearts of Sri Lankans and Chinese building bridges for cultural exchange between the two countries.\n\n\u201cSri Lanka has a long history and a splendid civilization, and Poya Day is also of great importance to people\u2019s lives. An ancient Chinese poem reads; the bright moon rises over the sea; we share this moment though far apart\u2019. The same bright moon carries the Sri Lankan people\u2019s hope for a peaceful harmonious life and the Chinese people\u2019s yearning for happiness and reunion. It is this moon that closely links the hearts of our two people\u2019s and builds bright bridges for our cultural exchanges,\u201d Mr. Huaziang said at the celebration of the Chinese Mid-Autumn Festival held in Colombo.\n\n\u201cToday\u2019s stage is a vivid epitome of China-Sri Lanka exchanges. Artists from Zhejiang . China, have brought not only the poetry of the Jiangnan water towns and the elegance of Chinese cultural heritage , but also , in programs such as \u2018Harmony of the Maritime Silk Road\u2019 a resonant blend of classic melodies from China and Sri Lanka . These Melodies spanning mountains and seas, showcase the balance of strength and tenderness in Eastern aesthetics, convey the good wishes for reunion at the Mid-Autumn Festival , and use art to play a contemporary movement of people to people connectivity and shared beauty between China and Sri Lanka,\u201d he added.\n\n\u201cArtistic dialogue between nations will transcend geographical and linguistic boundaries, understand each other's history, traditions and emotions and deepen mutual respect between nations,\u201d he also said."
  },
