    "chunk_text": "\u201cArtistic dialogue between nations will transcend geographical and linguistic boundaries, understand each other's history, traditions and emotions and deepen mutual respect between nations,\u201d he also said.\n\nVice Chancellor University of Colombo Prof. Indika Mahesh Karunatilaka recalled the long relationship which Chinese and Sri Lankan academics have maintained over the years.\n\nA media release issued on the Festival said it will further deepen cultural exchanges and mutual learning between China and Sri Lanka, the China Cultural Centre in Sri Lanka, the Department of Culture, Radio, Television and Tourism of Zhejiang Province. The Overseas Chinese Association in Sri Lanka jointly hosted the \"Mid-Autumn Festival Cultural Performance series under the guidance of the Embassy of the People's Republic of China in Sri Lanka. A delegation of 32 renowned artists from the Zhejiang Performing Arts Group (including the Zhejiang Song and Dance Theatre) participated in the event:"
