    "chunk_size_bytes": 1035,
    "chunk_text": "Eswatini Government confirms death of Sri Lankan national\n\nSep. 29 (Daily Mirror) - The Government of the Kingdom of Eswatini has confirmed the death of a Sri Lankan national, Mr. Kishanth Peramaiya, who was temporarily residing in the country under an arrangement with the Government of the United Kingdom.\n\nAccording to an official statement issued by the Eswatini Government, authorities in Eswatini and the United Kingdom had been engaged in consultations regarding Mr. Peramaiya\u2019s potential long-term residency in the Kingdom at the time of his death.\n\nThe statement, signed by Acting Government Spokesperson Thabile Mdluli on September 28, 2026, confirmed that discussions between the relevant authorities were ongoing.\n\nThe Eswatini Government said it is working closely with the British High Commission to make the necessary burial arrangements and engage with Mr. Peramaiya\u2019s family.\n\nThe government expressed its sincere condolences to Mr. Peramaiya\u2019s family and loved ones, saying it joins them in mourning their loss."
