    "md5": "0c51931d317817a1f569d663c5e43ceb",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1998,
    "chunk_text": "112 new Metro buses deployed on seven Western Province routes\n\nColombo, Sep. 29 (Daily Mirror) - A total of 112 newly introduced Metro buses were deployed yesterday (29) on seven routes in the Western Province, with the aim of easing traffic congestion in Colombo and providing a more comfortable and safer public transport service.\n\nThe buses were deployed at a ceremony held at the Thalangama Metro Bus Depot under the patronage of President Anura Kumara Dissanayake.\n\nThe modern Metro Bus service was initiated as a proposal in the 2025 Budget, with an allocation of Rs. 3 billion for the procurement of 100 comfortable low-floor buses.\n\nAccordingly, 104 buses received by Sri Lanka and eight buses provided by the Government of Japan have been deployed under the new service.\n\nThe buses will operate along seven routes centred on Colombo according to designated routes and timetables, enabling passengers to reach their destinations on schedule.\n\nOne of the key objectives of introducing the service is to reduce the number of private vehicles entering Colombo, particularly vehicles carrying only a single passenger.\n\nTransport, Highways and Urban Development Minister Bimal Rathnayake said public transport should be placed on the same level as Sri Lanka\u2019s free healthcare and education systems.\n\nHe said the President had emphasised this requirement during a recent progress review meeting and that the President\u2019s encouragement had been a major source of strength in taking forward the Metro Bus initiative.\n\nRathnayake said the Government had invested approximately Rs. 7.5 billion to establish the Metro service, describing the investment as a symbol of the country\u2019s economic strength.\n\nHe said the Government had taken less than a year to complete the initiative while adhering to relevant government circulars.\n\nThe Minister said another 50 buses were expected to be introduced before the Sinhala and Hindu New Year and deployed on inter-city services to Jaffna, Kandy and Galle."
