    "chunk_text": "He said the Government had taken less than a year to complete the initiative while adhering to relevant government circulars.\n\nThe Minister said another 50 buses were expected to be introduced before the Sinhala and Hindu New Year and deployed on inter-city services to Jaffna, Kandy and Galle.\n\nRathnayake also requested mayors to establish suitable parking facilities close to relevant bus stops to promote a Park-and-Ride system.\n\nMeanwhile, Lanka Metro Transit (Pvt) Ltd, established to implement the Metro Bus programme, has completed the planning, procurement, infrastructure development and trial-operation stages.\n\nThe initial Metro Bus route network comprises seven main routes with a total corridor length of approximately 188.7 kilometres.\n\nA fully digitalised system for Metro Bus operations has also been designed, with the procurement process now under way. The system is expected to support modern fleet management, passenger information, fare collection and operational monitoring.\n\nPlans for Metro Bus depots have also been completed, while construction and infrastructure development work has commenced.\n\nThe Road Development Authority and the Colombo Municipal Council are carrying out work to develop bus-stop facilities.\n\nThe Government plans to expand the Metro Bus service to several major cities across the country in the future.\n\nJapan has provided eight buses to support the launch of the service, while Rathnayake said the Chinese Government had agreed to provide another 100 buses to the Metro company following discussions held during President Dissanayake\u2019s visit to China."
