    "chunk_text": "The revised document is to be reviewed by the National Steering Committee for New Education Reforms and its sub-committees covering five key areas: curriculum reform, human resource development, education administration and infrastructure development, evaluation and assessment, and public awareness and promotion.\n\nMeanwhile, activity books and teacher guides covering all three terms are being prepared for Grades 1 and 2 for 2027, while modules and teacher guides for all three terms are being prepared for Grade 6.\n\nThe NIE has also trained master trainers for primary and secondary-level subjects, with provincial-level plans for teacher training currently being prepared.\n\nIn addition, the Evaluation and Assessment Sub-Committee has prepared a practical Policy Guide on School-Based Evaluation and Assessment, taking into account the resources available within the school system. The guide has been approved by the National Steering Committee.\n\nAccordingly, the Cabinet approved the proposal submitted by Prime Minister and Minister of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education Harini Amarasuriya to continue the reforms introduced for Grade 1 in 2026 and implement the reforms for Grades 2 and 6 in 2027."
