    "chunk_size_bytes": 579,
    "chunk_text": "Further evidence in Lalith-Kugan case set for Nov. 27\n\nColombo, Sep. 29 (Daily Mirror) - The Jaffna Magistrate\u2019s Court today fixed November 27 at 1.30 p.m. for the recording of further evidence from former President Gotabaya Rajapaksa in connection with the case relating to the disappearance of political activists Lalith Kumar Weeraraj and Kugan Muruganandhan in Jaffna in 2011.\n\nRajapaksa gave evidence today from around 1.45 p.m. to 3.00 p.m. before the Colombo Chief Magistrate\u2019s Court via video link, with the evidence being recorded by the Jaffna Magistrate\u2019s Court."
  },
