    "md5": "69aa70f49daff65be9b223f03a86da6c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1141,
    "chunk_text": "Baseline Road extension gets green light\n\nColombo, Sep. 29 (Daily Mirror) - The Cabinet of Ministers has approved the award of the contract for Phase III of the Baseline Road Extension Project to Maga Engineering (Pvt) Ltd at a cost of Rs. 2.89 billion, excluding Value Added Tax (VAT).\n\nThe decision was taken following the recommendations of a High-Level Procurement Committee, which evaluated seven bids submitted under a national competitive bidding process.\n\nThe project, proposed by the Minister of Transport, Highways and Urban Development, covers the development of a 0.86-kilometre section from Kirulapona Junction to Dutugemunu Street along the Colombo\u2013Horana Road.\n\nUnder the project, the existing road section will be upgraded to a six-lane roadway to improve traffic flow and connectivity in the area.\n\nThe development will also include an underpass, signalised intersections, dedicated pedestrian facilities and improvements to the existing drainage system.\n\nThe project is expected to strengthen road infrastructure along the Colombo\u2013Horana corridor and improve traffic management and road safety in the surrounding areas."
  },
