    "md5": "d05fea4f6bb840b5cf80ec325fa42775",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1956,
    "chunk_text": "President calls for single digital system for public services\n\nColombo, Sep. 29 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake has instructed officials to work towards establishing a single national digital system covering public services, while reviewing the ongoing digitalisation of local authorities and Divisional Secretariats.\n\nThe President gave the directive during a progress review meeting on the Government\u2019s digital transformation programme held at the Presidential Secretariat today (29).\n\nThe meeting focused on the digitalisation of local authorities and Divisional Secretariats, with the aim of providing faster, more efficient and transparent public services.\n\nA key area of discussion was the **National Framework for the Digitalisation of Local Authorities**, currently being developed by the Ministry of Public Administration, Provincial Councils and Local Government.\n\nPresident Dissanayake instructed officials to identify all services that local authorities are required to provide to the public and determine which of them could be incorporated into digital systems.\n\nHe also called for an assessment of whether existing digital platforms adequately cover these services.\n\nThe President emphasised the need to move away from separate digital systems operated independently by different government institutions and instead develop a single national system covering the public service.\n\nHe instructed the Ministry of Public Administration, Provincial Councils and Local Government and the Ministry of Digital Economy to closely coordinate their efforts towards this objective.\n\nThree officers from the Ministry of Digital Economy are also to be assigned to coordinate the further development of the national system operated under the Ministry of Public Administration, Provincial Councils and Local Government.\n\nThe officers will also identify shortcomings in existing systems and oversee necessary amendments and improvements."
  },
