    "chunk_size_bytes": 1945,
    "chunk_text": "Sajith ready for public debate on Government report on socio-economic situation\n\nColombo, Sep. 29 (Daily Mirror) - Opposition Leader Sajith Premadasa, who claimed that the report compiled by the Central Bank and the Department of Census and Statistics is full of errors, challenged the Government to a public debate on it.\n\nPremadasa stated that the report is full of errors, flaws and shortcomings.\n\nHe said it was a misleading document intended to deceive the 22 million citizens of the country. He emphasised that his criticism was based on solid facts and data and said he was ready for an open debate on the matter with any party at any time.\n\nThe Opposition Leader made these remarks during a special statement delivered today.\n\n\u201cThrough this report, the Government is attempting to paint a falsely beautiful picture of the country\u2019s situation. To achieve this, they have selectively included certain information while intentionally omitting other vital facts. When presenting data, there must be chronological consistency and integrity. The Central Bank and the Department of Census and Statistics have no right to present outdated data to formulate a conclusion,\u201d the Opposition Leader said.\n\nThe Opposition Leader noted that he was making these criticisms with a thorough understanding of economics, including both macroeconomic and microeconomic principles.\n\n\u201cAll socio-economic data in the Government report are from 2016 to 2019. For the main economic indicators, macroeconomic indicators, demographic data and life expectancy, 2024 data have been utilised. Indicators such as external trade, finance, consumer price indices, real GDP, imports and exports, prosperity indices and human development indices have also been compared with Asian and SAARC countries using recent data. However, in the section detailing socio-economic conditions, the data used are exclusively from the outdated 2016\u20132019 period,\u201d he also said."
