    "md5": "8249450d2b96e80e974213e35b28d539",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1827,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka, Brazil move to strengthen dairy sector cooperation\n\nThe Cabinet has approved the signing of a supplementary agreement with Brazil to pave the way for implementing a technical cooperation project aimed at developing Sri Lanka\u2019s dairy industry, Cabinet Spokesperson and Minister Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa said yesterday.\n\nSpeaking at the press briefing to announce decisions taken by the Cabinet of Ministers on Monday,\n\nDr. Jayatissa said the initiative builds on a basic Technical Cooperation Agreement signed between Sri Lanka and Brazil on 16 September 2008.\n\nUnder the agreement, a high-level delegation of Brazilian experts visited Sri Lanka in 2023 to conduct a comprehensive assessment of the technical assistance required for the development and capacity building of the country\u2019s dairy and sugarcane sectors.\n\nHe said, based on the findings of the Brazilian technical team and a concept paper submitted by Sri Lanka\u2019s National Science Foundation to the Brazilian Cooperation Agency, the two countries had agreed to prepare a cooperation agreement, including a logical framework, to implement a dairy industry development project.\n\nThe Cabinet has therefore approved a proposal submitted by Agriculture, Livestock, Land and Irrigation Minister to sign a Supplementary Adjustment Agreement between the Governments of Sri Lanka and Brazil.\n\nDr.Jayatissa said signing the supplementary agreement was a prerequisite for subsequently entering into a cooperation agreement among the Brazilian Cooperation Agency of the Brazilian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the Federal University of Vi\u00e7osa and the Government of Sri Lanka.\n\nThe cooperation agreement will provide the framework for implementing the project aimed at strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s dairy industry through Brazilian technical expertise and assistance."
