    "chunk_size_bytes": 1722,
    "chunk_text": "STC General targets wider institutional and consumer markets with three new product launches\n\nFrom left: Wasantha Dissanayake - Private Secretary to the Minister; Ravindra Fernando - Chairman/Managing Director, Sri Lanka State Trading (General) Corporation Ltd.; Deputy Minister R. M. Jayawardane; Deputy Minister Upali Samarasinghe; and Chamila Iddamalgoda - General Manager, STC\n\nSri Lanka State Trading (General) Corporation Ltd. (STC) has expanded its STC General Product portfolio with the launch of a 65 inch Smart Board, inverter air-conditioner and instant electric hot-water shower, extending its offering across digital technology and consumer electrical products.\n\nThe products were launched at a ceremony at Marino Beach Hotel, Colombo, under the patronage of Deputy Minister of Trade, Commerce, Food Security and Co-operative Development R.M Jayawardane, and Deputy Minister of Co-operative Development Upali Samarasinghe with the participation of STC Chairman/Managing Director Ravindra Fernando, senior officials, institutional customers and employees.\n\nThe launch forms part of STC\u2019s effort to expand its own-brand range and strengthen its presence in institutional and consumer markets. Technology and electrical products have become an increasingly important component of the Corporation\u2019s business alongside its established trading and procurement operations.\n\nThe 65 inch STC General Smart Board features a 4K UHD display, 8GB RAM, 128GB internal storage, Android 16 operating system and a 48MP built-in camera. Designed for educational institutions, training centres, meeting rooms and corporate environments, the Smart Board supports interactive teaching, presentations and digital collaboration."
  },
