    "md5": "7f850c40c8cbfea005d57ce124d92215",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1972,
    "chunk_text": "Infomate opens new chapter for SL\u2019s BPM industry with Kurunegala expansion\n\nInfomate (Pvt) Ltd, a Sri Lankan Business Process Management (BPM) and Business Process Outsourcing (BPO) company and a wholly owned subsidiary of John Keells Holdings PLC, is advancing its regional growth strategy with the opening of its second office in a regional city, this time in Kurunegala.\n\nHaving pioneered rural BPM in Sri Lanka through long-standing projects in Mahavilachchiya, Seenigama and Jaffna, Infomate has demonstrated that global business services can be successfully delivered beyond Colombo.\n\nThe Kurunegala expansion builds on this legacy, bringing international career opportunities closer to regional talentand enabling professionals to build careers serving global clients without relocating to Colombo.\n\nTaking the BPM industry beyond Colombo - Infomate\u2019s expansion reflects a broader transformation taking place across the global BPM industry. In markets such as India, leading BPM and shared services companies have successfully expanded into second-tier cities including Pune, Hyderabad and Coimbatore, creating new talent and delivery hubs beyond major metropolitan centres.\n\nKurunegala presents a similar opportunity for Sri Lanka. With a growing and educated talent pool and its strategic connectivity to multiple regions of the country, the city offers the potential to become a new centre for globally delivered business services. For Infomate, the decision represents an opportunity to tap into previously underserved talent while demonstrating that world-class BPM services can be delivered from locations beyond Colombo.\n\nJehan Perinpanayagam, CEO of Infomate said,\u201c Colombo has traditionally been the centre of Sri Lanka\u2019s corporate and technology-driven opportunities, drawing talent from across the country. With our expansion into Kurunegala, we are taking a different approach\u2014bringing global career opportunities closer to where talent lives."
  },
