    "time_ut": 1790731790.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-30-dailymirrorlk-3599691f-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "b3d00f93a8be815714b849ddfb98c5f1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1875,
    "chunk_text": "Ceyline Group unveils \u2018Roots for the Future\u2019 national reforestation initiative to mark 40th anniversary\n\nCeyline Group is celebrating its landmark 40th anniversary by launching \u2018Roots for the Future\u2019, a national reforestation initiative with a vision to plant and nurture 40,000 native trees across Sri Lanka.\n\nThe core objective of the \u2018Roots for the Future\u2019 initiative is to mobilize Sri Lanka\u2019s youth as active agents of natural capital restoration, establishing a self-sustaining culture of lifelong environmental accountability across school communities nationwide.\n\nThe project was launched with Vidyarathna College and Ashoka College Horana on board.\u00a0 Accordingly, Ceyline Group is replacing unmonitored \u201cplant-and-forget\u201d corporate events with a digital verification ecosystem anchored by the proprietary OXY App platform to combine youth empowerment with audited ecological restoration. The project creates a transparent tri-party framework uniting Ceyline Group, the Ministry of Education, and the Department of Forest Conservation, to secure a living green outline for Sri Lanka\u2019s future generations.\n\nAs the Primary Sponsor & Digital Ecosystem Owner, the Ceyline Group provides full baseline funding for the Phase 1 launch of 4,000 plants, soil nutrients, and operational deployment toward the 40,000-tree vision. The Group will deploy and host the OXY App digital governance architecture and also act as the corporate catalyst uniting national government bodies behind a shared ESG vision. The Department of Forest Conservation, in its role as \u201cTechnical Oversight & Scientific Validation\u201d, validates endemic and native plant species selections tailored to specific regional agro ecological zones. It also deploys local Forest Extension Officers to provide technical oversight, regional plant species validation, and scientific guidance."
  },
