    "chunk_text": "As the Primary Sponsor & Digital Ecosystem Owner, the Ceyline Group provides full baseline funding for the Phase 1 launch of 4,000 plants, soil nutrients, and operational deployment toward the 40,000-tree vision. The Group will deploy and host the OXY App digital governance architecture and also act as the corporate catalyst uniting national government bodies behind a shared ESG vision. The Department of Forest Conservation, in its role as \u201cTechnical Oversight & Scientific Validation\u201d, validates endemic and native plant species selections tailored to specific regional agro ecological zones. It also deploys local Forest Extension Officers to provide technical oversight, regional plant species validation, and scientific guidance.\n\nPhase 3 is actively underway where the digital platform is fully operational, actively tracking initial baseline planting across participating school networks with real-time audit capability, laying the groundwork to scale toward the 40,000 -tree vision. The 4th and final phase involves opening the platform architecture to external corporate co-sponsors to fund student incentive expansion and scale targets toward and beyond the 40,000-tree vision.\n\nNatasha Egodage - Executive Deputy Chairperson and Chief Purpose Officer of the Ceyline Group stated, \u201cCelebrating Ceyline\u2019s 40th anniversary with the \u2018Roots for the Future\u2019 initiative allows us to live our purpose: \u2018inspiring leadership in everyone we touch, to build a sustainable and equitable future for all.\u2019 We hope this project of environmental stewardship empowers and inspires the next generation of leaders.\u201d"
