    "chunk_size_bytes": 1641,
    "chunk_text": "Imran Noordeen appointed as Sheraton Colombo\u2019s Sales & Marketing Director\n\nSheraton Colombo Hotel has announced the appointment of Imran Noordeen as its new Director of Sales & Marketing, bringing with him more than two decades of experience across Sri Lanka\u2019s hospitality industry and international markets.\n\nImran\u2019s career reflects a steady progression through sales, marketing and commercial leadership roles across some of the country\u2019s most recognised hospitality brands.\n\nHaving started his career at Galle Face Hotel in 2006, he built his experience with Cinnamon City Hotels, Premier Inn Middle East in Dubai, Browns Hotels and Resorts.\n\nHe commenced his journey with Marriott International in 2017 with his appointment as Sales Manager for Weligama Bay Marriott Resort & Spa, and continued to serve as the commercial leader for Courtyard by Marriott Colombo and Sheraton Kosgoda Turtle Beach Resort. Most recently, he served as Director of Sales & Marketing for Cinnamon City Hotels.\n\nIn his new position at Sheraton Colombo Hotel, Imran will lead the hotel\u2019s sales and marketing strategy, with a focus on strengthening its market presence, developing strategic partnerships and driving meaningful commercial opportunities.\n\n\u201cI am delighted to return to Marriott International and be part of this exciting chapter for Sheraton Colombo Hotel. Sheraton has always represented meaningful connections, and I look forward to working closely with our associates, partners and guests to create experiences that resonate, while strengthening our position within Colombo\u2019s dynamic hospitality landscape,\u201d said Imran Noordeen."
  },
