    "chunk_size_bytes": 1833,
    "chunk_text": "EDB and SLAMERP partner to enhance energy efficiency and profitability  in rubber products manufacturing\n\nThe Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB), in collaboration with the Sri Lanka Association of Manufacturers and Exporters of Rubber Products (SLAMERP), conducted a full-day workshop titled \u201cBusiness Profit Improvement through Sustainable Energy Efficiency Management for the Rubber Products Manufacturing Industry\u201d at the EDB premises. Technical experts from the National Cleaner Production Centre (NCPC), Sri Lanka, led the programme.\n\nThe workshop aimed to strengthen the knowledge of technical personnel on efficient energy management, cost reduction, sustainable production and modern energy technologies. It followed a request from SLAMERP to raise awareness among its member companies.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s rubber products industry is a technology-intensive sector known internationally for high-quality, value-added products made from natural latex and dry rubber. Tyres account for about 60 percent of the sector\u2019s exports and gloves around 30 percent, with other rubber products making up the rest. However, heating, curing and other high-temperature processes make manufacturing energy-intensive, and high energy costs can significantly affect profitability and global competitiveness.\n\nThe programme opened with remarks by the EDB, followed by a keynote on \u201cEnergy Management as a Strategic Advantage\u201d by Eng. Samantha Kumarasena, Director General/Chief Executive Officer of NCPC Sri Lanka. Eng. Ruwan Wijemanne, Chief Operating Officer of NCPC, covered energy performance in rubber manufacturing and energy efficiency in electrical systems. Eng. M.M. Munsif, Senior Energy Expert at NCPC, spoke on building a sustainable Energy Management System (EnMS) and investing in energy efficiency and decarbonization."
  },
