    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "ce85054fe01ae898a39ded13f51a1c88",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 916,
    "chunk_text": "GGGI has already played a role in developing Sri Lanka\u2019s sustainable finance market. Through the Global Trust Fund on Sustainable Finance Instruments, funded by the Government of Luxembourg, it previously supported three thematic bond issuances in Sri Lanka, including the country\u2019s first blue bond.\n\nGGGI, together with the United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific, has also supported the Finance Ministry in designing Sri Lanka\u2019s first Sovereign Green Bond Framework.\n\nThe CSE said the domestic market is also gaining international visibility, with three Sri Lankan institutions receiving recognition at the 2026 Environmental Finance Sustainable Debt Awards for GSS+ bond issuances.\n\nThe latest programme is expected to broaden the prospective issuer pipeline by providing institutions considering sustainable debt instruments with technical support before entering the market."
  },
