    "chunk_text": "Financing continued to play a sizeable role in purchases. The financing share for motor cars increased to 47.4 percent from 42.8 percent in July, while that for SUVs rose to 45 percent from 41.9 percent. Small-car financing stood at 42.3 percent for brand-new vehicles and 49 percent for pre-owned cars.\n\nElectric car registrations fell to 558 from 992 in July, while electric SUVs dropped to 149 from 433. Electric two-wheelers, which continued to account for the bulk of EV registrations, declined to 4,133 from 5,544.\n\nBYD continued to dominate electric car registrations with 342 units, comprising 236 ATTO 1s, 103 Dolphin Dynamics and three Seal Comforts. Kaiyi followed with 65 units, BAW with 61 and Dongfeng with 54.\n\nAcross vehicle categories, BYD registrations fell to 498 in August from 1,320 in July, with the latest month\u2019s tally comprising 342 cars, 148 SUVs and eight pickups.\n\nHybrid registrations also softened, falling to 1,942 from 2,288 in July, with hybrid SUVs accounting for 1,893 units. Toyota led with 674, followed by Honda with 631, Jetour with 297 and BYD with 99."
