    "md5": "bb8b4844f7c4f93d7043709621cbb1f0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1627,
    "chunk_text": "On 19 September, Saudi air Defences intercepted a Houthi ballistic missile aimed at Riyadh the first such attack on the capital since hostilities escalated while reportedly intercepting additional strikes aimed at Bisha, a city in southwestern Saudi Arabia, in Asir Province, close to the Yemeni border, Taif a major city in Mecca Province, in the western highlands near Mecca. Farasan, and Yanbu a major port city on the Red Sea coast in Al Madinah Province, further north.\u00a0 The missile\u2019s approach disrupted flights at King Khalid International Airport and produced a visible plume of smoke near a fuel storage area; Saudi authorities reported no casualties.\u00a0 The Houthis stated the strikes targeted \u201csensitive sites\u201d in Riyadh and Saudi oil infrastructure a claim that remains independently unverified. Saudi Arabia has responded with intensified airstrikes on Houthiheld territory, the Houthi advance has continued.\n\nRiyadh\u2019s response has included the Mecca Joint Defence Agreement with Turkey and Pakistan, publicly framed as a mutual-Defence arrangement; one analysis (IANS, 21 September) assessed it as largely symbolic, on the view that Pakistan is unlikely to commit forces to Saudi Arabia\u2019s Defence. Separately, Washington signed a civilian nuclear cooperation agreement with Riyadh in July, and the Trump administration has pressed Saudi Arabia to join the Abraham Accords as a condition of that agreement\u2019s full implementation a linkage between Saudi nuclear cooperation and normalization with Israel that comes as Saudi territory faces attacks from an Iran-aligned group opposed to that normalization."
