    "chunk_text": "Riyadh\u2019s response has included the Mecca Joint Defence Agreement with Turkey and Pakistan, publicly framed as a mutual-Defence arrangement; one analysis (IANS, 21 September) assessed it as largely symbolic, on the view that Pakistan is unlikely to commit forces to Saudi Arabia\u2019s Defence. Separately, Washington signed a civilian nuclear cooperation agreement with Riyadh in July, and the Trump administration has pressed Saudi Arabia to join the Abraham Accords as a condition of that agreement\u2019s full implementation a linkage between Saudi nuclear cooperation and normalization with Israel that comes as Saudi territory faces attacks from an Iran-aligned group opposed to that normalization.\n\nThe Greenland settlement offers a contrasting case. Trump\u2019s earlier push to acquire the island, including remarks not ruling out military force, prompted eighteen months of transatlantic concern, French troop deployments to the island, new European consular presence in Nuuk, and strain within NATO discussed at the July Ankara summit. That approach did not produce a territorial transfer."
