    "chunk_size_bytes": 1827,
    "chunk_text": "Next IMF programme depends on macro economic stability\n\nColombo, Sep. 30 (Daily Mirror) - Amidst uncertainty about the Government\u2019s next move after the current IMF (International Monetary Fund) programme with politicians across the divide expressing different views, an IMF spokesperson said the international lender\u2019s focus is to bring the current arrangement to the finishing line, and if there is any such request for a fresh one, it will be considered only after assessment of macroeconomic stability and balance-of-payments need.\n\nIn response to a query by the Daily Mirror regarding talks about another IMF programme , the spokesperson said still two reviews remain under the ongoing EFF(Extended Fund Facility) arrangement, which is in place through March, next year.\n\n\u201cHence, the immediate priority should be on getting the current programme to the finish line,\u201d the spokesperson said.\n\nAccording to the spokesperson, it is ultimately a decision for the Sri Lankan authorities to decide whether another programme is needed, but as of now a formal request has not been forwarded for a successor arrangement.\n\nReferring to the procedure in such a case, the spokesperson said, \u201cTypically, when an IMF member country formally expresses interest in a new arrangement, IMF staff and the authorities work closely to assess the macroeconomic situation, determine whether a balance-of-payments need exists, and discuss program design accordingly. Once staff-level agreement is reached on a new arrangement, approval of the IMF Executive Board would be needed,\u201d\n\nAn IMF team led by Evan Papageorgiou visited Sri Lanka during September 10-23, 2026, to discuss (i) recent macroeconomic developments and progress in implementing economic and financial policies under the EFF arrangement, and (ii) policy recommendations."
  },
