    "chunk_size_bytes": 838,
    "chunk_text": "Fort Court to hear case against Ranil today\n\nColombo, Sep. 30 (Daily Mirror) - A case filed under the Offences Against Public Property Act against former President Ranil Wickremesinghe and former Presidential Secretary Saman Ekanayake is scheduled to be taken up today (30) before the Colombo Fort Magistrate\u2019s Court.\n\nThe case relates to allegations concerning the alleged misuse or misappropriation of state funds.\n\nThe Criminal Investigation Department (CID) had previously informed the court that investigations into the matter had been completed and that relevant investigation extracts had been forwarded to the Attorney General for legal advice.\n\nFollowing the CID\u2019s submission, Colombo Fort Magistrate Pasan Amarasena ordered that the case be called today to receive the Attorney General\u2019s position and further instructions."
