    "md5": "7957f4847088187c3e603b743d7cb3b8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 919,
    "chunk_text": "1st World Congress on Snakes 2026 to be held in Sri Lanka\n\nColombo, Sep. 30 (Daily Mirror) - The inaugural ceremony of the 1st World Congress on Snakes \u2013 2026, being held in Sri Lanka for the first time, is scheduled to take place with the participation of Environment Minister Dhammika Patabendi.\n\nThe international congress, themed \u201cSnakes, Science, Species Survival & Sri Lanka,\u201d is expected to bring together local and international scholars, researchers, environmentalists and experts in the field.\n\nThe congress will focus on key issues related to snake diversity, conservation and scientific research in Sri Lanka, while providing a platform for experts to share knowledge and discuss challenges concerning snake species and their survival.\n\nThe event is expected to highlight the importance of scientific research and conservation efforts in understanding and protecting Sri Lanka\u2019s diverse snake fauna."
