    "chunk_text": "The evidence was recorded from the Jaffna Magistrate\u2019s Court on behalf of the prosecution under the direction of Counsel Nuwan Bopage.\n\nWhile giving evidence, Gotabaya Rajapaksa, responding to several questions put to him, said that he could not remember the relevant incidents as a considerable period of time had passed.\n\nQ: Do you accept that if civilians disappear in a country, it poses a threat to national security?\n\nA: Gotabaya Rajapaksa: \u201cPeople disappear for various reasons. The police take specific action regarding such incidents. Not every disappearance is brought before the National Security Council. There are instances where information is received. If it is a special situation, information has been received.\u201d\n\nThereafter, while giving evidence regarding the alleged abduction of former Western Provincial Council member Sagala Senaratne, Gotabaya Rajapaksa said that he did not remember the incident.\n\nQ: When former Western Provincial Council member Sagala Senaratne was abducted, you received information regarding it, didn\u2019t you?\n\nA: Gotabaya Rajapaksa: \u201cI cannot answer that, Your Honour. That happened 15 years ago.\u201d\n\nQ: Sagala Senaratne stated at a media briefing that his life was saved because of the then President and you. Do you remember that?\n\nQ: I suggest to you that you became aware of the abduction of Sagala Senaratne after it occurred. Do you accept that?\n\nThereafter, questions were put to him regarding the abduction of journalist Keith Noyahr. Responding to those questions, Gotabaya Rajapaksa said that he remembered Keith Noyahr but did not remember the details of the incident concerning him.\n\nA: Gotabaya Rajapaksa: \u201cI remember him. I remember the incident to some extent. I do not remember the details.\u201d\n\nQ: What did you mean when you said you remember it to some extent?\n\nA: Gotabaya Rajapaksa: \u201cI remember that an incident took place. I did not come prepared for this today. That is why I said I remember it to some extent.\u201d"
