    "chunk_text": "Q: What did you mean when you said you remember it to some extent?\n\nA: Gotabaya Rajapaksa: \u201cI remember that an incident took place. I did not come prepared for this today. That is why I said I remember it to some extent.\u201d\n\nQ: Do you know that he was abducted by a group of persons and subjected to torture?\n\nA: Gotabaya Rajapaksa: \u201cI do not know that he was subjected to an abduction. But I know that he disappeared and was found.\u201d\n\nQ: Do you remember receiving a telephone call informing you that he had disappeared?\n\nA: Gotabaya Rajapaksa: \u201cIt was something that happened 15 years ago. I do not remember now who spoke to me over the telephone.\u201d\n\nQ: Do you remember informing the then Inspector General of Police Jayampathi Wickramaratne about it?\n\nA: Gotabaya Rajapaksa: \u201cIf I had learned about such an incident, I would have informed the Inspector General of Police about it.\u201d\n\nQ: Do you remember informing Defence Secretary Major General Hendawitharana about it?\n\nA: Gotabaya Rajapaksa: \u201cThis happened a long time ago. Therefore, I do not remember it now.\u201d\n\nQ: Do you know that Keith Noyahr had sustained serious injuries and was later left at a certain location?\n\nQ: I suggest to you that Keith Noyahr was released without being killed after being abducted, on your instructions.\n\nA: Gotabaya Rajapaksa: \u201cI reject that, Your Honour. I initially said that such an incident had occurred. I do not know how it happened or who did it. Also, when I am asked about it after 15 years, I do not remember.\u201d\n\nQ: I suggest to you that in a report submitted to the Criminal Investigation Department in January 2017, you had reported the matter to the Deputy Inspector General of Police.\n\nQ: Do you remember that five officers of the Army Tripoli Platoon were named as suspects in connection with the incident?\n\nQ: I suggest to you that, as Defence Secretary at the time, you directly intervened and gave instructions regarding abductions and disappearances."
  },
