    "chunk_text": "The Prime Minister announced that arrangements had been made to implement education reforms for Grades 2 and 6 next year. Cabinet approval was granted on September 28 for the 13-year curriculum framework, the concept paper of the National Education Commission and the student assessment framework linked to the reforms.\n\nShe noted that a Sri Lankan film had, for the first time, been selected for submission to the Academy Awards, while athlete Rumesh Tharanga had won a gold medal at the Asian Games.\n\nThe Prime Minister expressed hope that the newly opened Bataduwa Rathanajothi School of Aesthetic Education would become a starting point for Sri Lankan students to achieve further success internationally.\n\nShe encouraged students to make use of the growing global opportunities and described the establishment of the school as an important beginning."
