    "md5": "e0062170d4a241b868b3be5aee279ac0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 866,
    "chunk_text": "The Committee was told that sports facilities should be maintained as a government responsibility to promote public health and community welfare, rather than being operated as profit-making ventures.\n\nThe Committee also discussed the development of sports facilities in Ampara, the upgrading of Weber Stadium in Batticaloa and the Hingurakgoda Sports Complex, improvements to sports facilities in Hali-Ela, Badulla, and issues concerning the Bandaragama Public Grounds in Kalutara.\n\nIt was further informed that government funding for international competitions would be provided only to official national teams representing Sri Lanka and for officially recognised international tournaments.\n\nThe Committee also stressed that there would be no discrimination based on race or region in selecting national teams or sending athletes and teams to overseas competitions."
