    "chunk_text": "President seeks mechanism to educate parents on drug threat\n\nColombo, Sep. 30 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake has instructed officials to establish a mechanism to actively involve parents in protecting children from the growing drug menace, stressing that strong parent-child relationships are more effective than legal measures alone.\n\nHe said parents should be directly educated on the seriousness of the drug threat and trained to identify and monitor changes in their children\u2019s behaviour.\n\nThe President issued the instructions at a meeting of the \u201cA Nation United\u201d National Steering Committee established to eradicate the drug menace, held today at the Presidential Secretariat.\n\nHe also stressed the need for a trusted person to guide parents when their children are at risk of being exposed to drugs. Noting that parents often turn to teachers or religious leaders for assistance, he directed officials to develop a systematic programme to provide reliable guidance.\n\nHe said teachers involved in such a programme should receive special training.\n\nThe President also called for further strengthening measures to dismantle drug distribution networks.\n\nThe meeting was informed that the Government Analyst\u2019s Department had increased its daily output of forensic reports following the expansion of facilities and improvements in efficiency. Around 8,000 drug-related forensic reports were completed during September alone, with Navy personnel assisting in data entry.\n\nOfficials said the faster processing of forensic reports had enabled a significant number of suspects remanded for drug-related offences to obtain bail, helping to ease prison overcrowding.\n\nDissanayake instructed officials to refer the new drug control Bill currently before Parliament to the relevant committee during the first week of October, obtain its approval and take steps to have it passed by Parliament by the third week of October."
