    "chunk_size_bytes": 1529,
    "chunk_text": "Dissanayake instructed officials to refer the new drug control Bill currently before Parliament to the relevant committee during the first week of October, obtain its approval and take steps to have it passed by Parliament by the third week of October.\n\nThe President instructed officials to discuss the practical issues involved with the Defence Ministry Secretary and other relevant officials and take necessary action.\n\nHe also inquired into measures to enable expert reports and Government Analyst\u2019s reports to be submitted directly to courts by email under Act No. 7 of 2025.\n\nProgress in filling vacancies at the Legal Draftsman\u2019s Department was also reviewed, along with programmes conducted in international schools to combat drug use and their effectiveness.\n\nThe President further stressed the need for social media campaigns targeting young people to raise awareness of the dangers of drug use.\n\nThe meeting also discussed the drug-related challenges emerging in the Northern and Eastern regions following the war and measures being implemented to address them.\n\nDissanayake emphasised the importance of maintaining the 1818 hotline for information on drug trafficking, distribution and other related illegal activities. He called for greater publicity on action taken in response to information received through the hotline to strengthen public confidence in the service.\n\nThe progress of the drug rehabilitation programme, including measures to increase the capacity of rehabilitation centres, was also reviewed."
