    "chunk_size_bytes": 722,
    "chunk_text": "Ranil\u2019s security officer hospitalised following alleged assault by video journalist\n\nColombo, Sep. 30 (Daily Mirror) - A security officer attached to the security detail of former President Ranil Wickremesinghe was admitted to the National Hospital in Colombo today after he was allegedly struck on the head with a camera by a television cameraman.\n\nSources from the former President\u2019s office told Daily Mirror that the officer had lodged a complaint with the Slave Island Police before being admitted to hospital.\n\nThe incident allegedly occurred near the gate of the Colombo Fort Magistrate's Court as Wickremesinghe was leaving the court following a hearing in a case filed over allegations of misusing state funds."
