    "md5": "b9ff1fe61aa1f17c0e10a7b323af6d2e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1386,
    "chunk_text": "57 officers of tri-forces receive \u2019\u2019Vishishta Seva Vibhushana\u2019\u2019 medals\n\nColombo, Sep 30 (Daily Mirror) - A total of 57 serving and retired senior officers of the Sri Lanka Army, Navy and Air Force were presented with the \u201cVishishta Seva Vibhushana\u201d medals by President Anura Kumara Dissanayake today.\n\nThe awards were presented at the Presidential Secretariat in recognition of the distinguished and dedicated service rendered by officers of the regular forces.\n\nAddressing the ceremony, President Dissanayake said the recipients had made an exceptional contribution to the country and its people while remaining committed to their duties and responsibilities under all circumstances.\n\nHe said they had continued to serve regardless of whether it was day or night, whether weather conditions were favourable or adverse, or whether their lives were at risk.\n\nThe President said the country needed a public service characterised by such dedication and accountability.\n\nThe \u201cVishishta Seva Vibhushana\u201d is a distinguished military honour established by Presidential proclamation. It is awarded to officers of the three Armed Forces who have completed at least 25 years of continuous service and maintained a commendable service record.\n\nThe conferment, forfeiture and restoration of the medal are governed by regulations issued by the President and published in the Gazette."
  },
