    "chunk_text": "The proposed reforms would also require affiliated bodies, including district associations, provincial bodies and clubs, to comply with financial and governance regulations. Wickramaratne said there would be no tolerance for financial or administrative irregularities.\n\nSLC is working with technical experts, to strengthen its technical capabilities. The reforms also include improvements to coaching education, sports medicine and physiotherapy, sports psychology and development programmes for women's cricket.\n\nWickramaratne said administrators and staff should consider themselves temporary custodians of a national institution, with the ultimate objective being to establish a transparent, resilient and world-class cricket system that serves the public.\n\n\"All of us who work here are only here for a period of time... But the institution must go on, and cricket must continue forward,\" he said."
