    "chunk_text": "Opposition\u2019s strategic dilemmas, Easter massacre matrix\n\nFirst understand the masterplan, then connect the dots to discern the mastermind\n\nSajith at Polduwa: Undeniable success, but could be more inclusive\n\nAn opinion poll in the Sunday Times (27 Sep.) on the 2nd anniversary of AKD-NPP rule shows 58% dissatisfaction and only 42% satisfaction. This means that President Dissanayake has retained the vote\u2014below an absolute majority\u2014that brought him into office, but that the JVP-NPP\u2019s high popularity at the Parliamentary election has been reduced to the same level as his, while he hasn\u2019t increased his popularity either.\n\nThe 58% negative vote should gladden the Opposition, but it really can\u2019t because the Opposition contains a bipolar split between Sajith/SJB and Namal/SLPP. Namal may have run the gruelling legal gauntlet by Presidential election 2029.\n\nThere are only two scenarios/templates in the playbook which can break the Opposition stalemate in 2029:\n\nI. Sajith emulates his father\u2019s 1988 breakthrough victory beating the formidable Sirimavo Bandaranaike by swinging the poor among SLFP voters and JVP supporters through the inspiring vision of Janasaviya, the radical poverty-reduction program.\n\nII. Namal combines and emulates CBK\u2019s 1994 repositioning of her party and 1999 defeat of Ranil, and his father\u2019s patriotic-populist 2005 victory over Ranil.\n\nThe UNP fails to recognise that its decades-long inability to elect a President to lead the country was because it de-Premadasaised its economic ideology post-1993, and failed to transition over a decade ago to Sajith as leader.\n\nThere is no bigger indictment of the UNP and the pro-Ranil caucus in the SJB than the electorate\u2019s verdict on \u2018unmandated\u2019 President Wickremesinghe who was consigned to third place in 2024 having \u2018saved the country\u2019."
  },
