    "chunk_size_bytes": 2039,
    "chunk_text": "There is no bigger indictment of the UNP and the pro-Ranil caucus in the SJB than the electorate\u2019s verdict on \u2018unmandated\u2019 President Wickremesinghe who was consigned to third place in 2024 having \u2018saved the country\u2019.\n\nNamal is rightly allergic \u2013 for ideological \u2018brand\u2019 reasons \u2013 to any alliance with Ranil\u2019s UNP (hence the latter\u2019s Anuradhapura absence).\n\nThe UNP has no successor to Ranil. The party can avoid electoral-political extinction only if it recognises Sajith as leader/candidate\u00a0 and enters an equation with the SJB as main force. That\u2019s the last move with which Ranil can redeem himself and be assured of respectful recognition and status.\n\nThe rest of the Joint Opposition including the SLFP should recognise Namal as leader/candidate, abandoning delusions of a non-Sajith/non-Namal candidate with a mass base, national resonance and double-digit viability.\n\nSajith Premadasa and the SJB scored a significant tactical and symbolic victory with their impressive \u2018swarm\u2019 demonstration, over 5000-strong, at Polduwa on 24 September, proving the SJB\u2019s dominant status within the Opposition.\n\nThat victory was more limited than it might have been, and had an avoidable downside, because of an arrogant, disruptive streak on the part of some overtly right-wing SJB organisers/MPs\u2014notorious loose cannon\u2014exhibiting sectarianism, isolationism and unilateralism.\n\nTo succeed and prevail, Sajith and the SJB should treat five strategic political realities as fundamentals:\n\n1. A \u2018One-Party State\u2019 project cannot be defeated by a mirroring \u2018One-Party Opposition\u2019 project and posture. It can only be defeated by a broad, politically pluralist democratic project with social democracy at the core.\n\n2. The SJB which since its inception failed twice (2020, 2024) to break out of its parent/predecessor UNP\u2019s 20% electoral bunker, cannot afford to risk going it alone, not least in a three-way race. It must win over the middle-ground, the swing voters and new voters, to constitute a majority."
  },
