    "chunk_text": "2. The SJB which since its inception failed twice (2020, 2024) to break out of its parent/predecessor UNP\u2019s 20% electoral bunker, cannot afford to risk going it alone, not least in a three-way race. It must win over the middle-ground, the swing voters and new voters, to constitute a majority.\n\n4. Sajith Premadasa is SJB leader and Opposition Leader, and as such must lead, include and represent the interests of the whole Opposition\u2014not just one (albeit biggest) component, his own party, though axiomatically that would be primary.\n\n5. The SJB is the main and leading Opposition party and must be recognised as such, but it does not hold a monopoly of the Oppositional space. SJB primacy must not translate into exclusivity or self-quarantine. To lead, the SJB must draw in others who follow; form alliances, blocs, partnerships; act in unison or coordination with diverse parties on common issues against a common authoritarian adversary.\n\nThe 22nd Amendment battle dispelled the ridiculous though widespread illusion that Prime Minister Harini Amarasuriya was an enlightened liberal dissident and potential counterweight within the AKD Cabinet and JVP-NPP Parliamentary group.\n\nShe mounted a wall-to-wall defence of the amendment, and pronounced harshly on her uncle, Prof. G.L. Peiris\u2014though the English language provided for less rude, insolent judgmentalism and more finesse and civility. Prof. G.L. Peiris\u2019 detailed critique of 22A did not come from his Ministerial past which she finds so reprehensible, but from his stellar scholarly side.\n\nComrade Minister Bimal Rathnayake\u2019s announcement that the Government will not seek to enter a successor IMF program after the current one expires in 2027,\u00a0 leaves me suspicious about what he doesn\u2019t say: that the Government will not re-enter the international money markets in 2027. The recourse to the high-interest global money markets as distinct from bilateral and multilateral funding and foreign direct investment is the crux of our crisis."
