    "md5": "5fe28963f7d9663a263de2eed15e69df",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1869,
    "chunk_text": "Comrade Minister Bimal Rathnayake\u2019s announcement that the Government will not seek to enter a successor IMF program after the current one expires in 2027,\u00a0 leaves me suspicious about what he doesn\u2019t say: that the Government will not re-enter the international money markets in 2027. The recourse to the high-interest global money markets as distinct from bilateral and multilateral funding and foreign direct investment is the crux of our crisis.\n\nResistance resumes in the form of the Jana Aragala Vyaparaya mobilisation at Campbell Park on 3 October against unaffordable taxation. Wasantha Mudalige, Aragalaya hero, issued a convincing clarion call: (https://www.facebook.com/share/v/19qxeLyCcp/)\n\nReconstruct the masterplan, and connect the dots to discern the mastermind/s.\n\nThe conviction by the court of those most closely involved in the Easter Sunday massacre is welcome but is only half the story and does not\u2014cannot\u2014complete the search for justice.\n\nThe verdict deals with \u2018sins of commission\u2019\u2014those who assisted or played some role in the Easter massacre by their active involvement. But there were also \u2018sins of omission\u2019. Evil was committed not only by those who blew up the innocent and those who assisted them along the way, but also by those who had been informed that the evil deed would happen and chose to do nothing about it, or dragged their feet with the result that a preventable atrocity was not prevented.\n\nIn a superb piece of investigative reportage, the Jaffna Monitor reconstructs the story of the 17-day delay.\n\n\u2018\u2026India\u2019s warning to the State Intelligence Service arrived on April 4, 2019, followed by further information on April 18 and 19; on the evening of the 20th and again at first light on the 21st, the head of the SIS passed his own warnings to the inspector general of police and the defence secretary\u2026"
