    "md5": "ea32f91c49c148f7321b25350cacf9a3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1981,
    "chunk_text": "\u2018\u2026India\u2019s warning to the State Intelligence Service arrived on April 4, 2019, followed by further information on April 18 and 19; on the evening of the 20th and again at first light on the 21st, the head of the SIS passed his own warnings to the inspector general of police and the defence secretary\u2026\n\n\u2026On April 7 a top-secret letter reached Sisira Mendis, the Chief of National Intelligence. It set out the same warning and added the methods the group might use: a suicide attack, an armed attack, a knife attack, an attack with a truck.\n\nOn April 8 the defence secretary was told, and advised that the police be informed.\n\nOn April 9 the security chiefs met. That same day Jayawardena sent the inspector general of police a report identifying four of the six men India had named.\n\n\u2026Then, on April 20, the Indian counterpart messaged Jayawardena again. He wanted feedback on what he had sent at the start of the month. He added that the attack was expected \u201cat any time on or before 21.04.2019,\u201d and that a dry run had already been carried out at Kattankudy.\n\nThat was the same evening a former Sea Tiger in Puthukudiyiruppu took a call from an Indian police officer and relayed the warning to his handler in Vavuniya.\n\nThe last message came at 8.27 the next morning. It said the attackers would probably move within hours. The first bomb went off eighteen minutes later\u2026\u2019\n\nAs respected author of several books on the LTTE war, MR Narayan Swamy has underscored:\n\n\u2018\u2026It is by now public knowledge that an Indian agency passed on highly credible intelligence which, had it been acted upon, could not only have failed the murder conspiracy but also led to the arrests of the bombers. Sadly, the inputs received were not followed up. No amount of planning by the terrorists and no amount of overt or covert help they allegedly received from anyone within Sri Lanka or outside could have succeeded in killing people en masse if the warnings had been heeded\u2026\u2019"
  },
