    "chunk_size_bytes": 1837,
    "chunk_text": "Their names are all known from previous inquiries. Suresh Sallay isn\u2019t one of them. His name seems only to crop up in Azad Maulana\u2019s clip in the TV program. Is he a scapegoat or red herring? He has the wrong profile--not have enough seniority and personal authority to be the mastermind; too junior, youthful, lightweight. Shouldn\u2019t the mastermind have been a heavyweight; some former covert operations chieftain committed to a certain political outcome, who once had authority over them all; someone who remained and remains in the shadows?\n\nThese unprovoked attacks on Muslim targets outside the East by extremist ethnoreligious majoritarian groups, gave the opening for Zahran Hashim to discuss, train for and plan violent attacks on Sinhala targets in the country at large.\n\nPerhaps these were two prongs of one plot, or consecutive steps up the escalation ladder:\n\n(a) Create or encourage the creation of Islamophobic Sinhala-Buddhist extremist organisations and discourse and provoke the Eastern Wahhabi fundamentalists to shift focus from exercising cultural domination over Eastern Muslims, to targeting the Sinhala people.\n\n(b) Ignore the information about the Zahran network and the terrorist build-up, and divert attention to the non-existent LTTE.\n\n(c) Allow the attacks to happen against Sinhala Christian sites and worshippers.\n\n(d) By-pass and override the Cardinal\u2019s successful attempts to stop an anti-Muslim backlash, and enhance an anti-Muslim backlash outside the areas where Christians were a majority or significant minority, in Sinhala-Buddhist majority areas, though the Sinhala-Buddhists hadn\u2019t been targets\u2014thus rousing a tsunami of Sinhala-Buddhist ultranationalism.\n\n(e) Use that ultranationalism as ramp to enable the Sinhala-Buddhist extremist candidate to catapult to the candidacy and victory."
