    "chunk_text": "Was the \u2018failure/delay\u2019 to act on the Easter warnings the same tactical thinking that a few years later, made Netanyahu (according to Haaretz) refrain from communicating the warnings from the UAE about the Hamas attack of October 7th?\n\nDouglas Devananda was in his early 20s when he was first detained at the CID\u2019s headquarters on the infamous Fourth Floor in the early 1980s.\n\nThat\u2019s the tragic cycle of the true anti-fascist hero in \u2018the Upside Down\u2019 i.e., present day Sri Lanka after two years of rule by AKD-JVP-NPP.\n\nI am glad that the response to Maitreyi Ramakrishnan \u2018from Tamil Eelam\u2019 whose far more serious transgression is to publicly accuse Sri Lanka of \u2018genocide\u2019, has not been limited to the Sinhala ultranationalists whose discordant discourse turns everybody off.\n\nI draw the readers\u2019 attention to two young voices, representing a post-Aragalaya discourse.\n\nI don\u2019t know the name of this young lady, but she and her partner post under the tag ChrisnCrys. Hers is the perfect postwar non-racist response to the \u2018Tamil Eelam/Genocide\u2019 discourse: \u201cSo tired of this discourse. It\u2019s 2026. Let\u2019s move forward.\u201d (https://www.facebook.com/reel/1226928786316887)\n\nThe other youngster is Riz Razak. He has a superbly articulate rebuttal of the \u2018genocide\u2019 allegation by Maitreyi Ramakrishnan. (https://www.facebook.com/reel/2104942370907883)"
