    "md5": "87729dfe9134310802796a585a2ad32a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1830,
    "chunk_text": "Keells marks 35 years of keeping life fresh for Sri Lanka\n\nFor Keells, freshness has always meant more than what reaches a supermarket shelf. It represents a commitment built over 35 years to improving everyday experiences, strengthening communities and creating opportunities for the people connected to its journey.\n\nAs Keells surpasses its 150th outlet milestone, reflecting on a journey where freshness has always been more than what reaches the shelf; it is reflected in the way Keells supports people, strengthens communities and creates better everyday experiences. From empowering farmers and employees to connecting families with fresh choices, Keells has continued to bring this belief to life through freshness, convenience, trust and care, improving the quality of life for the nation. It is not a new promise, but an outlook that has guided Keells from the very beginning.\n\nSince opening its first store at Liberty Plaza, Colombo in 1991, Keells has evolved alongside changing consumer needs, moving beyond traditional retail to create a connected ecosystem that supports customers, farmers, suppliers, employees, and communities. Today, with 150 stores across Sri Lanka, the brand continues to build on its purpose of improving the quality of life for the nation.w\n\nFor customers, this journey is reflected in the everyday choices and experiences Keells continues to create. From farm-fresh produce and prepared food offerings to an expanding range of products, new food experiences and digital innovations such as the Keells Nexus App, the brand continues to evolve around the changing needs of Sri Lankan households. The Nexus ecosystem now connects with 2.9 million members, offering a more personalised and accessible omnichannel experience through relevant promotions, personalised offers and exclusive rewards."
  },
