    "chunk_text": "Port City Colombo builds investment momentum across UAE, Oman, and Qatar\n\nPort City Colombo Delegation meeting with Ministry of Commerce, Industry and Investment Promotion Royal Advisor for Foreign Trade and International Cooperation Pankaj Khimji, and Undersecretary for Commerce and Industry Ghalib bin Saeed bin Majid Al Maamari\n\nHigh-level engagements strengthen regional partnerships and advance Port City Colombo\u2019s Gulf investment strategy\n\nPort City Colombo hosted an exclusive investor forum at The St. Regis Abu Dhabi on 25 September 2026, bringing together senior UAE business leaders, investors, and institutional stakeholders for a focused morning of dialogue on Sri Lanka\u2019s investment proposition and the opportunities available within Port City Colombo\u2019s Special Economic Zone.\n\nThe forum formed the centrepiece of a structured seven-day Gulf roadshow spanning Abu Dhabi, Muscat, and Doha \u2014 reflecting the sustained and growing interest from the Gulf investment community in Port City Colombo following a series of high-profile engagements across the region throughout 2026.\n\nThe roadshow is a direct response to the momentum generated by Port City Colombo\u2019s Gulf outreach program this year, and the specific appetite from Abu Dhabi\u2019s distinct institutional and sovereign investment community for a more focused and substantive engagement with Sri Lanka\u2019s investment proposition."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-10-01-dailyftlk-741c9226",
    "num": "dailyftlk-741c9226",
    "date_str": "2026-10-01",
    "description": "Port City Colombo builds investment momentum across UAE, Oman, and Qatar",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/Port-City-Colombo-builds-investment-momentum-across-UAE-Oman-and-Qatar/34-798021",
    "lang": "en",
