    "chunk_text": "\u201cAbu Dhabi\u2019s rise as a premier global trading and investment hub is driven by its strategic location at the crossroads of East and West, its massive sovereign wealth, and its progressive regulatory framework,\u201d he said. \u201cIn many ways, Sri Lanka shares some of the same strategic advantages, such as its location in the heart of the Indian Ocean and its natural deep-water ports. It is this shared geographic strength that creates a strong foundation for collaboration between our two countries and investors. Port City Colombo is not a mere development project. It is a strategic national initiative designed to position Sri Lanka as a neutral, wholly connected platform for businesses, linking South Asia with the Middle East, Asia, and beyond.\u201d\n\nBringing the formal proceedings to a close, Colombo Port City Economic Commission Director Commercial Radika Obeyesekere, acknowledged the invaluable support extended by the Embassy of Sri Lanka in the UAE in making the forum a success.\n\nCommenting on the significance of Port City Colombo\u2019s Gulf roadshow, CHEC Port City Colombo\u00a0 Ltd., Managing Director Xiong Hongfeng said: \u201cThe depth of engagement we have seen across this roadshow \u2014 from Muscat to Abu Dhabi to Doha \u2014 reflects a growing recognition among Gulf investors that Port City Colombo offers a credible and familiar platform for accessing South Asia\u2019s growth story. We look forward to translating these conversations into concrete investment partnerships.\u201d\n\nThe Abu Dhabi forum was preceded by a series of high-level bilateral meetings in Muscat, where the Port City Colombo delegation engaged with senior representatives of Khazaen Economic City, the Oman Chamber of Commerce and Industry (OCCI), and the Ministry of Commerce, Industry and Investment Promotion."
