    "chunk_text": "The Abu Dhabi forum was preceded by a series of high-level bilateral meetings in Muscat, where the Port City Colombo delegation engaged with senior representatives of Khazaen Economic City, the Oman Chamber of Commerce and Industry (OCCI), and the Ministry of Commerce, Industry and Investment Promotion.\n\nBuilding on the strong foundation established through Port City Colombo\u2019s Muscat investor forum in June 2026 and the subsequent reciprocal delegation visit to Port City Colombo in August, discussions focused on bilateral trade and investment opportunities, the Oman\u2013South Asia investment and trade corridor, and pathways for Omani businesses and institutions to establish a presence within Port City Colombo\u2019s SEZ framework.\n\nThe roadshow concluded in Doha with a significant meeting with Qatar Chamber of Commerce and Industry First Vice Chairman Mohamed bin Ahmed bin Twar marking an important step in further strengthening Port City Colombo\u2019s engagement with Qatar\u2019s business and investment community. The fruitful discussion was facilitated by the Embassy of Sri Lanka in the State of Qatar and led by Ambassador of Sri Lanka to Qatar Sithara Khan.\n\nThe delegation also held dedicated discussions with senior Embassy officials and engaged with senior representatives of the Qatar\u2013Sri Lanka Business Council, the Sri Lanka Coordinating Committee (SLCC), and the Sri Lanka Business and Professional Council (SLBPC).\n\nTogether, these high-level engagements further deepened Port City Colombo\u2019s ongoing outreach in Qatar, strengthening institutional and business relationships and creating new avenues for sustained dialogue, collaboration and cross border investment ties."
