    "md5": "3fb25bbbb35ba76c1ad9fbfabca417a9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1879,
    "chunk_text": "Reliance Consumer Products CEO keynotes SLEIS 2026\n\nReliance Consumer Products Ltd., CEO T. Krishnakumar, popularly known as KK, will deliver the keynote address on the opening day of the Sri Lanka Economic and Investment Summit 2026, bringing more than four decades of experience across leading consumer brands and FMCG markets to the Summit\u2019s discussions on Sri Lanka\u2019s growth and investment opportunities.\n\nOrganised by The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce, SLEIS 2026 will take place on 12 and 13 October 2026 at the Shangri-La Colombo under the theme \u201cPositioning Sri Lanka in a Changing Global Economy: Resilience, Reform, and the Future of Economic Policy.\u201d\n\nKK has built a 41-year career across consumer brands and FMCG markets in India and other developing and emerging economies. He previously served as President of Coca-Cola India and Southwest Asia, where he shaped business strategy and drove revenue growth across the region.\n\nHe now leads Reliance Consumer Products Limited, where he is building the company\u2019s presence across multiple categories and developing new customers, partnerships, strategic alliances and market opportunities.\n\nHis experience offers an incisive perspective on how businesses assess markets, respond to changing consumer demand and build for growth. His participation at SLEIS 2026 comes as Sri Lanka looks to attract investment, strengthen its domestic market and deepen its links with the wider Asian economy.\n\nKK holds an MBA in Marketing from the Indian Institute of Management Bangalore and a BE (Hons) from the College of Engineering Guindy. He also completed an Advanced Management Program at Wharton Business School.\n\nHis keynote will form part of the Summit\u2019s wider discussions on how Sri Lanka can turn economic reform and emerging opportunities into sustained growth, investment and stronger private sector participation."
  },
