    "md5": "d3233ce0a47415d7c4d40d4e7229fdca",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1858,
    "chunk_text": "Akram Cassim re-elected SLGJA President for third term\n\nAkram Cassim was re-elected President of the Sri Lanka Gem and Jewellery Association (SLGJA) for a third term at the Association\u2019s Annual General Meeting held recently.\n\nThe AGM also elected a new Board representing a strong mix of youth and experience, bringing together members from across the gem, jewellery and lapidary sectors and from key gem and jewellery regions of Sri Lanka.\n\nJoining Cassim in the new leadership team are Shezan Mansoor as Vice President and COO; Shezard Careem as Head of the Jewellery Segment; Razni Haniffa as Head of the Gem Segment; Amanda Wijemanne as Head of the Lapidary Segment; Shezmin Munsoor as Head of Promotions and FACETS; and Nawrooz Azmi as Head of Finance.\n\nCassim said he was delighted with the composition of the new Board and its broad representation across the industry.\n\n\u201cWe have a well-balanced Board combining experience with a new generation of industry leaders, representing the different sectors and regions that make up Sri Lanka\u2019s gem and jewellery industry. I believe this gives us a strong team to address the challenges before us, bring fresh ideas to the table and take the industry forward together.\u201d\n\nIn his address to the AGM, Cassim highlighted industry reform as a key priority, including continued engagement with the Industry Ministry, NGJA, EDB, Customs and other relevant authorities on tax, fiscal and regulatory matters. He noted the progress made on the importation of rough gemstones while identifying the liberalisation of gold imports as an important next step in supporting jewellery manufacturing and value-added exports.\n\nHe also highlighted the continued development of FACETS Sri Lanka, traceability, gem and jewellery tourism and greater participation by the younger generation as priorities for the Association."
  },
