    "chunk_size_bytes": 1746,
    "chunk_text": "FAAMA appoints new Executive Committee for 2026/27, targeting  $ 1 b local value-addition opportunity\n\nThe Fabric and Apparel Accessory Manufacturers Association (FAAMA) has reappointed Husni Salieh of Noyon Lanka Ltd., Chairman for the 2026/27 term at its Annual General Meeting held on 25 September 2026 at the Hilton Colombo.\n\nThe AGM was graced virtually by Board of Investment of Sri Lanka Chairman Duminda Hulangamuwa as Chief Guest, and Export Development Board Chairman Mangala Wijesinghe in person as Guest of Honour.\n\nThe event brought together FAAMA members, industry leaders and government representatives providing an opportunity to reflect on the Association\u2019s achievements and discuss priorities for the year ahead.\n\nFAAMA is a member association of the Joint Apparel Association Forum (JAAF), the apex body representing Sri Lanka\u2019s apparel industry. JAAF Chairman Felix Fernando congratulated the new Chair and said: \u201cI am confident that the new leadership will help strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s local fabric and accessories supply chain and drive the industry towards our 2030 goals.\u201d\n\nReviewing the year, Salieh said that Sri Lanka\u2019s Fabric and Apparel Accessory industry contributes an estimated $ 800 million to $ 1 billion in export revenue as part of Sri Lanka\u2019s $ 5 billion apparel and textile exports. A significant share of raw materials is still imported.\n\n\u201cThere is a billion-dollar opportunity for more locally sourced raw materials as apparel in the country looks to grow from $ 5 billion to $ 8 billion by 2030,\u201d he said. \u201cMany of the challenges our industry faces cannot be addressed by any one company, association or institution working independently. They require a collective industry response.\u201d"
  },
