    "chunk_size_bytes": 1802,
    "chunk_text": "IGP orders criminal probe into Colombo Port drug seizure\n\nColombo, Oct 01 (Daily Mirror) - The Inspector General of Police (IGP) has directed the Criminal Investigation Department (CID) to conduct a formal criminal investigation into alleged negligence and delays by police officers in handling intelligence related to a major illicit drug consignment seized at the Colombo Port on August 31, 2026.\n\nThe decision follows an interim investigation by the Police Special Investigation Unit (SIU), which found that officers responsible for acting on an initial intelligence report had allegedly failed to take appropriate action.\n\nAccording to the Police, Senior Deputy Inspector General of Police (SDIG) Ranmal Kodituwakku received intelligence on August 14 that two containers containing illegal drugs had been imported into Sri Lanka and were located at the Colombo International Container Terminals (CICT).\n\nThe information was forwarded to the Police Narcotic Bureau (PNB) on the same day. However, after it was found that appropriate action had not been taken, the IGP ordered the SIU to conduct an internal inquiry.\n\nThe SIU's interim findings indicated alleged negligence and dereliction of duty by officers assigned to act on the initial intelligence. The unit recommended that a comprehensive criminal investigation be conducted alongside the ongoing departmental inquiry.\n\nThe investigation also revealed that Sub-Inspector Ekanayake of the Central Crimes Investigation Bureau (CCIB) received separate information about the same consignment from a personal informant on August 22.\n\nPolice said SI Ekanayake acted immediately on the information. A team led by the Director of the CCIB went to the Colombo Port on August 31 and began scanning the containers in coordination with Customs officials."
  },
