    "chunk_size_bytes": 1900,
    "chunk_text": "Every child must have equal opportunity to realise their potential: President\n\nColombo, Oct. 1 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake said every child should have equal and fair opportunities to realise their potential, pursue their dreams and shape the future they wish for themselves, irrespective of their background.\n\nIn his World Children\u2019s Day message issued for today (October 1), the President said children were the most valuable asset of a nation and that ensuring their physical and mental well-being and creating an environment conducive to their proper development were among the primary responsibilities of any government.\n\nHe said the country being built for children should not merely be one prepared to be handed over to them in the future, but one that gives space to their dreams today, listens to their voices and provides opportunities for them to realise their potential.\n\n\u201cFor the best interests of children, we are taking the necessary steps to ensure equal access to education, guidance, social protection, opportunities for sport, leisure and recreation, proper nutrition and access to healthcare, while protecting children from all forms of violence and discrimination and safeguarding their rights,\u201d he said.\n\nPresident Dissanayake said that race, religion, economic status, geographical background or any other circumstance should not become a barrier to a child\u2019s education or proper development.\n\nHe said the Government had already begun the process of reforming Sri Lanka\u2019s education system and transforming it towards a skills-based system suited to the modern world, while ensuring that it did not place a burden on parents or cause distress to children.\n\n\u201cOur aim is to ensure that no child is left behind in the new Sri Lanka we are building, and to provide every child with opportunities for development in a safe environment,\u201d he said."
  },
