    "md5": "23d24d0f141826c1a62f0a74bac664d4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1300,
    "chunk_text": "He said the Government had already begun the process of reforming Sri Lanka\u2019s education system and transforming it towards a skills-based system suited to the modern world, while ensuring that it did not place a burden on parents or cause distress to children.\n\n\u201cOur aim is to ensure that no child is left behind in the new Sri Lanka we are building, and to provide every child with opportunities for development in a safe environment,\u201d he said.\n\nHe also said the Government was steering the country\u2019s economy towards a stable direction in order to provide children with a safe and happy childhood free from the effects of an unstable economy.\n\nAt the same time, he said the national operation \u201cA Nation United\u201d (Ratama Ekata) had been launched to bring people together to protect the younger generation from the threat of illicit drugs.\n\nPresident Dissanayake also commended the Ministry of Women and Child Affairs for organising this year\u2019s World Children\u2019s Day celebrations under the theme \u201cStrong Minds \u2013 Enriched Children\u201d, declaring a National Children\u2019s Day Week and conducting programmes aimed at strengthening children\u2019s rights, well-being, protection, education and freedom.\n\nHe extended his heartfelt wishes to all children in Sri Lanka on World Children\u2019s Day."
