    "chunk_text": "The Executive Centre expands Sri Lankan footprint\n\nTo offer more than 150+ workstations, bringing TEC\u2019s signature hospitality-led workspace experience to one of Colombo\u2019s most prestigious business addresses\n\nThe Executive Centre (TEC), a premium flexible workspace provider, is set to further strengthen its presence in Sri Lanka with the launch of a new, state-of-the-art centre at Level 33, East Tower, World Trade Centre Colombo, scheduled to open on December 1, 2026.\n\nLocated within one of Colombo\u2019s most prestigious commercial addresses, the new centre spans approximately 8,900 sq. ft. and offers over 150 workstations, reinforcing TEC\u2019s commitment to meeting the growing demand for premium, flexible workspaces in Sri Lanka. The expansion builds on the success of TEC\u2019s existing centres in Colombo, where the company has consistently served multinational corporations, financial institutions and high-growth enterprises seeking world-class workplace solutions.\n\nDesigned in line with TEC\u2019s global standards, the new centre combines sophisticated interiors with thoughtfully curated amenities to create a seamless workplace experience. Members will have access to elegantly designed private offices, collaborative coworking spaces, premium meeting rooms, phone booths and hospitality-inspired member lounges, complemented by TEC\u2019s signature personalised service and enterprise-grade technology.\n\nAs organisations increasingly prioritise workplace quality, flexibility and employee experience, TEC\u2019s investment in WTC Colombo offers businesses the agility to scale rapidly without compromising on corporate prestige."
