    "description": "Markss-George Steuart Health expand access to healthcare solutions across Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-news/Markss-George-Steuart-Health-expand-access-to-healthcare-solutions-across-Sri-Lanka/273-351496",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1790830428.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-10-01-dailymirrorlk-77097bc6-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "56aae97c39c9b09ee2642137fc1799c7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1784,
    "chunk_text": "Markss-George Steuart Health expand access to healthcare solutions across Sri Lanka\n\nFrom left: George Steuart Health Finance Director Thulitha J., Markss CCO Damian Silva, Markss CEO Sajeevan W., PC Shanaka Wijesinghe PC of Markss, Markss Chairman Rajeev N., George Steuart Health Executive Director Sanjiva W., George Steuart Health Managing Director Erandajith R. and George Steuart Health Director Thushantha N.\n\nMarkss HLC, a Sri Lankan healthcare company celebrating its 20th anniversary this month and George Steuart Health (GS Health), the healthcare vertical of George Steuart & Company, yesterday announced a strategic partnership covering the marketing and distribution of selected products from Markss\u2019 pharmaceutical portfolio.\n\nUnder the partnership, GS Health will leverage its established nationwide distribution network, experienced field force and long-standing relationships with pharmacies, hospitals and the medical community to expand the reach and availability of selected Markss pharmaceutical products across Sri Lanka.\n\nThe partnership enables Markss to further strengthen its focus on the critical care segment, where the company has established a strong presence, while continuing to invest in and accelerate the introduction of advanced healthcare solutions currently in its pipeline.\n\nThe collaboration also represents the beginning of a broader strategic relationship between the two companies, with both Markss and GS Health committed to exploring opportunities to further strengthen and expand the partnership in the future.\n\n\u201cAs Markss celebrates 20 years of serving Sri Lanka\u2019s healthcare community, this partnership with George Steuart Health marks an important step in our next chapter,\u201d said Markss founder and Chairman Rajiv Nanayakkara."
  },
