    "md5": "dbb32b925cb624089cc91d2c2461fbf8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 945,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cAs Markss celebrates 20 years of serving Sri Lanka\u2019s healthcare community, this partnership with George Steuart Health marks an important step in our next chapter,\u201d said Markss founder and Chairman Rajiv Nanayakkara.\n\n\u201cGS Health is pleased to partner with Markss and support the wider reach of its selected pharmaceutical products through our established distribution capabilities,\u201d said GS Health Managing Director Erandajith Ranasinghe.\n\n\u201cThis collaboration is an opportunity for both organisations to build a strong and sustainable relationship, while contributing to greater access to quality healthcare solutions across Sri Lanka. We look forward to further developing the partnership in the years ahead.\u201d\n\nThe agreement was formally signed last week by Sajeevan Wickramasingha, who assumes the role of Managing Director of Markss, effective October 01, 2026 and George Steuart Health Managing Director Erandajith Ranasinghe."
