    "description": "BOC marks World Children\u2019s Day with focus on preparing young Sri Lankans for future",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-news/BOC-marks-World-Childrens-Day-with-focus-on-preparing-young-Sri-Lankans-for-future/273-351498",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1790830619.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-10-01-dailymirrorlk-0956aeea-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "57a7f2abbc1cda938e58eea3f1f54ff7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1877,
    "chunk_text": "BOC marks World Children\u2019s Day with focus on preparing young Sri Lankans for future\n\nSenior Deputy General Manager and Head of Development and Branch Banking Badra Kalyanapriya Gurusinghe\n\nAs Sri Lanka marks the World Children\u2019s Day, Bank of Ceylon (BOC) is highlighting the role that the parents, families and financial institutions can play in helping children develop these skills while also creating a financial foundation for their education and future needs.\n\nAt the centre of BOC\u2019s offering for children is Ran Kekulu, its dedicated children\u2019s savings account. While the account enables the parents and guardians to build savings for a child over time, BOC sees its purpose as extending beyond the amount accumulated \u2013 encouraging children to participate in saving.\n\nRan Kekulu also provides benefits aimed at supporting children and their families beyond conventional savings. These include insurance coverage for guardians of up to Rs.1 million, Rs.30 million worth of scholarships for 2,000 high achievers annually, Grade 5 Scholarship seminars, 10,000 gift items for students who qualify for the Grade 5 Scholarship and additional Grade 5 Scholarship opportunities for differently abled students, subject to applicable terms and conditions.\n\n\u201cThe Children\u2019s Day is an opportunity to think not only about what we can give our children today but also about how well we are preparing them for tomorrow. Teaching children to understand the savings habit, to save towards something they want and to make responsible choices are lessons that can remain relevant throughout their lives. Through Ran Kekulu, Haritha Kekulu, Diyawara Kekulu and PFC Minor for children, BOC aims to support both children and parents as they build that foundation,\u201d said BOC Senior Deputy General Manager and Head of Development and Branch Banking Badra Kalyanapriya Gurusinghe."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-10-01-dailymirrorlk-0956aeea",
