    "chunk_size_bytes": 1964,
    "chunk_text": "Akram Cassim re-elected as SLGJA President for 3rd term\n\nFrom left: Incoming office bearers Shezmin Mansoor, Razni Haniffa, Shezard Careem, Akram Cassim, Shezan Mansoor, Nawrooz Azmi and Amanda Wijemanne From left: Incoming office bearers Shezmin Mansoor, Razni Haniffa, Shezard Careem, Akram Cassim, Shezan Mansoor, Nawrooz Azmi and Amanda Wijemanne\n\nAkram Cassim was re-elected as President of the Sri Lanka Gem and Jewellery Association (SLGJA) for a third term, at the association\u2019s Annual General Meeting (AGM) held this week.\n\nThe AGM also elected a new board representing a strong mix of youth and experience, bringing together the members from across the gem, jewellery and lapidary sectors and from key gem and jewellery regions of Sri Lanka.\n\nJoining Cassim in the new leadership team are Shezan Mansoor as Vice President and COO, Shezard Careem as Head of Jewellery Segment, Razni Haniffa as Head of Gem Segment, Amanda Wijemanne as Head of Lapidary Segment, Shezmin Munsoor as Head of Promotions and FACETS and Nawrooz Azmi as Head of Finance.\n\nCassim said he was delighted with the composition of the new board and its broad representation across the industry.\n\n\u201cWe have a well-balanced board combining experience with a new generation of industry leaders, representing the different sectors and regions that make up Sri Lanka\u2019s gem and jewellery industry. I believe this gives us a strong team to address the challenges before us, bring fresh ideas to the table and take the industry forward together.\u201d\n\nIn his address to the AGM, Cassim highlighted industry reform as a key priority, including continued engagement with the Industries Ministry, NGJA, EDB, Customs and other relevant authorities on tax, fiscal and regulatory matters.\n\nHe noted the progress made on the importation of rough gemstones while identifying the liberalisation of gold imports as an important next step in supporting jewellery manufacturing and value-added exports."
