    "chunk_text": "He noted the progress made on the importation of rough gemstones while identifying the liberalisation of gold imports as an important next step in supporting jewellery manufacturing and value-added exports.\n\nLooking ahead to FACETS Sri Lanka 2027, its 34th edition, Cassim called on the entire industry to support the exhibition by bringing international buyers and sponsors to Sri Lanka and using their global networks to further strengthen the show.\n\nHe also welcomed G\u00fcbelin Gem Lab as an official partner of FACETS 2027.\n\nWith the SLGJA marking its 25th anniversary next year, Cassim said the milestone was an opportunity to celebrate the association\u2019s achievements while setting an ambitious direction for the future.\n\n\u201cWe have a proud heritage, a remarkable industry and tremendous potential. With confidence, ambition and shared purpose, we can strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s position on the world stage.\u201d\n\nHe summed up the association\u2019s direction for the year ahead in three words: \u201cOne industry, one vision, one voice\u201d.\n\nMeanwhile, Vice President and COO Shezan Mansoor added, \u201cI believe, with the collective support and participation of our membership, under the guidance and leadership of the new board, we can continue to strengthen the association and move forward together - better and stronger.\u201d\n\nSLGJA board 2026-27: 1. Akram Cassim \u2013 President, 2. Shezan Mansoor \u2013 Vice President | COO, 3. Amanda Wijemanne \u2013 Vice President \u2013 Lapidary, 4. Shezard Careem \u2013 Vice President \u2013 Jewellery, 5. Razni Haniffa \u2013 Vice President \u2013 Gem Segment, 6. Nawrooz Azmi \u2013 Vice President \u2013 Finance, 7. Shezmin Mansoor \u2013 Vice President \u2013 Promotions, 8. D. Balasubramanium \u2013 Assistant Vice President \u2013 Operations, 9. Ashfaq Deen \u2013 Assistant Vice President \u2013 Finance"
