    "chunk_text": "Rajapaksa further said that he had not been involved in any operation on the ground,\u00a0 and that his duty as Defence Secretary was to convey policies adopted by the Government to those institutions. When asked whether he was aware of abductions and disappearances that happened in the country,\u00a0 he said that these were \u201cmatters presented with the intention of gaining political advantage and that there is no truth in them.\u201d He said that these were said with the intention of damaging the reputation of the country.\n\nPeople including victims have been longing for answers. But when former political leaders respond in such a manner, the quest for accountability becomes a series of dead-ends.\n\nBut when accountability becomes a lost memory, it does more harm than good to a society and the principle of democracy.\n\n\u2018Your Thought\u2019 is a space, a right of the readers to support or contradict and discuss the issues highlighted in the editorial and other articles in the editorial and op-ed pages. Designed as the reader\u2019s editorial; our readers can send in their writings, with a word count not exceeding 200, to \u2018Your Thought\u2019, Daily Mirror Political Features Desk, No 8, Hunupitiya Cross Road, Colombo 2 or email to [email\u00a0protected]"
