    "chunk_size_bytes": 768,
    "chunk_text": "Please Maintain Our Street Lights\n\nStreet lighting is an essential part of road safety. It helps pedestrians and motorists see one another and identify junctions, crossings and other hazards at night. Unfortunately, many street lights remain out of order for long periods. Though a faulty light may seem a minor matter, an unlit road or junction can create serious risks for all road users. The authorities responsible should regularly inspect street lights and repair faults without delay. There should also be a simple system for the public to report defective lights and have complaints promptly attended to. Street lights are public facilities maintained with public funds. Keeping them working should be treated as a basic responsibility, not an optional service."
