    "chunk_text": "Apart from these shifts, no leader who claimed they would alter the course of political history actually did so. The best example of this is the repeated promise made by various parties to completely abolish the Executive Presidency. Chandrika Kumaratunga was the first to give such a promise in 1994. However, she did not possess the required two-thirds majority. Although the then United National Party (UNP) leader Gamini Dissanayake stated at one stage that he was ready to offer the opposition support to pass it, Chandrika did not follow through. To this day, that system of governance remains in practice.\n\nIn Sri Lanka, political parties campaign during elections as if they are bitter ideological enemies of other parties. However, except for J.R. Jayewardene, who fundamentally altered the structure of the system of governance, all subsequent leaders have merely driven the same vehicle handed down to them without ever reversing the course of history."
