    "chunk_text": "India will always support Sri Lanka\u2019s progress, prosperity: Jaishankar tells Tilvin\n\nHindu: Indian External Affairs Minister S. Jaishankar met with Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna General Secretary Tilvin Silva and his delegation from Sri Lanka this morning.\n\nA five-member delegation of Sri Lanka\u2019s ruling Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna (JVP) had arrived in India for a five-day visit from September 27 to October 1, 2026, as part of JVP-BJP meeting.\n\nFollowing his interaction with the Mr. Silva, Mr. Jaishankar posted on X that it was pleasure to meet him and his Sri Lankan delegation.\n\n\u201cHad a good discussion on strengthening our deep bonds of friendship,\u201d he said on his X post.\n\nHe further added, \u201cAs a trusted partner, India will always support Sri Lanka\u2019s progress and prosperity.\u201d\n\nThis is Mr. Silva\u2019s second visit to India. Following his visit in February, Mr. Silva had spoken of the need to shift the stance of the Sri Lankan party (National People\u2019s Power) that once vehemently resisted India.\n\nApart from Mr. Silva, the JVP\u2019s central committee member Chandrika Adikari, Member of Parliament Aboobucker Athambawa, district committee member Kabilan Suntharamoorthy, and member of international department Kalpana Madhubhashini, was also part of the delegation.\n\n\u201cThe visit aims to strengthen BJP-JVP engagement, facilitate the exchange of organisational experiences and further deepen ties between the two political parties,\u201d the in-charge of BJP\u2019s foreign affairs department Vijay Chauthaiwale said."
