    "chunk_text": "Tilvin meets Jaishankar as  BJP-hosted visit to India concludes\n\nIndian External Affairs Minister S. Jaishankar met Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna (JVP) General Secretary Tilvin Silva and his delegation in New Delhi on the final day of their five-day visit to India.\n\nJaishankar said the two sides had a \u2018good discussion\u2019 on strengthening the bonds of friendship between the two countries. \u201cAs a trusted partner, India will always support Sri Lanka\u2019s progress and prosperity,\u201d he said in a social media post.\n\nSilva led a five-member JVP delegation to India from 27 September to 1 October at the invitation of India\u2019s ruling Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP), under its \u2018Know BJP\u2019 program. The JVP is the main constituent party of Sri Lanka\u2019s ruling National People\u2019s Power (NPP). The BJP said the visit was intended to strengthen engagement between the two parties, exchange organisational experience and deepen ties.\n\nThe delegation comprised Silva, JVP Central Committee Member Chandrika Adikari, MP Aboobucker Athambawa, District Committee Member Kabilan Suntharamoorthy and International Department Member Kalpana Madhubhashini.\n\nThe delegation held talks with BJP National General Secretary (Organisation) B.L. Santhosh and other senior party figures on the BJP\u2019s organisational structure, grassroots membership network and development programs in India. Earlier discussions during the visit also touched on Indian fishermen, refugee resettlement and cooperation between the two countries.\n\nThe delegation also met Delhi Chief Minister Rekha Gupta and was welcomed at the Delhi BJP office by Delhi BJP President Harsh Malhotra. Its program included meetings with the BJP\u2019s women\u2019s and youth organisations and visits to the Indian Parliament and the National War Memorial."
