    "md5": "3295b0ce383a22e00a0fb02e104b18be",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1991,
    "chunk_text": "IGP says CA Sri Lanka\u2019s newly launched Faculty  of Forensic Accounting  a timely national initiative\n\nFrom left: CA Sri Lanka President Tishan Subasinghe, Inspector General of Police Priyantha Weerasooriya, CA Sri Lanka Vice President Anoji de Silva and Forensic Accounting and Investigation Committee Chairman Ashane Jayasekera\n\nThe Inspector General of Police (IGP) Priyantha Weerasooriya last week commended the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka (CA Sri Lanka), highlighting that the newly launched specialised Faculty of Forensic Accounting and Investigation was a timely national initiative.\n\nSpeaking at the launch ceremony held at the Institute, IGP Weerasooriya, who was the Chief Guest at the occasion, said: \u201cLaw enforcement agencies, including the Sri Lanka Police, require strong collaboration with highly trained professional accountants and forensic experts. By building specialised human capital, expertise and modern investigative competencies, CA Sri Lanka is directly contributing to strengthening our nation\u2019s resilience against economic crimes.\u201d\n\nHe also said modern financial crimes, cyber fraud, money laundering and complex corporate irregularities are no longer confined within local boundaries. They have become sophisticated, highly networked and highly globalised.\n\n\u201cIn our present Sri Lankan context, as our country moves steadily towards economic recovery and long-term financial stability, safeguarding our financial infrastructure is paramount. Criminal activities such as financial fraud not only drain economic resources but also damage institutional integrity and investor confidence.\u201d\n\nHe made these comments in the presence of Guest of Honour Deputy Inspector General of Police (DIG), Financial Crimes Investigation Division (FCID), M. D. P. Dayaratne, as well as CA Sri Lanka\u2019s President Tishan Subasinghe, Vice President Anoji de Silva, Forensic Accounting and Investigation Committee Chairman Ashane Jayasekera among others."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
