    "chunk_text": "TIN becomes gateway to key transactions: What changes from 1 November 2026?\n\nMandatory submission of the TIN Certificate introduces a new compliance checkpoint across banking, property, vehicles and business registration\n\nThis article is based principally on Inland Revenue Department Circular No. SEC/2026/E/07 dated 22 September 2026, issued under the Inland Revenue Act, No. 24 of 2017 as amended by the Inland Revenue (Amendment) Act, No. 11 of 2026. The Circular is addressed to banks and financial institutions, local authorities, the Department of Motor Traffic, Provincial Revenue Commissioners, Divisional Secretaries, the Registrar General\u2019s Department, the Registrar General of Companies, credit-card issuing institutions and other relevant Government institutions"
