    "chunk_size_bytes": 864,
    "chunk_text": "And most importantly, did we prevent another child from experiencing the same thing?\n\nAnd organisations that work in the field of child protection have a responsibility to ensure that their work does not end with a programme, a publication, a pledge or a photograph.\n\nSomewhere, a child is trying to decide whether an adult can be trusted.\n\nThe question is whether we are prepared to do something about it.\n\nSo celebrate them today. Let them have the cake. Let them have the ice cream. Let them sing. Let them dance. Let them make their art. Let them have their day.\n\nBut tomorrow, when the decorations come down and the photographs stop appearing on our feeds, the protection must continue. Because the greatest gift we can give a child is not a celebration for a day.\n\n(The author is an Attorney-At-Law and Founder/Senior Legal Consultant Child Protection Force)"
