    "chunk_size_bytes": 1043,
    "chunk_text": "ASPI falls 2.46% in Sept., down 8% for year\n\nThird quarter erases most of second-quarter recovery, following March\u2019s 11.24% plunge\n\nThe All Share Price Index (ASPI) fell 2.46% in September and the S&P SL20 Index 1.92%, Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE) data showed. This was the ASPI\u2019s sixth monthly decline in the nine months of 2026, against three monthly gains.\n\nCompounding the monthly moves, the ASPI is down about 8.1% for the year to date and the S&P SL20 about 4.3%.\n\nThe market entered 2026 on firm footing, with the ASPI rising in each of the last four months of 2025 and adding 5.25% in January. It then plunged 11.24% in March, recovered partly with a 7% gain in April, and traded flat in May and June.\n\nThe ASPI fell 5.09% in July and rose 0.99% in August before September\u2019s decline. This took its third-quarter loss to about 6.5%, erasing most of the second quarter\u2019s 6.7% gain.\n\nCentral Bank data show net foreign outflows from the CSE of $ 166 million in January to August, exceeding the $ 122 million for the whole of 2025."
