    "chunk_size_bytes": 724,
    "chunk_text": "Colombo-Gampola train services resume after 10 months\n\nColombo, October 2 (Daily Mirror) - Train services on the Upcountry railway line are scheduled to resume today (Oct. 2), nearly 10 months after operations were suspended following the impact of Cyclone Ditwah, the Railway Department said.\n\nRailway Transport Superintendent Asanka Samarasinghe said train services operating from Colombo to Peradeniya and Gampola would recommence from today.\n\nHe said services on the Upcountry line had remained suspended for approximately 10 months due to damage caused by Cyclone Ditwah.\n\nThe resumption of services is expected to restore rail connectivity between Colombo and several key destinations along the Upcountry railway line."
