    "chunk_size_bytes": 1836,
    "chunk_text": "Macroeconomic stability achieved within two years: Labour Minister\n\nColombo, Oct. 2 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka has achieved macroeconomic stability within the past two years, although some experts had earlier said it could take at least five years, Labour Minister and Deputy Minister of Finance Dr. Anil Jayantha Fernando said.\n\nHe said this achievement was possible because of the contribution, cooperation and commitment of all stakeholders involved in the country\u2019s economic recovery.\n\nDr. Fernando made these remarks on September 30 at a ceremony held at the Ministry of Labour to sign the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) for the Decent Work Country Programme (DWCP) for 2026\u20132032 with the International Labour Organization (ILO).\n\nHe said the main challenge now was to build on the economic stability achieved and move the country towards economic transformation.\n\n\u201cThe main challenge before us now is to develop the right strategies to move forward from economic stability and take the country towards economic transformation,\u201d he said.\n\nHe said this transformation should support the Government\u2019s wider goal of creating \u201cA Thriving Nation \u2013 A Beautiful Life\u201d.\n\nDr. Fernando said economic growth and development were important to achieve this goal. He added that the Government had given priority to inclusive and sustainable economic growth in its Budget.\n\nHe said the Government was now preparing the 2027 Budget, which is expected to be presented later this year. The Budget is being prepared by considering the country\u2019s past and present economic situation and current needs.\n\nThe Minister also stressed the importance of decent work in the country\u2019s economic transformation. He said decent work was closely linked to workers\u2019 rights, better working conditions, dignity, freedom and democratic values."
  },
