    "chunk_size_bytes": 1961,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka promotes tourism, Ceylon Tea and cuisine in Washington\n\nWASHINGTON D.C. - Sri Lanka promoted its tourism attractions, Ceylon Tea and traditional cuisine to an American audience at a special reception hosted by the Embassy of Sri Lanka in Washington D.C. in collaboration with the International Club of DC.\n\nThe event was held on September 18, 2026, at the Embassy premises, with a large number of members of the International Club of DC attending the reception.\n\nWelcoming the guests, Charge d\u2019Affaires Madhuka Wickramachchi invited them to visit Sri Lanka and experience its rich culture, tropical beauty and hospitality.\n\nWickramachchi highlighted the exceptional diversity Sri Lanka offers tourists, particularly in terms of culture, natural beauty, history and adventure.\n\nHe also recalled the famous words of American author Mark Twain during his journey to Sri Lanka about a century ago, using the author's observations to highlight the island's enduring appeal to visitors.\n\nThe reception combined tourism promotion with a showcase of Sri Lankan culture, food and tea.\n\nSeveral Sri Lankan dance troupes from the Washington D.C., Maryland and Virginia (DMV) area performed traditional dances during the evening.\n\nThe performances gave the audience an opportunity to experience Sri Lanka's rich dance traditions through distinctive rhythms, colourful costumes and traditional movements.\n\nGuests were also served traditional Sri Lankan cuisine, giving them an opportunity to experience the country's culinary traditions, distinctive flavours and hospitality.\n\nFreshly brewed hot and iced Ceylon Tea was served to guests as part of efforts to promote Sri Lanka's globally recognised tea industry and introduce the product to a wider American audience.\n\nThe Embassy said the combination of tea, food and cultural performances created an engaging experience for the guests and helped generate greater interest in Sri Lanka as a tourism destination."
