    "chunk_text": "Freshly brewed hot and iced Ceylon Tea was served to guests as part of efforts to promote Sri Lanka's globally recognised tea industry and introduce the product to a wider American audience.\n\nThe Embassy said the combination of tea, food and cultural performances created an engaging experience for the guests and helped generate greater interest in Sri Lanka as a tourism destination.\n\nThe Embassy sought to highlight Sri Lanka as an attractive destination for affluent and niche American travellers interested in culture, adventure, natural beauty and warm hospitality.\n\nThe International Club of DC, which has members from a range of professional sectors, brought together a large and diverse group of guests for the event.\n\nThe club promotes international cultural experiences through art, music, dance and theatre, while also providing opportunities for its members to experience cuisines from different parts of the world.\n\nThe Embassy said its collaboration with the International Club of DC provided an opportunity to introduce Sri Lanka's cultural heritage, cuisine and Ceylon Tea to an audience interested in international experiences.\n\nThe reception therefore served as a platform to promote Sri Lanka beyond its traditional tourism image, presenting its culture, cuisine, tea, natural beauty and hospitality as part of a wider experience for international visitors.\n\nThe event was organised by the Embassy of Sri Lanka in Washington D.C. as part of efforts to deepen cultural links and people-to-people connections between Sri Lanka and the United States."
