    "chunk_size_bytes": 1037,
    "chunk_text": "Musk reignites Meta rivalry with \u2018Instagram is for girls\u2019 remark\n\nHindustan Times - Elon Musk has reignited his long-running rivalry with Meta and its social media platforms after saying that \u201cInstagram is for girls\u201d, sparking debate over gender stereotypes online.\n\nMusk made the comment on October 1 in response to a post by venture capitalist Geiger Capital, who said he had \u201cofficially deleted Instagram\u201d and described the platform as an \u201cinherently female app\u201d.\n\nThe comment was widely shared on X, attracting thousands of reactions and a range of responses from users.\n\nThe remark has added another episode to Musk\u2019s ongoing rivalry with Meta, which owns Instagram, Facebook and WhatsApp.\n\nThe billionaire has previously exchanged criticism with Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg and has frequently used X to comment on rival social media platforms.\n\nMusk\u2019s latest comment, however, focused on the perceived gender identity of Instagram\u2019s user base, prompting discussion about stereotypes surrounding social media use."
