    "md5": "425148ec65e2235fa6b158a00b3fcebb",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1987,
    "chunk_text": "Newburgh Ella recognised as SL\u2019s 1st certified paperless operation hotel\n\nNewburgh Ella \u2013 The Tea Factory Resort by Browns Hotels & Resorts has been recognised by the National Cleaner Production Centre (NCPC), Sri Lanka, as the first hotel in Sri Lanka to achieve a certified paperless operation, marking a significant milestone in the country\u2019s journey towards more resource-efficient and digitally enabled hospitality.\n\nThe certification was formally presented by NCPC Director General and CEO Samantha Kumarasena to Browns Hotels & Resorts CEO Eksath Wijeratne, recognising Newburgh Ella\u2019s achievement in establishing a paperless hotel operation.\n\nThe recognition is particularly significant for Newburgh Ella, a 41-room resort housed within a former tea factory dating back to 1903. A building that once relied on handwritten ledgers, registers and paper records to document the daily movement of tea, now operates through digital systems across guest services and hotel operations.\n\nNewburgh Ella\u2019s paperless approach extends far beyond replacing the printed menus or introducing digital check-in. The hotel has digitised the processes across departments, creating a connected system that allows information, approvals, monitoring and documentation to move digitally throughout the operation.\n\nThe guests can complete their registration digitally, access dining menus electronically and receive the bills and folios without the printed documents. In finance and administration, the approvals, records and documentation are managed through digital systems, reducing the need for physical files and paper-based circulation. The digital approach continues across the operational departments. The engineering teams use digital systems to monitor areas such as electricity consumption, allowing the usage to be recorded and reviewed efficiently. In the kitchen, the chefs record temperature checks digitally, creating an accessible record for food safety monitoring and audits."
  },
