    "chunk_text": "The guests can complete their registration digitally, access dining menus electronically and receive the bills and folios without the printed documents. In finance and administration, the approvals, records and documentation are managed through digital systems, reducing the need for physical files and paper-based circulation. The digital approach continues across the operational departments. The engineering teams use digital systems to monitor areas such as electricity consumption, allowing the usage to be recorded and reviewed efficiently. In the kitchen, the chefs record temperature checks digitally, creating an accessible record for food safety monitoring and audits.\n\nThe same systems make routine compliance and audit documentation more efficient. Since operational information is recorded within structured digital systems, the teams can access records when required without searching through physical files, while the managers can monitor processes and maintain documentation in a consistent and traceable manner.\n\n\u201cNewburgh Ella was created to give a historic property a new chapter without losing what makes it special. The paperless operation is part of that thinking. We have looked at the way a hotel works, from the guest journey to the back office and challenged ourselves to remove the unnecessary paper wherever technology allows us to do so. Having this work recognised by the NCPC is an important milestone for Browns Hotels & Resorts,\u201d said Wijeratne."
