    "chunk_size_bytes": 1910,
    "chunk_text": "HMD and Dialog Axiata partner to introduce new 4G Feature Phone range to Sri Lanka\n\nHMD (Human Mobile Devices), the leading European mobile phone manufacturer and maker of Nokia phones, has partnered with Dialog Axiata PLC, to officially introduce a new range of affordable 4G feature phones to Sri Lanka, including the HMD 101 4G and HMD 102 4G.\n\nCombining the legendary durability and trust of Nokia\u2019s hardware with Dialog\u2019s nationwide coverage, this strategic initiative supports the country\u2019s transition from legacy 2G networks to modern 4G LTE while prioritizing an upgraded, superior connectivity experience for local consumers.\n\nThe feature phone segment remains a vital component of Sri Lanka\u2019s mobile landscape, serving as an indispensable primary tool for daily communication in many households and a trusted, long-lasting secondary backup device for professionals and travellers seeking a digital detox.\n\nWhile migrating users from 2G to 4G is a core network objective, the focus of this partnership centres directly on elevating what local consumers value most: clear HD voice through VoLTE call quality, stronger reception, modern USB Type-C charging convenience, rugged IP52 splash resistance, and a long battery life without requiring an expensive or complex smartphone. Leading the new 4G offering, the HMD 101 4G is engineered for maximum everyday reliability and communication efficiency. It features a clear 2.0-inch display, dual SIM 4G VoLTE connectivity, a modern USB Type-C charging port, an MP3 player, wireless FM radio, and a powerful dual LED torch.\n\nComplementing this, the HMD 102 4G brings a touch of modern style to the segment, combining all core 4G features with a sleek rounded design, a smartphone-inspired camera module with rear camera and LED flash, auto call recording, and practical daily utilities making high-quality 4G hardware accessible across every budget."
