    "chunk_text": "The Plan has set an ambitious target of increasing Sri Lanka\u2019s exports to approximately US$36 Bn by 2030, comprising merchandise and services exports. Achieving this target requires coordinated implementation across government institutions, the private sector and other stakeholders.\n\nThe meeting also emphasized the need to identify implementation bottlenecks and develop practical solutions to fast-track the implementation of NEDP activities.\n\nThe discussion provided an opportunity for participating agencies to review implementation priorities, clarify institutional responsibilities and identify areas requiring greater coordination and support.\n\nDuring the meeting, the guidelines approved by the Secretary, Ministry of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development, in line with the Cabinet decision, were circulated among the Lead Implementing Agencies to guide the implementation of the NEDP 2026\u20132030.\n\nThe coordination meeting marks an important step in strengthening the institutional mechanism for implementing Sri Lanka\u2019s national export development agenda and advancing the country towards a more competitive, diversified and sustainable export economy."
