    "md5": "c98cb6118278e6d17963449c1ad9ef1d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1926,
    "chunk_text": "Kannangara sees demand building on the back of the government\u2019s move to award tenders to local construction companies. He pointed to projects such as the Kandy tunnel, multimodal transport hubs, water projects and the long-awaited Central Expressway, as well as the group\u2019s own construction requirements at Port City Colombo.\n\n\u201cThe opportunities are coming. The industry is getting opportunities as well as we are getting them. So we are ready for that, and this is something targeting all these projects,\u201d he stressed.\n\nMeanwhile, Kannangara revealed that Melwa\u2019s steel arm has obtained certification from the UK Certification Authority for Reinforcing Steels (CARES), a requirement for supplying reinforcing steel to European construction projects. The certification followed a process that took three to five years. He claimed that only three manufacturers in South Asia hold it, two of them in India, which makes Melwa the only Sri Lankan company to have it.\n\n\u201cThis is the first time we are coming out to the media with this. We have got the CARES certificate, which is a necessary certificate to export steel to the European market,\u201d he disclosed.\n\nThe certification builds on an export record that already includes shipments to neighbouring countries and Melwa\u2019s maiden 15,000-tonne consignment of reinforcement steel to Canada. Kannangara described that shipment as a first for a Sri Lankan company in the Canadian construction market.\n\nFounded in 2002 under the Melwire Group, Melwa has grown from a steel bar maker into a diversified group spanning construction steel, galvanised products and welding rods, and in 2021 it had explored a 1.3 million tonne cement plant near the Hambantota International Port. More recently, the group has partnered with Prime Group to amass around 16 acres in the Port City Colombo Marina District, making the partnership the largest property investor in the Port City."
