    "chunk_text": "BOC\u2019s market position remained a rating strength. The bank accounts for around 22 percent of banking-sector assets and deposits, while its extensive branch network and deposit franchise provide an advantage in generating business at acceptable risk, Fitch said.\n\nFitch expects stronger economic resilience to reduce BOC\u2019s earnings volatility over the medium term. Near-term profitability could face pressure from moderately higher funding costs and lower interest income from government securities.\n\nDomestic funding and liquidity conditions should also become more stable, while access to foreign-currency funding is expected to widen gradually.\n\nDespite the upgrades, Fitch affirmed BOC\u2019s Government Support Rating at \u2018ns\u2019, or \u201cno support\u201d, reflecting constraints on the state\u2019s capacity to provide extraordinary assistance.\n\nThe agency said the government\u2019s weak finances and modest foreign reserves continued to limit that capacity.\n\nFurther upgrades to BOC\u2019s long-term ratings would most likely depend on an improvement in Sri Lanka\u2019s sovereign credit profile and the banking sector\u2019s operating environment. A sovereign downgrade, a significant deterioration in operating conditions or renewed foreign-currency funding and liquidity constraints could trigger a downgrade."
