    "chunk_size_bytes": 1709,
    "chunk_text": "Determine whether attack near courts was aimed at RW\n\nColombo, Oct. 2 (Daily Mirror) - The United National Party (UNP) yesterday called for a free and fair investigation into Wednesday\u2019s incident outside the Magistrate\u2019s Court, where a cameraman allegedly attacked a security officer providing protection to former President Ranil Wickremesinghe.\n\nThe party said law enforcement authorities should determine the motive behind the attack.\n\nUNP Chairman Wajira Abeywardena, rejecting Deputy Minister Sunil Watagala\u2019s remarks that the incident was minor and not serious, said a free and fair investigation was essential to establish what had prompted the attack.\n\n\u201cWe feel that the Deputy Minister\u2019s comments are an indication that a proper investigation will not be conducted into the incident. This is a serious incident as it is the first time we have seen a security officer being attacked. The motive behind the attack should be determined,\u201d he told a media briefing.\n\n\u201cA weapon, regardless of what it is, can be used in different ways. It can be used for self-defence or to kill someone. Therefore, it is not appropriate to come out with different interpretations about it,\u201d he added.\n\nFormer Minister Rajitha Senaratne said the incident raised questions as to whether it could have been a rehearsal for a more serious attack targeting former President Wickremesinghe.\n\n\u201cWe heard the Deputy Minister saying Wednesday\u2019s incident was a minor one. One wonders what he meant by serious attacks. Does he refer to the insurgencies in 1971 and 1988/89 as serious attacks?\u201d Dr. Senaratne questioned.\n\nThe security officer injured in Wednesday\u2019s attack was admitted to hospital that evening."
