    "chunk_text": "The differing accounts given by the prosecution witnesses created a significant contradiction in the evidence concerning the identification of the accused. While one witness claimed that the accused had been identified, another eyewitness testified that identification was not possible because the assailants' faces had been concealed.\n\nThe High Court, having considered the evidence placed before it and the charges against the accused, acquitted them of the several charges relating to the incident.\n\nSenior Counsel Darshana Kuruppu, together with Counsel Pramuditha Senevirathne and Manoj Gunawardana\u00a0 appeared for the accused."
