    "md5": "cf9fa96030613cb11005fd385a0d05c1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1749,
    "chunk_text": "IndiGo resumes key India-Sri Lanka flights\n\nColombo, Oct. 2 (Daily Mirror) - India\u2019s leading low-cost carrier IndiGo has resumed daily flights on key routes between India and Sri Lanka, strengthening air connectivity between the two neighbouring countries and supporting tourism, trade and business travel.\n\nThe airline resumed services on three important routes from October 1, including New Delhi-Colombo, Bengaluru-Colombo and Tiruchirappalli (Trichy)-Jaffna.\n\nThe resumption of daily flights between New Delhi and Colombo, as well as Bengaluru and Colombo, is expected to cater to demand from tourists, business travellers and diplomatic passengers travelling between India and Sri Lanka.\n\nMeanwhile, IndiGo\u2019s direct service between Tiruchirappalli Airport in Tamil Nadu and Jaffna International Airport resumed on October 1 after a three-month suspension.\n\nThe Trichy-Jaffna service is scheduled to operate three days a week, on Tuesdays, Thursdays and Saturdays.\n\nOn these days, the flight will depart Trichy at 1.05 p.m. and arrive at Jaffna at 1.50 p.m. It will leave Jaffna for Trichy at 2.30 p.m.\n\nA total of 88 passengers travelled on the flight when the service resumed yesterday.\n\nThe restoration of the direct air link has been welcomed by people in the Northern Province, as it provides a faster and more convenient travel option for those travelling between northern Sri Lanka and Tamil Nadu.\n\nThe Trichy-Jaffna route is also expected to facilitate long-standing cultural, family and commercial ties between Tamil Nadu and the Northern Province.\n\nThe renewed air links between the two countries are expected to contribute to the further development of tourism, trade and economic and social relations between India and Sri Lanka."
  },
