    "chunk_size_bytes": 1947,
    "chunk_text": "Exams Dept. key to future-ready education: PM\n\nColombo, Oct. 2 (Daily Mirror) - The Examinations Department plays a vital role as a trusted partner in the Government\u2019s efforts to build a future-ready education system based on social justice, Prime Minister and Minister of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education Dr. Harini Amarasuriya said\n\nShe made these remarks while attending the \u2018Vajra Prabha\u2019 ceremony held at the Department of Examinations premises on October 1 to mark the institution\u2019s 75th anniversary.\n\nEstablished in 1951, the Examinations Department is Sri Lanka\u2019s principal national assessment institution, responsible for conducting major examinations including the Grade 5 Scholarship Examination, G.C.E. Ordinary Level and Advanced Level examinations and various competitive examinations, as well as issuing examination results and certificates.\n\nThe department evaluates hundreds of thousands of candidates each year and plays a key role in maintaining credibility in the country\u2019s education and professional sectors.\n\nA commemorative stamp and anniversary magazine marking the department\u2019s 75th anniversary were launched during the ceremony. Commemorative gifts were also presented to retired Commissioners General of Examinations.\n\nAddressing the gathering, Prime Minister Amarasuriya said the public has placed considerable trust in the Examinations Department as an institution that plays an important role in determining the future of children.\n\nShe said the department contributes to ensuring fairness and justice in society by providing opportunities for individuals to progress based on their abilities and dedication.\n\nThe Prime Minister commended the commitment of department officials in conducting the G.C.E. Advanced Level Examination without disruption, particularly during severe disasters in recent years, and praised their willingness to go beyond their regular duties when necessary."
  },
