    "chunk_text": "The Prime Minister commended the commitment of department officials in conducting the G.C.E. Advanced Level Examination without disruption, particularly during severe disasters in recent years, and praised their willingness to go beyond their regular duties when necessary.\n\nThe Prime Minister also appreciated the support provided by the department towards successfully conducting examination-related activities for the recruitment of teachers scheduled to take place this year.\n\nShe highlighted the need to make appropriate use of new technology and digitalisation to preserve the public trust built in the institution over the past 75 years.\n\nAt the same time, she highlighted the department\u2019s responsibility to protect highly sensitive examination information in an increasingly digital environment.\n\nThe Prime Minister said the Government would take steps to expand necessary training opportunities to strengthen the capacity of Department of Examinations staff to meet emerging technological challenges.\n\nDeputy Minister of Vocational Education Nalin Hewage, Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education Ministry Secretary Nalaka Kaluwewa, Commissioner General of Examinations Indika Liyanage and Additional Commissioners General of Examinations and other officials attended the event."
